      "comment" : "Appearance sidebar setting for the current theme's loaded-tab text and favicon color."
    },
    "Unloaded tab color" : {
      "comment" : "Appearance sidebar setting for the current theme's unloaded-tab text and favicon color."
    },
    "Loaded tab opacity" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label for the current theme's loaded-tab text and favicon opacity slider."
    },
    "Unloaded tab opacity" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label for the current theme's unloaded-tab text and favicon opacity slider."
    },
    "Text and icon color and opacity are saved separately for each theme." : {
      "comment" : "Caption beneath loaded/unloaded sidebar color settings; each appearance theme keeps its own values."
    },
    "Unloaded tab action" : {
      "comment" : "Appearance sidebar setting choosing how an unloaded tab can be removed."
    },
    "For unloaded tab rows only: hold ⌘ to remove, or show an X next to Play." : {
      "comment" : "Caption for unloaded-tab controls; X removes the saved link while Play reloads it."
    },
    "Hold ⌘" : {
      "comment" : "Choice requiring the Command modifier to remove an unloaded tab."
    },
    "Unlock the vault to import the passwords saved before Credential Manager." : {

    },
    "Unlock this vault to turn on sync." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sync with iCloud switch, disabled, while the vault is locked. Sync needs the vault unlocked."
    },
    "Use “%@” on %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Headline of the toolbar popover after a login or code was picked by hand (Pick Credential…) on a website it is not saved for. First %@ is the credential's name (its username, or display name), second %@ is the page's website as the address bar draws it (punycode). Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Usual web port only. Add a port to include another." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a developer site that has no port. It covers port 80 for http and 443 for https only."
    },
    "Vault on your other devices" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the card on the Vault tab that offers to add a vault another Mac syncs through iCloud. Sentence case."
    },
    "Website access" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Assistant, Acting on websites. It chooses how much of a website the assistant may use when that website has no setting of its own: Ask, Read Only or Allow Control. Sentence case."
    },
    "With the default set to Allow Control, paired apps open and use new websites without asking again. They still ask on pages with a password or payment field, and before signing in, purchases, and deleting." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Follow Website access row on the Connected apps page. Allow Control is the exact name of a Website access level. Paired apps are apps the user paired with WSurf."
    },
    "Ask to close tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Closing tabs row in Settings › Assistant, the default: the assistant and connected apps ask before closing a tab. Sentence case."
    },
    "Allow closing tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Closing tabs row in Settings › Assistant, shown under the Allow Control default: the assistant closes ordinary tabs without asking. Sentence case."
    },
    "Closing tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Assistant, Acting on websites, shown under the Allow Control default. It chooses whether the assistant asks before closing a tab. Sentence case."
    },
    "Pinned tabs are never closed. The assistant can always close tabs it opened. Connected apps ask unless they opened the tab or have Developer access." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Closing tabs row in Settings › Assistant. Pinned tabs are the tabs the person pinned, including pages in a pinned folder. Developer access is the Developer level of a paired app on the Connected apps page."
    },
    "Close “%@”?" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the sheet that asks whether the assistant or a connected app may close a tab. %@ is the title of the tab, cut to one short line."
    },
    "Close this tab?" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the sheet that asks whether the assistant or a connected app may close a tab, when the tab has no title."
    },
    "“%@” wants to close this tab." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the sheet that asks whether a connected app may close a tab. %@ is the app’s name."
    },
    "The assistant wants to close this tab." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the sheet that asks whether the assistant may close a tab."
    },
    "You can reopen it with Reopen Last Closed Tab." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the sheet that asks whether the assistant or a connected app may close a tab. Reopen Last Closed Tab is the name of the menu command. Left out for private tabs, which cannot be reopened."
    },
    "Keep Open" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the sheet that asks whether the assistant or a connected app may close a tab: leaves the tab open. Title Case."
    },
    "Don’t ask again for this task" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox in the sheet that asks whether the assistant may close a tab. When checked and the person closes the tab, the assistant closes other tabs of the same task without asking."
    },
    "Don’t ask again for this connection" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox in the sheet that asks whether a connected app may close a tab. When checked and the person closes the tab, that connection closes other tabs without asking until it disconnects."
    },
    "Don’t suggest merging these credentials again" : {
      "comment" : "Help tooltip of the Not the Same button."
    },
    "Without asking" : {
      "comment" : "Label beside the menu on a paired app’s row. The menu sets what the app may do on developer sites without a prompt: Off, Development or Developer."
    },
    "Without asking works only on developer sites in the Developer profile. Developer also skips the confirmation before purchases, sending, and deleting there." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the Developer work section on the Connected apps page."
    },
    "WSurf added the app but couldn’t save its pairing. Choose Pair to try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when the client’s configuration was written but the pairing record could not be saved."
    },
    "WSurf can’t save a passkey here: Credential Manager has no vault yet." : {

    },
    "WSurf copies a configuration that pairs the app you paste it into. Keep it private." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert that asks for an app name before copying a configuration that contains a pairing token."
    },
    "WSurf couldn’t pair this app. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the client list when Copy Configuration could not save the new pairing."
    },
    "WSurf couldn’t revoke this app. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Connected apps page when the pairing could not be removed."
    },
    "WSurf couldn’t save this change. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Connected apps page when a change to a paired app or the developer settings could not be stored."
    },
    "WSurf keeps up to %lld developer sites. Remove one to add another." : {
      "comment" : "Error when the developer site list is full. The number is the most sites that can be listed."
    },
    "WSurf now keeps passwords only in Credential Manager, an encrypted vault you unlock with a passkey. Passwords saved in the profile “%@” aren’t filled until you import them. Nothing is deleted without your confirmation." : {

    },
    "X next to Play" : {
      "comment" : "Choice showing a separate remove X immediately left of the unloaded-tab Play button."
    },
    "Choose light, dark, pastel Calm, or match your Mac." : {
      "comment" : "Search result description for Appearance theme choices, including the two pastel Calm presets."
    },
    "Remove Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Explicit destructive sidebar context-menu command that removes the tab and its saved link."
    },
    "Remove Other Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive tab context-menu command that removes other tabs."
    },
    "Remove Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation button for explicitly removing selected tabs and their saved sidebar links."
    },
    "Remove %lld Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive sidebar context-menu command. The integer is the number of selected tabs to remove."
    },
    "Remove %lld tabs?" : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation title for removing selected tabs. The integer is the number of tabs."
    },
    "Unload %lld Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Sidebar context-menu command that unloads selected tabs without removing their links or pins."
    },
    "Free Memory" : {
      "comment" : "Command that unloads every background tab in every window now, in WebKit and Chromium. Title Case. File menu item, command palette entry and the button in Settings > General."
    },
    "Free memory" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Settings > General row, and its Settings search entry, with the Free Memory button. Sentence case."
    },
    "Unloads background tabs now, in WebKit and Chromium. They reload when you open them; Chromium tabs restore their address but not Back/Forward history. Chromium’s helper processes stay until you quit WSurf." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Free memory row in Settings > General, and its Settings search entry. Chromium’s graphics, network and storage helper processes cannot be released without quitting WSurf."
    },
    "unload every background tab" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Free Memory command in the command palette. Sentence fragment, lower case."
    },
    "No background tabs to unload." : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice after Free Memory when every tab is the current tab, already unloaded or protected."
    },
    "Unloaded 1 tab." : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice after Free Memory unloaded exactly one tab."
    },
    "Unloaded %lld tabs." : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice after Free Memory. The integer is how many tabs were unloaded, at least 2."
    },
    "This tab has unsaved form changes." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "This tab has an active download." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "This tab is using the camera or microphone." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "The assistant is working in this tab." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "This tab is playing media." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "This tab is visible in a split." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "This tab is kept active by a site setting." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "Private tabs cannot be unloaded." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why private browsing tabs are not eligible for unloading."
    },
    "Extension tabs cannot be unloaded." : {
      "comment" : "Notice explaining why an extension page is not eligible for unloading."
    },
    "This tab cannot be unloaded right now." : {
      "comment" : "Fallback notice when a tab cannot safely be unloaded."
    },
    "" : {
      "comment" : "Not shown to anyone: the empty branch of a conditional tooltip on the sidebar's New Tab and Settings rows, used when the sidebar is wide enough to show the row's own title. Leave the translation empty."
    },
    "Your passwords are imported. Remove the old list in Credential Manager when you’re ready." : {

    },
    "Your saved passwords are now only in Credential Manager." : {

    },
    "“%@” is playing" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the speaker glyph of a collapsed folder in the sidebar, saying which tab inside it is making sound. %@ is the tab's title, written by the website — never translated. Keep the curly quotation marks around it."
    },
    "“%@” wants more access" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the dialog shown when an already-installed extension asks for permissions or website access beyond what it was granted. %@ is the extension’s own name, taken from its manifest and never translated. Curly quotation marks; sentence case with no final full stop, as macOS dialog titles are written."
    },
    "“Allow Once” lasts until you leave this website." : {
      "comment" : "Explanatory line under the question in the permission panel. The quoted phrase is the exact label of the “Allow Once” button in the same panel — translate it identically there and here, and keep the curly quotation marks. Full sentence."
    },
    "(%@ cached)" : {
      "comment" : "Trailing note on the input-token field of the agent activity column's usage footer, reading “12K in (38% cached)”. %@ is an already-formatted percentage (with its own per-cent sign) for the share of input the provider served from its cache. Keep the parentheses; very tight."
    },
    "%@\n%@\n\nChoose access:\n• Read Only: read page content.\n• Allow Control: also click, type, and navigate." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@\n%2$@\n\nChoose access:\n• Read Only: read page content.\n• Allow Control: also click, type, and navigate."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ — answering" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the permission badge in the address bar while a permission request is on screen waiting for an answer. %@ is the localized permission name (Camera, Microphone, Location, Notifications); the em dash and the word after it are a status fragment, not a sentence."
    },
    "%@ · from %@" : {
      "comment" : "Second line of a row in the Downloads list. The first %@ is the size summary (“2.4 MB”, or “1.2 MB of 5 MB” while running); the second %@ is the host the file came from, e.g. example.com. The · is a separator between two facts, not a word."
    },
    "%@ / %@ tokens" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ / %2$@ tokens"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (default)" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the Open With submenu of a download’s right-click menu on the Downloads page, for the app the Mac opens that file with by default. %@ is the app’s name, for example Preview. Keep the parentheses, as the Finder does."
    },
    "%@ allowed" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in the one-line summary under a website in the list. %@ is a list of permission names already worded and joined, for example camera and microphone. Lower case: it is joined with other fragments, never shown alone."
    },
    "%@ blocked" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in the one-line summary under a website in the list, for permissions that were refused. %@ is a list of permission names already worded and joined. Lower case: joined with other fragments, never shown alone."
    },
    "%@ doesn’t offer suggestions." : {

    },
    "%@ has a small context window. Enabling more than %lld tools leaves less room for page content and may reduce accuracy." : {
      "comment" : "Warning on the Tools settings page. %@ is the provider name, %lld the recommended tool count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@’s context is small, and every tool takes a share of it. More than %2$lld tools can push out page content and confuse smaller models."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ in" : {
      "comment" : "Token counter in the footer of the agent activity column, in a monospaced one-line row that reads “3 req · 12K in (38% cached) · 2K out”. %@ is an abbreviated count of tokens sent to the model; “in” is the short form of “sent in”. Extremely tight — keep it to a word or two."
    },
    "In a micro window. Click to move it back here, or Option-click to show the micro window." : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the same mark on a sidebar row (see “In Micro Window”). Clicking the row brings the page back into this window, in the row's place; Option-clicking it brings the micro window to the front instead. “Option” is the name of the key; use the name printed on keyboards in the target language. Full sentences."
    },
    "In iCloud, but deleted here." : {
      "comment" : "Row caption in the Review Sync Changes sheet for an entry that was deleted on this Mac before."
    },
    "%@ in use" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the permission badge in the address bar while a website is actively using a capability. %@ is the permission's own name, itself localized: Camera, Microphone, Location or Notifications. The phrase continues from that noun, so it is a fragment rather than a sentence."
    },
    "%@ isn’t ready" : {

    },
    "%@ of %@" : {
      "comment" : "Progress line under a file in the downloads list. The first %@ is the amount received and the second the file's total size, both already formatted by the system, e.g. “3.2 MB of 18 MB”; the order may be changed with positional specifiers."
    },
    "%@ out" : {
      "comment" : "The other half of the same footer line in the agent activity column: %@ is an abbreviated count of tokens the model produced, and “out” is the short form of “returned”. Must balance the “%@ in” string beside it; extremely tight."
    },
    "Outline Elements" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the Developer Tools menu that draws a thin red outline around every element of the page so the layout can be seen. A check mark shows when it is on. Outline is a verb. Title Case."
    },
    "%@ Suggestions" : {
      "comment" : "Section heading over the search-engine completions in the address bar results list and in the ⌘K palette. %@ is the name of the chosen search engine (DuckDuckGo, Google, Bing…) — a product name, never translated. Title Case."
    },
    "%@ tokens" : {
      "comment" : "Detected context window size on a provider page. %@ is a formatted number, e.g. 32,768."
    },
    "%@ tokens used" : {

    },
    "%@ unavailable, using Apple Intelligence" : {
      "comment" : "Status message shown when the chosen model provider cannot answer and WSurf falls back to the on-device model. %@ is the provider's name, e.g. OpenAI or Ollama. “Apple Intelligence” is Apple's product name — leave as is."
    },
    "%@ wants to open %@.\n\nIt will be able to read the page, click, type, and navigate." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ wants to open %2$@.\n\nIt will be able to read the page, click, type, and navigate."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ will be imported." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the confirmation dialog shown before bookmarks are imported. %@ is a count fragment such as “87 bookmarks”. The sentence “The bookmarks go into a new folder in the sidebar.” follows it."
    },
    "%@ without asking" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in the one-line summary under a website, naming what the assistant may do there unprompted. %@ is a list of action kinds already worded and joined, for example purchases. Lower case: joined with other fragments."
    },
    "%@: %lld tabs" : {
      "comment" : "One line of the Organize Tabs proposal, shown as a bulleted list: the name of a folder that would be made, then how many tabs would go into it. The name comes from the language model and is not translated. A group always holds two or more tabs, so the plural is constant.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@: %2$lld tabs"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@. Pick another provider in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Status message when the selected model provider cannot be used. %@ is a reason sentence supplied elsewhere and carrying no final full stop, e.g. “Apple Intelligence isn’t available on this Mac”. “Settings” is the name of the app's Settings window."
    },
    "%lld bookmarks" : {
      "comment" : "Count fragment dropped into the import dialog’s “… will be imported.” and into “Imported ….”. %lld is the number of bookmarks. A mid-sentence fragment, not a sentence of its own.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld bookmark"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld bookmarks"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld changes from iCloud couldn’t be read and were skipped." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the Sync with iCloud caption. %lld is a number of at least 1. Changes that could not be opened with this vault’s key."
    },
    "%lld changes from your other devices will be added when you unlock this vault." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sync with iCloud switch while the vault is locked and other devices sent changes. %lld is a number of at least 1. Sentence case."
    },
    "%lld downloads will be removed from the list. The files stay in your Downloads folder." : {
      "comment" : "Explanatory text in the confirmation sheet for clearing the download list, shown both in the downloads popover and on the Downloads settings page. %lld is how many finished downloads disappear from the list. “Downloads folder” is the macOS folder of that name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld download will be removed from the list. The file stays in your Downloads folder."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld downloads will be removed from the list. The files stay in your Downloads folder."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld entries" : {
      "comment" : "Detail line beside the “Clear History…” command in the ⌘K palette. %lld is how many history entries exist and would be cleared. Sentence-case caption, no verb, very tight.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entry"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entries"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld entries are from a newer version of WSurf. Update WSurf to sync them." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the Sync with iCloud caption. %lld is a number of at least 1. Entries another device saved in a format only a newer version of WSurf reads; they stay as they are until WSurf is updated."
    },
    "%lld entries are too large to sync or hold only files, so they stay on this Mac." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the Sync with iCloud caption. %lld is a number of at least 1. Files are never synced."
    },
    "%lld entries don’t sync until you choose." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the card for entries that wait for a choice about sync. %lld is a number of at least 1."
    },
    "%lld entries, each kept for %@" : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the Entries list in Settings, Autofill, Input History, shown while the list is unlocked. The first number is how many entries the list holds. %@ is how long each entry is kept, such as “30 minutes” or “1 week”. A mid-sentence time span, not a sentence of its own.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entry, each kept for %@"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entries, each kept for %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld entries, kept until you delete them" : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the Entries list in Settings, Autofill, Input History, shown while the list is unlocked and entries never expire. %lld is how many entries the list holds.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entry, kept until you delete it"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld entries, kept until you delete them"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld entries need a choice. Review them on the Vault tab." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sync with iCloud switch when entries wait for a choice: they changed on two devices, differ with no common ground, are deleted on one, or cannot be added on this Mac. %lld is a number of at least 1. Vault tab is the tab of the Autofill page."
    },
    "%lld entries were deleted on this Mac. Delete them on your other devices too?" : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sync with iCloud switch when a large number of entries were deleted on this Mac and the deletion has not been sent yet. %lld is a number of at least 21. The next row asks for the answer."
    },
    "%lld extensions, %lld running." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Extensions settings title. The first %lld is the total number of extensions available, the second is how many are switched on in this profile."
    },
    "%lld extensions, all running." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Extensions settings title. %lld is the total of extensions installed in WSurf plus Safari extensions found on the Mac, and every one of them is switched on."
    },
    "%lld folders" : {
      "comment" : "How many tab folders a profile has, shown after “%lld tabs” and joined to it by “ · ”. A fragment, not a sentence. %lld is the number of folders.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld folder"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld folders"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld installed" : {
      "comment" : "How many extensions a profile has, shown under the word “Extensions” on a profile’s page. A fragment, not a sentence. %lld is the number of extensions.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld installed"
