    },
    "Add connection…" : {

    },
    "Add extensions" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the third onboarding screen, where the reader installs browser extensions in one click. An extension is an add-on that changes how websites behave."
    },
    "Add extensions from the Chrome Web Store or Firefox Add-ons." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Add extensions heading. These refers to the extensions listed below it. Chrome and Firefox are browser names and are never translated; their stores are the websites the extensions are downloaded from, and opening a store page in WSurf is how the reader installs more."
    },
    "Add Inspect Element to a page’s right-click menu. Websites in Developer mode, such as localhost, keep it even when this is off." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Web Inspector row in Settings > Advanced, and the same wording in the Settings search index. The switch adds Inspect Element to a page’s right-click menu; the second sentence says websites in Developer mode (localhost and other local addresses, or any website the person turned it on for) keep it when the switch is off. Curly apostrophe."
    },
    "Add it to this Mac with your unlock passkey. Its entries download when you unlock it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Vault on your other devices card."
    },
    "Add Key…" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the API key row in Settings > Provider that opens the key-entry popover; it reads Change… once a key is stored. Title Case; the trailing character is a real ellipsis (…) promising a popover, so keep it."
    },
    "Add WSurf to %@" : {
      "comment" : "MCP client setup accessibility label. The placeholder is the client app name."
