    },
    "Share tabs through iCloud" : {
      "comment" : "Row title on a profile’s settings page: the switch that shares the tabs open in this profile with the person’s other devices through iCloud. iCloud is Apple’s product name — leave as is. Sentence case."
    },
    "Shared tabs: %lld · Tool calls: %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Native MCP connection settings or access prompt. MCP is the protocol name. Inserted client names, website addresses, and page titles are supplied at runtime; do not translate them."
    },
    "Short" : {

    },
    "Show %@ on the toolbar" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the Pin button in the extensions overflow popover. %@ is the extension’s own display name, taken from the extension’s manifest — it is not translated. Show is a verb, and toolbar is the row of buttons at the top of the window."
    },
    "Show a link’s address at the bottom of the page when you point at it." : {

    },
    "Show All" : {
      "comment" : "Serves two places at once: the standard macOS application-menu command that unhides all applications, and a button at the end of the start page’s history list that reveals the full list. Use Apple’s own wording for the system command, since that is the one users recognise. Title Case, Show is a verb."
    },
    "Show All Downloads" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the foot of the small list that opens over the Downloads button: it opens the full Downloads page. Title Case, tight."
    },
    "Show All History" : {
      "comment" : "Menu bar command under History, shortcut ⌘Y, which opens the full history list. Title Case and established platform terminology."
    },
