    },
    "Turn Off Developer Mode for “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the bottom of the Developer Tools menu that turns Developer mode off for one website. %@ is the website’s host name, such as localhost, and is never translated. Title Case. Quotation marks are curly."
    },
    "Turn on any Safari extension you already have. The App Store keeps it up to date." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the Safari extensions section on the Extensions settings page. The first sentence invites the person to switch on an extension that arrived with an app they installed; the second says updates come through the App Store rather than through WSurf. Safari and App Store are product names and are never translated."
    },
    "Turn on Apple Intelligence in System Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Setup hint shown when the Apple Intelligence provider is chosen but not enabled on the Mac. Apple Intelligence and System Settings are Apple’s names — use Apple’s own translations, since the user has to find them on screen."
    },
    "Turn scripts off for every website." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search caption for the JavaScript switch, which carries no caption on the page."
    },
    "Turn sections on or off. Drag to reorder." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Start Page heading in the editor popover. Two short sentences."
    },
    "Turn them on in Settings › General." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under “Lyrics are off”. “Them” is the lyrics. The › is the separator macOS uses between a settings window and one of its pages; keep the page names as they are translated elsewhere. Full sentence."
    },
    "Turn this off if the website breaks." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Block known trackers switch on one website's page, saying what to do when tracker blocking stops a website working. Imperative."
    },
    "Turn this off to keep this website’s video in its tab." : {

    },
    "Turning it off also removes the thin outline macOS draws around the window." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Shadow setting in Settings › Appearance › Window, and its Settings search description. “It” is the window shadow. The thin outline is the dark line that macOS draws just outside every window together with its shadow. One sentence with a final full stop."
    },
    "Turning this off affects new replies. It does not delete earlier copies or change OpenAI’s other data-retention policies." : {

    },
    "Type" : {
      "comment" : "Tool name in assistant settings: typing into fields on a web page."
    },
    "Type > for commands" : {
      "comment" : "Note beside the Actions heading in the ⌘K palette, telling the reader that typing the greater-than sign filters the list down to commands only. Keep the “>” character as it is: it is the key the user presses, not punctuation."
    },
    "Type in Focused Field" : {

    },
    "Type into a field selected from a screenshot." : {

    },
    "Type on page" : {

    },
    "Type your question" : {
      "comment" : "Stands in for the question in the Ask row of the address bar results, from the moment “@” is typed until a question is actually there. The row leads the list so that Return sends a question rather than attaching a tab. Sentence case, imperative."
    },
    "Unavailable" : {
      "comment" : "Status shown beside a chosen AI provider that cannot run on this Mac. A single word in a narrow status chip, so keep it short."
    },
    "Undo" : {
      "comment" : "Standard macOS Edit menu command, shortcut ⌘Z. Use Apple’s own wording for it in the target language."
    },
    "Unexpected response from the provider" : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when the AI provider’s reply could not be understood. Provider means the AI provider. No final full stop."
    },
    "unknown" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase word used as the provider’s error message when the server’s reply carried none; it is then inserted after the colon in a line such as Provider error 500: unknown. Deliberately lowercase because it sits mid-sentence."
    },
    "Unlock Cards" : {

    },
    "Unlock one of this profile’s vaults first, then add this vault." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Vault on your other devices card when no vault of the profile is unlocked to approve adding another."
    },
    "Unlock Other Vaults…" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the bottom left of the Pick Credential… sheet, shown while another vault of the profile is locked: unlocks one (Touch ID or passkey) and lists its entries too. Title Case, ellipsis because it asks for authentication."
    },
    "Unmute" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the same speaker button in the media dock once sound is off; it lets the sound back. Verb, one word; pairs with “Mute”."
    },
    "Unmute microphone" : {

    },
    "Unmute Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the same small speaker button in a sidebar tab row once the tab has been silenced; it lets the sound back. Title Case, narrow row."
    },
    "Unmute This Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the toolbar's speaker button once the current tab has been silenced. Title Case."
    },
    "Unmute WSurf" : {
      "comment" : "The same menu item, right-click item and list button while WSurf is muted: it ends the mute of all of WSurf and puts back each tab's own mute setting. Title Case verb phrase, the opposite of “Mute WSurf”."
    },
    "Unmute WSurf to talk with the assistant by voice." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the voice conversation panel when the person starts a voice conversation with the assistant while all of WSurf is muted (Mute WSurf, the speaker, ⌃⌘M): the conversation does not start, because nothing of it could be heard, and this says what to do. Full sentence with a full stop, imperative, like other hints. “WSurf” is the app's name and is never translated; “Unmute WSurf” is the same wording as the menu item and the speaker's button."
    },
    "Unmutes WSurf and gives each tab its own setting back." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the speaker button while WSurf is muted: it says what pressing the button does. Full sentence with a full stop, third person, like other hints."
    },
    "Unpin" : {
      "comment" : "Folder context-menu command or drag label that takes a row out of the pinned section. Imperative verb, one word."
    },
    "Unpin Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Command that takes the pin off a tab, which then drops out of the pinned rows. Five surfaces share it: the context menu of a pinned tab row, the minus button on that row, the toolbar button while the pinned page is on screen, the search palette, and the File menu item on ⌘D while the pinned page is on screen. Title Case."
    },
    "Unsupported CRX container version %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when an extension package uses a file format version the app cannot read. %lld is the version number found in the file. CRX is the name of Chrome’s extension package format — leave as is. No final full stop."
    },
    "Untitled" : {
      "comment" : "Name suggested in the save panel for a page that has no title and no address to name the file after. A noun."
    },
    "Up to date" : {
      "comment" : "Update status meaning no newer version exists, shown both in the Settings update section and on the sidebar update card. An adjective phrase describing the app."
    },
    "Up to date." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sync with iCloud switch when every change has been sent and received. A sentence fragment. Sentence case."
    },
    "Update" : {

    },
    "Update Available" : {
      "comment" : "Compact title in the blue-tinted sidebar banner when a newer version of WSurf can be installed. Title Case."
    },
    "Update card?" : {

    },
    "Update channel" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the pop-up menu in Settings > About that chooses which builds the app updates to. The choices are “Release” and “Preview”. Sentence case. “Channel” is the usual software word for a stream of builds."
    },
    "Update needs approval" : {
      "comment" : "Small tag on an installed extension’s row in Settings, shown when a newer version asks for more website access or permissions than you approved and so has not been installed. Clicking it checks again and asks. Sentence case, no final full stop."
    },
    "Update password?" : {

    },
    "Update Pinned URL" : {
      "comment" : "Command that makes the page a pinned tab shows now its new pinned page, replacing the one it returned to. Shown while the tab is away from its pinned page: in the context menu of a pinned tab row or Favorite, as the File menu item on ⌘D, and in the search palette. Undo restores the old page. Title Case."
    },
    "update.banner.downloadingShare" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the software-update button in the sidebar while a release is being fetched. %@ is an already-formatted percentage and carries its own per-cent sign. Kept separate from “Downloading %@”, where %@ is a version number instead. The button is narrow, so keep this short.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Downloading %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "update.banner.install" : {
      "comment" : "The one button that updates the app, in the update banner and on the About settings page. One click downloads the update, installs it and restarts WSurf; there is no second step. A verb (a command). Its twin is the plain “Install” key, the extension button — the same English word for a different button, so the two are kept apart. The button is narrow, so keep this short.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Install"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "update.banner.preparingShare" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the software-update button in the sidebar while the downloaded release is being unpacked. %@ is an already-formatted percentage and carries its own per-cent sign. Kept separate from “Preparing %@”, where %@ is a version number instead. The button is narrow, so keep this short.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Preparing %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Updated to %@" : {
      "comment" : "Two uses of one wording. 1) Title of the card at the bottom of the sidebar, and tooltip and VoiceOver label of its badge in the icons-only sidebar, shown for a few seconds after the first launch of a new build. %@ is the new version number, for example 0.1.12, never translated. 2) Tag on an extension row in Settings > Extensions that was just updated; there %@ is the extension’s version. Past participle, no full stop."
    },
    "Upload" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the confirmation that uploads this Mac’s copy of a vault to iCloud again."
    },
    "Upload “%@” to iCloud?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation shown when sync is turned on again after the vault was removed from iCloud or the account changed. %@ is the vault’s name."
    },
    "Use %@" : {
      "comment" : "Settings → Assistant → a provider page. %@ is the provider name, e.g. \"Ollama\". Button that makes this provider the one that answers."
    },
    "Use %@ where the search term goes." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Search URL field, telling the user what to put in their custom search address. %@ is always filled with the literal two characters %s, which the user has to type into the address — it is inserted rather than written in the text so it is not mistaken for a format specifier. Keep it as a placeholder; do not translate what it stands for."
    },
    "Use %s where the search term goes." : {
      "comment" : "The same instruction as it is indexed for the Settings search, where the token is written out literally. %s here is not a placeholder to be filled in — it is the exact text the user has to type into their custom search address, so keep the two characters %s unchanged."
    },
    "Use controls on a permitted embedded website." : {

    },
    "Use embedded page" : {

    },
    "Use Embedded Pages" : {

    },
    "Use HTTPS to encrypt your API key. HTTP is allowed only for localhost." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the field where a user-added endpoint address is typed, shown when a remote address uses an insecure protocol. https, http and localhost are technical terms and must stay exactly as they are, including their lowercase spelling. In the clear means unencrypted."
    },
    "Use iCloud Version" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Review Sync Changes sheet that takes iCloud’s version of an entry. Title Case for a command."
    },
    "Use Icons Only" : {
      "comment" : "Checkmark item in the right-click menu of the sidebar toggle button; switches the sidebar to its narrow favicons-without-titles look. The same choice Settings calls “Icons only”. Title Case."
    },
    "Use keyboard controls on a page." : {

    },
    "Use Minimal Window Style" : {
