      "comment" : "Context-menu item on a space icon in the sidebar. Opens a small dialog to rename the space or change its icon. Title Case, ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "New Space…" : {
      "comment" : "Command in the profile menu, the ⌘K palette and the space icons' context menu. Opens a dialog that names a new space (a named set of tabs and folders). Title Case, ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Delete Space…" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive context-menu item on a space icon in the sidebar. Asks before closing the space's tabs and removing it. Title Case, ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Deleted on another device, changed here." : {
      "comment" : "Row caption in the Review Sync Changes sheet."
    },
    "Move to Space" : {
      "comment" : "Submenu in the sidebar's tab and folder context menus listing the other spaces of the profile. Choosing one moves the selected rows there. Title Case."
    },
    "Move to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Review Sync Changes sheet that moves an entry to Trash because another device deleted it. Title Case for a command."
    },
    "New Space" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the dialog that names a new space, and the name a space gets when its name is left empty. Title Case."
    },
    "Edit Space" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the dialog that renames a space or changes its icon. Title Case."
    },
    "Create Space" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the New Space dialog. Title Case."
    },
    "Space Name" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder and accessibility label of the name field in the New Space and Edit Space dialogs. Title Case."
    },
    "Icon" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label of the icon picker in the New Space and Edit Space dialogs. Noun."
    },
    "Show Space %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Hidden menu commands under Window bound to ⌃1 through ⌃9. %lld is the space's position in the sidebar's row of space icons, a number from 1 to 9. Title Case."
    },
    "A space shows its own tabs and folders. Pins, Favorites, sign-ins, history and passwords stay with the profile." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation in the New Space and Edit Space dialogs. A space only changes which tabs and folders the window lists; the profile's pinned tabs, Favorites, website sign-ins, browsing history and passwords are shared by all its spaces."
    },
    "Its tabs and folders close. Pins, Favorites, sign-ins, history and passwords stay with the profile." : {
      "comment" : "Detail of the confirmation shown before deleting a space. Deleting closes the space's tabs and folders; it never deletes the profile or its passwords."
    },
    "Its vaults are also removed from iCloud. Your other devices keep their copies. To keep them in iCloud, turn off Sync with iCloud for each vault first." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the Delete profile confirmation when the profile has a vault that syncs through iCloud. Sync with iCloud is the name of the switch."
    },
    "Its vaults sync through iCloud. Add it to use them on this Mac." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of a row in the On your other devices section."
    },
    "Switch to “%@”?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the one-time question before choosing a space that belongs to another profile. %@ is the space's name. Switching changes the whole window to that profile."
    },
    "“%@” has its own sign-ins and data, in the profile “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the one-time question before choosing a space of another profile. The first %@ is the space's name, the second the name of the profile it belongs to."
    },
    "Switching locks this profile’s passwords, disconnects external apps from this window, stops the assistant and reloads your tabs." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the one-time question before choosing a space of another profile: what a profile switch does to the window. External apps are MCP clients controlling the browser."
    },
    "Switch" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the question before switching to a space of another profile. Verb."
    },
    "Don’t ask again" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox under the question before switching to a space of another profile. When on, later switches happen without asking."
    },
    "Share sign-ins with “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the New Space dialog. %@ is a profile's name. The new space uses that profile's website sign-ins, history and passwords."
    },
    "Separate sign-ins and data" : {
      "comment" : "Last choice in the New Space dialog: the new space gets its own new profile, with its own website sign-ins, history and passwords."
    },
    "A new profile with its own sign-ins, history and passwords." : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the Separate sign-ins and data choice in the New Space dialog."
    },
    "Sign-ins and data" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label of the menu in the New Space dialog that chooses which profile's sign-ins the space uses, or separate ones."
    },
    "%@ — %@ profile" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of a space icon that belongs to another profile. The first %@ is the space's name, the second the profile's name, for example: Clients — Work profile."
    },
    "%@ +%lld" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the toolbar badge when several external apps use the window. %@ is the name of the first app (not translated), %lld is how many more there are, e.g. “Claude Code +2”. May be followed by a tier name. Very tight."
    },
    "%@ can read this tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the “AI” mark on a tab when one external app has read-only access to the tab. %@ is the app’s name, not translated. “Read” means see the page contents."
    },
    "%@ controls this tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the “AI” mark on a tab’s sidebar row, favorite tile or split cell when one external app (such as Claude Code, connected by MCP) has control access to the tab. %@ is the app’s name, not translated."
    },
    "%@ copy" : {
      "comment" : "Default name for a saved copy of a theme, used by duplicating a theme and migrating old customizations. %@ is the theme’s name, such as Standard or Nord, giving “Nord copy”. Lowercase “copy” follows the name."
    },
    "%@ Custom" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the editable copy made from a built-in theme on the first color edit or with Customize. %@ is the built-in theme’s name, such as Nord, giving “Nord Custom”. Custom is an adjective that follows the name."
    },
    "%@ failed and nothing was written. This import was discarded and the file was not changed. To import it, choose the file again." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when importing a password CSV file that the user chose fails and nothing was saved. %@ is a short, already translated phrase naming the step that failed, such as “Import” or “Saving the imported credentials”, and it starts the sentence. Full sentences."
    },
    "%@ failed and nothing was written. This import was discarded and the old list was not changed. To import it, choose Review again." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when importing the old list (the passwords WSurf saved before Credential Manager) fails and nothing was saved. %@ is a short, already translated phrase naming the step that failed and it starts the sentence. “Review” is the button “Review…” on the old-passwords card; match its translation."
    },
    "%@ failed and nothing was written. This transfer was discarded. Export again from Passwords." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when an import sent by another app (Apple’s Passwords) failed before saving. %@ is a short, already translated phrase naming the step that failed, such as “Import” or “Saving the imported credentials”, and it starts the sentence. Full sentences."
    },
    "%@ groups were left as they were because merging them would pass a limit." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the Suggested Merges sheet’s result message. %@ is the number of groups not merged because merging them would pass a limit."
    },
    "%@ is also enabled and may still fill passwords on its own. Turn it off in Extensions to use only Credential Manager." : {
      "comment" : "Note under the Save and fill section of Settings › Autofill, shown when a password-manager extension is installed. %@ is that extension’s name (not translated). Extensions is the Settings page for extensions; Credential Manager is WSurf’s own vault. Sentence case."
    },
    "%@ is using this window" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the toolbar badge shown while one external app (such as Claude Code, connected by MCP) can act in the window. %@ is the app’s name, not translated. Also read in the sentence “%@. Press Option-Command-Period…”."
    },
    "%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a part of a received item was skipped because WSurf has no place for its kind yet. %@ is the kind of the part and starts the sentence, such as “A generated password” (translated separately). Sentence case."
    },
    "%@ item(s) will be deleted permanently when you leave Trash. You’ll confirm with an unlock passkey." : {
      "comment" : "Warning in the bar at the top of the Trash list while items are marked for deletion (with the X key); there is no dialog. %@ is the number of marked items, already formatted as text; “item(s)” covers one or many. The deletion runs when the user leaves Trash, after a passkey prompt."
    },
    "%@ moved to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet. %@ is the part that was moved to Trash in WSurf: Login, Passkey, Verification code, Notes, or Cards and other items. It starts the sentence."
    },
    "%@ on %@" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the “Passkeys not confirmed with the website” section, for one passkey. First %@ is the passkey’s user name, second %@ the website’s domain. Do not translate them; reorder if the grammar needs it."
    },
    "%@ removed for good" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet. %@ is the part that was removed from Trash for good in WSurf: Login, Passkey, Verification code, Notes, or Cards and other items. It starts the sentence."
    },
    "%@ selected" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the bar above the credential list in the Vault tab while credentials are selected. %@ is the number selected, already formatted for the locale (for example 1,204). Also read by VoiceOver as a header."
    },
    "%@ won’t be kept: the merged credential won’t fill there." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the merge sheet for a website of another credential that is left out. %@ is that website’s host name, for example “login.example.com”, and is not translated. Sentence."
    },
    "%@ won’t be recorded." : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation note under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill after the user excludes a website from Input History. %@ is that website’s host name, such as example.com, and is never translated."
    },
    "%@ · %lld earlier versions kept" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a removed item’s name in the Trash list. First %@ is what was removed, already translated (Credential, Password, Verification code, Passkey, Details, Notes, Cards and other items or Files). %lld is how many earlier versions are kept with it, at least 1, so the singular can occur. The · is a separator."
    },
    "%@ · Vault %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a vault in the Vault pop-up menus of Settings › Credentials, the page title, the “Which vault?” prompt and the Pick Credential… sheet (when there is more than one vault). Shown for an unlocked vault that has a name of its own. %@ is that name, chosen by the user (do not translate it); %lld is the vault’s number, as in “Vault 1”. The middle dot separates the two."
    },
    "%@, %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of a favorite tile in the sidebar. First %@ is a status such as “New”, second %@ is “Loaded” or “Unloaded”. Joined with a comma. Not shown on screen."
    },
    "%@, light and dark" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of a theme card in Settings › Appearance when the appearance follows the Mac, so the thumbnail shows both a light and a dark half. %@ is the theme’s name (Nord, Calm, …)."
    },
    "%@, rendering engine: %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of the address field in the toolbar. First %@ is what the field shows (the page address or typed text), second %@ is the engine of the loaded page, WebKit or Chromium (not translated). Not shown on screen."
    },
    "%@. Press Option-Command-Period to stop it." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement made when the toolbar badge appears. %@ is the sentence “<app> is using this window” (without final period). The key combination is the Stop External Connections shortcut; write the key names as macOS shows them."
    },
    "%lld apps can read this tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the “AI” mark on a tab when several external apps have only read access. %lld is the number of apps, at least 2. Sidebar tab row, favorite tile or split cell."
    },
    "%lld apps control this tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the “AI” mark on a tab when several external apps can control it. %lld is the number of apps, at least 2. Sidebar tab row, favorite tile or split cell."
    },
    "%lld cards and other items" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds 3 cards and other items.” %lld is a number above 1. Plural counterpart of “a card or other item”. Never starts a sentence."
    },
    "%lld cards in the file couldn’t be read and are left out." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the import review caption of Safari payment cards. %lld is the number of cards in the chosen file that could not be read and are skipped."
    },
    "%lld credentials move to Trash with their history, and their passwords and codes stay in the History of “%@”. They can’t be restored while “%@” is in the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Merge Credentials?” dialog when several credentials are merged away. %lld is how many move to Trash (at least 2); first and second %@ are the title of the primary credential and are not translated. Trash is the vault’s Trash."
    },
    "%lld external apps are using this window" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the toolbar badge when several external apps can act in the window. %lld is the number of apps, at least 2. The one-app form is “%@ is using this window”."
    },
    "%lld files" : {
      "comment" : "Plural of “1 file”: fragment of the detail line of a credential row in the list. %lld is the number of attached files, 2 or more."
    },
    "%lld files use %@ of this vault’s %@. Files are encrypted in the vault and open only while it is unlocked." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Vault tab when the Files filter is chosen. %lld is the number of files in the vault; the first %@ is the space they use and the second the vault’s file limit, both sizes such as “12 MB”."
    },
    "%lld items added" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet. %lld is the number of cards or other items added in WSurf that the other app’s copy doesn’t have; it is 2 or more. Plural counterpart of “An item added”."
    },
    "%lld items will be deleted permanently when you leave Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Trash list of the Credentials page after the user marks several Trash items for deletion with X. %lld is how many (2 or more). Nothing is deleted until the user leaves Trash; the notice offers Undo."
    },
    "%lld moved into the vault and %lld were already in it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the message in the dialog confirming that the old copies of cards and addresses are erased. First %lld is how many were moved into the vault, second %lld how many were already there."
    },
    "%lld moved, %lld already in the vault, %lld not in the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Caption after cards and addresses were moved to the vault in Settings › Autofill, used when some old copies are not in the vault. In order: how many were moved, how many were already in the vault, how many are not in the vault."
    },
    "%lld moved, %lld already in the vault. Undo moves the new entries to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Caption after cards and addresses were moved to the vault in Settings › Autofill. First %lld is how many were moved, second %lld how many were already in the vault. Undo is the button beside it; Trash is the vault’s Trash. Sentence case."
    },
    "%lld notes added" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet. %lld is the number of notes added in WSurf that the other app’s copy doesn’t have; it is 2 or more. Plural counterpart of “A note added”."
    },
    "%lld of %lld aren’t in the vault, so erasing deletes them permanently." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the erase confirmation message when some old cards or addresses are not in the vault. First %lld is how many are not in the vault, second %lld is the total number of old entries."
    },
    "%lld of %lld passwords from the old list aren’t in Credential Manager because you skipped them, kept a different password, or they can’t be imported. Removing the list deletes them permanently." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the message in the “Remove the Old Passwords List?” confirmation. The first %lld is how many passwords from the old list are not in Credential Manager (skipped, different password or not importable), the second is the total in the old list. It says removing the list deletes them permanently."
    },
    "%lld of %lld will be added to the vault. The others are already in it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the import review sheet, and under the list in the step that moves old cards and addresses to the vault. First %lld is how many entries will be added, second %lld is how many are listed in total. Sentence case."
    },
    "%lld passkey(s)" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment in an account’s line in the account chooser of the passkey sheets, saying how many passkeys that account already holds. %lld is at least 1. Joined with fragments such as “password” by a middle dot, so keep it short and lowercase; the (s) covers singular and plural."
    },
    "%lld passkeys" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a credential’s detail line in the merge sheet, import review and credential list, for credentials with several passkeys. %lld is the number of passkeys, at least 2; one passkey reads “Passkey”. Lowercase fragment."
    },
    "%lld pt" : {
      "comment" : "Value shown to the right of a slider in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. %lld is a whole number of points (pt, the macOS unit of screen size). Narrow, fixed width, so keep it short."
    },
    "%lld selected" : {
      "comment" : "Counter at the right of the search bar of the Export sheet. %lld is the number of credentials currently selected; it can be 0. Very short."
    },
    "+%lld more" : {
      "comment" : "Short fragment after a list: “example.com +2 more” for an import review row’s extra websites, and “A, B, C +4 more” for credential names in the Suggested Merges sheet. %lld is how many are not shown. Lowercase “more”."
    },
    "1 day" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Keep entries for” menu of Input History (Settings › Autofill, Vault tab): how long recorded entries are kept. Also inserted into the footnote “…each kept for %@”. A fixed span, so write the form for 1."
    },
    "1 file" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment of the detail line of a credential row in the list, after Password, Passkey and so on, separated by “ · ”: the credential has one attached file. Singular; the plural is “%lld files”."
    },
    "1 item will be deleted permanently when you leave Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Trash list of the Credentials page after the user marks one Trash item for deletion with X. Nothing is deleted until the user leaves Trash, and the notice offers Undo. Singular; the plural is a separate entry."
    },
    "1 week" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Keep entries for” menu of Input History (Settings › Autofill, Vault tab): how long recorded entries are kept. Also inserted into the footnote “…each kept for %@”. A fixed span, so write the form for 1."
    },
    "2 hours" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Keep entries for” menu of Input History (Settings › Autofill, Vault tab): how long recorded entries are kept. Also inserted into the footnote “…each kept for %@”. A fixed span, not a count, so write the right form for 2."
    },
    "30 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Keep entries for” menu of Input History (Settings › Autofill, Vault tab): how long recorded entries are kept. Also inserted into the footnote “…each kept for %@”. A fixed span, not a count, so write the right form for 30."
    },
    "^[%lld matching credential](inflect: true)" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement when the number of matching rows changes while the user searches the fill dropdown for a saved login. %lld is the number of matches. It uses automatic grammar agreement markup, “^[…](inflect: true)”, so keep that structure; the counterpart for zero is “No matches”."
    },
    "a card or other item" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds a card or other item.” An item saved with a credential, such as a payment card or an address. Singular; the plural is “%lld cards and other items”."
    },
    "A connected app controls this tab. Take it over first." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown when the user tries to unload (put to sleep) a tab that a connected app, an external MCP client, is controlling. Take Over is the name of the command in the tab’s context menu and in the connected-app popover."
    },
    "A copy from before the vault was upgraded still exists at %@ and still holds them; delete it yourself if you want it gone." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the permanent-deletion warning when a copy of the vault made before its upgrade to a new format still exists. %@ is the file path of that copy and stays untranslated. “Them” means the items being deleted. Joined with other sentences into one paragraph."
    },
    "A copy from before the vault was upgraded. It lacks every change made since." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a file path in the “Credentials can’t be opened” card: this file is the backup made before the vault was upgraded to a newer format. Sentences."
    },
    "A copy from before this vault was upgraded still exists at %@ and still holds its old contents. WSurf never deletes it; delete it yourself if you want it gone." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Delete Vault sheet about the backup copy made before the vault was upgraded. %@ is the file path of that copy (a path, not to be translated). Sentence case."
    },
    "A copy of the older vault kept while an upgrade was in progress." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a file path in the “Credentials can’t be opened” card: this file is a copy of the older vault kept during an upgrade. Sentence."
    },
    "A credential that holds several kinds counts under each. Passkeys counts every passkey." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Statistics section. A credential can hold several kinds of data, for example a password and a passkey, and is then counted in each kind’s row. “Passkeys” is the name of the Passkeys row and must match its translation; that row counts every passkey, not just the credentials holding one."
    },
    "A credential vault already exists for this profile. Unlock it instead." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the user tries to create a vault but the profile already has one. The second sentence tells the user to unlock it."
    },
    "A credential with the same identity is already in the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused, after “This can’t be restored right now.”: the vault already holds a credential with the same internal identity as the removed one. Joined with the sentences around it into one paragraph."
    },
    "A CSV file holds only passwords with a website. It will not contain: %lld logins without a website, %lld credentials without a password, %lld passkeys or %lld verification code setups. Notes are written only for a login whose Notes choice is on." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the Export Passwords to CSV sheet (Settings › Autofill), shown before anything is written. It lists what a CSV file cannot hold. The four %lld are, in order: logins without a website, credentials without a password, passkeys, and verification code setups. “Notes” is the Notes checkbox in the list below the paragraph."
    },
    "A CSV file holds passwords with their websites only, and isn’t encrypted: delete it once you have used it. Passkeys and verification codes can only be moved with Export… and the system’s credential exchange." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Import & Export section. “Export…” names the button of the Export to another app row and must match it. The system’s credential exchange is the macOS way of moving credentials between apps. CSV stays untranslated."
    },
    "A driver’s license" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A driver’s license item."
    },
    "A field was saved as plain text without its original details." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a field of a received item was kept as plain text, without its original type, ID or label. Full sentence."
    },
    "A generated password" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A password generated by the other app; WSurf does not store this kind."
    },
    "A kind of item WSurf doesn’t know" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. Used for a kind of item that this version of WSurf doesn’t recognize; WSurf does not store it."
    },
    "A line around the edge of the window. It follows the corners." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Border setting in Settings › Appearance › Window, and its Settings search description. The line runs along the window’s rounded corners. Two short sentences with final full stops."
    },
    "A link to another item" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. An entry that only points to another item; WSurf does not store this kind."
    },
    "A login" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A username and password for a website."
    },
    "A login has no username and no password, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a login was skipped because it has neither a username nor a password. Full sentence."
    },
    "A name" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A person’s name item."
    },
    "A new passkey for an additional vault needs one of your other vaults unlocked first." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Create Credential Vault sheet, shown when New passkey is disabled because the profile already has a vault and none is unlocked to approve creating another. “Additional” means any vault after the first."
    },
    "A note" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A text note."
    },
    "a note" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds a note.” A free-text note saved with a credential. Singular; the plural is “%lld notes”. Never starts a sentence."
    },
    "A note added" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: one note was added in WSurf that the other app’s copy doesn’t have. Singular counterpart of “%lld notes added”. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "A passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A passkey, the sign-in credential that replaces a password."
    },
    "a passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds a note and a passkey.” Singular; the plural is “%lld passkeys”. Never starts a sentence."
    },
    "A passkey for “%@” on %@ was saved to Credential Manager, but WSurf could not confirm that the website received it. Test signing in on the website, and remove the passkey in Settings if it does not work." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Passkey saved, but not confirmed” alert. First %@ is the user name the website asked to register; second %@ is the website’s domain, such as example.com. Neither is translated. Keep the curly quotation marks."
    },
    "A passkey has no user handle, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because it has no user handle (the technical identifier of the account the passkey belongs to). Full sentence."
    },
    "a passkey key is larger than %@ bytes" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. “Passkey key” means the cryptographic key stored inside a passkey. %@ is the maximum size in bytes."
    },
    "A passkey uses a signature type other than ES256, which WSurf doesn’t support, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because it signs with something other than ES256 (a standard signature algorithm; leave the name as is). Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey was saved here, but WSurf could not confirm that the website received it. Unlock to see which one." : {
      "comment" : "Note on the locked card when WSurf saved a passkey but could not confirm that the website got it. “Which one” means which passkey; Unlock is the button on the same card. Sentence."
    },
    "A passkey with the same ID but another key is already saved, so it isn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row that is skipped: a saved passkey has the same ID but a different cryptographic key, so this one is not imported. ID is the passkey’s technical identifier."
    },
    "A passkey’s credential ID is empty or longer than %lld bytes, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because its credential ID (its technical identifier) is missing or too long. %lld is the maximum length in bytes. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s extension data is too large, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because the optional extension data (FIDO2 extensions) stored with it is too large. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s private key isn’t in a format WSurf can read, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because its private key can’t be read by WSurf. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s user handle is longer than %lld bytes, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because its user handle (the technical identifier of its account) is too long. %lld is the maximum length in bytes. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s user name or display name is longer than %lld bytes, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because its user name or display name is too long. %lld is the maximum length in bytes. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s website couldn’t be checked because WSurf’s list of domain suffixes isn’t available, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because WSurf couldn’t load its list of domain suffixes (the public endings such as “com”) to check the passkey’s website. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passkey’s website isn’t a valid name or is a domain suffix such as “com”, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a passkey was skipped because its website is not a valid name or is only a domain suffix (the public ending shared by many sites). “com” is an example. Full sentence."
    },
    "A passport" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A passport item."
    },
    "A payment card" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A payment card item."
    },
    "A profile keeps at least one vault. Nothing was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the user tries to delete a profile’s only vault. Full sentences."
    },
    "A profile keeps at least one vault. To remove its credentials, move them to Trash and empty it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Delete vault row when the profile has only one vault. A profile is a WSurf browser profile. At the end, “it” means Trash."
    },
    "A saved credential already uses this username on the same website." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused, after “This can’t be restored right now.”: another saved credential has the same username for the same website. Joined with the sentences around it into one paragraph."
    },
    "A saved passkey for the same website and account already exists." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused, after “This can’t be restored right now.”: the vault already has a passkey for the same website and account. Joined with the sentences around it into one paragraph."
    },
    "A selected credential changed or WSurf was locked, so no credentials were sent. Review the selection and export again." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the export sheet when a selected credential changed, or WSurf locked, before the export could be handed over. Review is a verb here (look the selection over again), not a button name. Full sentences."
    },
    "A temporary file from checking the vault couldn’t be removed. It holds only opaque ids and digests, and you can delete it yourself." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a file path in the Vault check section. “Opaque ids and digests” are meaningless identifiers and hashes, not secrets; the user may delete the file by hand."
    },
    "A verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A one-time code used for two-step verification."
    },
    "a verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds a verification code.” A one-time sign-in code; there is no plural version. Never starts a sentence."
    },
    "A verification code has settings WSurf can’t use, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a verification code (one-time code) was skipped because its settings, such as algorithm, digits or period, aren’t usable. Full sentence."
    },
    "a website" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment inside a sentence on an import review row, such as “Merging adds a website and a passkey.” Singular; the plural is “%lld websites”. Never starts a sentence."
    },
    "A Wi-Fi network" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A Wi-Fi network item."
    },
    "Accent color" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the highlight color of the interface. Sentence case."
    },
    "Accessing credentials…" : {
      "comment" : "Heading with a spinner on the locked Credentials card while WSurf is busy with the vault, such as unlocking it, and no vault check is running. Ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Account %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Extra detail on a row of the autofill dropdown. When two saved logins would look identical, each gets a number to tell them apart. %lld is the position, 1, 2, 3 and so on."
    },
    "Account: %@ — %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the passkey sheet naming the one account that will be used. First %@ is the account’s name (its display name or user name), second %@ is further detail about it, such as the user name. Keep the dash between them."
    },
    "Actions for %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the ⋯ menu button on a file row in the Files section of the credential editor. %@ is the file’s name and is not translated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Actions for all" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label only, for the ⋯ menu button in an import review group heading; its menu acts on every item of the group at once."
    },
    "Active" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the first segment of the two-segment switch (Active and Trash) above the credentials list on the Vault tab: it shows the saved credentials that are not in Trash. One word, an adjective; the switch is narrow, so keep it short."
    },
    "Add %@ to “%@”?" : {
      "comment" : "Headline of the toolbar popover offering to add the current website to a saved login of a related website instead of saving a copy. First %@ is the current website (address-bar form), second %@ is the saved login’s name. A question."
    },
    "Add a login, or choose what to add from the menu" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the plus Add button on the Vault tab: clicking adds a login, and its arrow offers other kinds of entry. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Add a login, passkey or verification code to see it here." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the “No credentials” empty state on the Vault tab."
    },
    "Add Credential" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the credential editor sheet when a new credential is being created; the Edit Credential heading replaces it for an existing one. Also the VoiceOver label of the Add (+) button at the top of the credential list. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Add Favorite" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the context menu of sidebar tabs and splits: adds the tab to the Favorites tiles at the top of the sidebar. Title Case, a verb phrase. Counterpart “Remove Favorite”."
    },
    "Add Field" : {
      "comment" : "Small button with a plus icon at the bottom of a custom-fields item in the credential editor that adds a new field; also the title of a menu on other items that adds a missing field, such as a card’s PIN. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Add File…" : {
      "comment" : "Button with a plus icon in the Files section of the credential editor; it opens the Mac file chooser. Title Case, a verb phrase, ellipsis because a panel follows."
    },
    "Add Item" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the menu button with a plus icon in the Cards and other items section of the credential editor; its menu lists kinds of item to add. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Add Note" : {
      "comment" : "Button with a plus icon in the Notes section of the credential editor that adds a new empty note. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Add note %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the “Add” button beside a note of the earlier version in the History panel. %lld is the note’s position in that version’s notes, starting at 1. A verb phrase."
    },
    "Add Separately" : {
      "comment" : "Action in the import review sheet, on an item that conflicts with a saved credential and in the menu of one of its parts: adds the other app’s version as a separate credential next to the saved one. Title Case, a command; tight space."
    },
    "Add Sign-in and Websites" : {
      "comment" : "Small button in the credential editor of an identity; it reveals the sign-in, websites, verification code and passkey sections so the identity can have a login after all. Title Case, a verb phrase; “Sign-in” is a noun."
    },
    "Add Unlock Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the chip button with a plus icon in the Unlock passkeys section header; it starts adding another passkey that can unlock the vault. Verb phrase, Title Case, tight."
    },
    "Add Website" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the toolbar popover that adds the current website to an existing saved login; it saves no new copy. Title Case, a verb phrase. It can be the secondary button, next to “Not Now”, when the site looks like an imitation."
    },
    "Add website %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the “Add” button beside a website that the earlier version had and the current credential lacks; it puts the website back into the editor. %@ is the website address and should not be translated."
    },
    "Added %lld entries to the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after cards (from a Safari export) or contacts were imported into the vault; it offers Undo. %lld is the number of new entries, 2 or more; the singular is a separate entry."
    },
    "Added 1 entry to the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after cards (from a Safari export) or contacts were imported into the vault; it offers Undo. Singular form; the plural is “Added %lld entries to the vault.”"
    },
    "Address save suggestions" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Save and fill section of Settings › Autofill, with the caption “Restore prompts on excluded sites.” and a Reset button that brings back the offers to save contact details and addresses on sites where the user chose not to be asked again. Sentence case."
    },
    "Addresses" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: entries that hold a postal address. A plural noun; tight."
    },
    "Adds %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row, after “Same website, username and password as …”. %@ is a list joined with “and” of fragments such as “a note and a passkey”."
    },
    "Adds to a credential that is already saved." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row for a new item that Import adds to a credential that is already saved, rather than creating a new one."
    },
    "Adjust the text size in the sidebar." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Sidebar font size” entry in Settings › Appearance. Imperative."
    },
    "Adjusted a little so it stays readable." : {
      "comment" : "Note under a text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance when the color drawn differs slightly from the chosen one, changed by the least amount that keeps the text readable."
    },
    "After 1 hour" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Lock credentials” pop-up menu in the Vaults section of Settings › Credentials: how long the selected vault stays unlocked, counted from the unlock. Singular; the one choice counted in hours. Sentence case."
    },
    "After 1 minute" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Lock credentials” pop-up menu in the Vaults section of Settings › Credentials: how long the selected vault stays unlocked, counted from the unlock. Singular counterpart of the “After 5 minutes” style choices. Sentence case."
    },
    "After 15 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Lock credentials” pop-up menu in the Vaults section of Settings › Credentials: how long the selected vault stays unlocked, counted from the unlock. Plural; a number of minutes follows “After”. Sentence case."
    },
    "After 30 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Lock credentials” pop-up menu in the Vaults section of Settings › Credentials: how long the selected vault stays unlocked, counted from the unlock. Plural; a number of minutes follows “After”. Sentence case."
    },
    "After 5 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the “Lock credentials” pop-up menu in the Vaults section of Settings › Credentials: how long the selected vault stays unlocked, counted from the unlock. Plural; a number of minutes follows “After”. Sentence case."
    },
    "After this, the passwords you imported exist only in your vault. If you lose every passkey that unlocks it, they can’t be recovered. You can add a second unlock passkey in Credential Manager." : {
      "comment" : "Second paragraph of the “Remove the Old Passwords List?” confirmation: after removal the imported passwords exist only in the vault, so losing every unlock passkey makes them unrecoverable. Full sentences. “Credential Manager” is the feature’s name."
    },
    "After: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the Websites part of the merge sheet. %@ is the merged credential’s websites after the merge: host names joined as a list by the system, or “No website”. Fragment, very short."
    },
    "AI" : {
      "comment" : "Text of a tiny capsule badge on a sidebar tab row meaning an external app (connected by MCP) holds access to that tab. Abbreviation of artificial intelligence; use the common local abbreviation. Two letters at most, very tight."
    },
    "All" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip with a count after it, such as “All 12”: every item in the import review sheet, and every kind of entry in the Vault tab’s list of credentials. One word, very tight."
    },
    "Allow Development" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the dialog that asks whether a connected app may access a tab, next to Read Only, Allow Control and Don’t Allow. It grants development access: inspecting page structure and styles, reading console and network metadata, and changing the viewport. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Already saved" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a group in the import review sheet, and its filter chip: items already in the vault or changed only in WSurf. Also the first word of an import receipt line for a credential that was left unchanged. A state, not a command. Sentence case."
    },
    "Already saved as “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the details of one part of an import review row: the saved credential that holds it. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated. No final period."
    },
    "Already saved as “%@”, with a different value." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: the saved credential named in the quotes holds this part, but with a different value than the other app’s. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Already saved as “%@”. Choose what to do with the rest of this item." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: one part of the item matches the saved credential named in the quotes, while another part still needs a decision. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Already saved as “%@”. Import links the two, so the next import finds it unchanged." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: the item is the same as the saved credential named in the quotes. Import only records that link, so the next import finds it unchanged. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Already saved as “%@”. Nothing changes." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row that matches the saved credential named in the quotes and will be left alone. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Already saved. Nothing changes." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row that is already saved and will be left alone."
    },
    "Also fill on" : {
      "comment" : "Small bold sub-heading in the Websites part of the merge sheet over checkboxes, one per website of another site; ticking one makes the merged credential fill there too. Sentence case, a fragment."
    },
    "Also kept" : {
      "comment" : "Sub-heading in the merge sheet over lines counting what the merge keeps in addition: passkeys, notes, items and passwords in History. Sentence case."
    },
    "Also saved in %@." : {
      "comment" : "Follows the reuse note in the credential editor in Settings › Credentials. %@ is a list of the names of the other credentials that save the same password, joined in the system’s list format: at most three names, then “%lld more”. A full sentence."
    },
    "An address" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A postal address item."
    },
    "An API key" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. A stored API key item."
    },
    "An earlier import brought these, and this transfer doesn’t have them. They stay in WSurf unless you move them to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “No longer in Passwords” heading in the import review sheet. “These” are the listed credentials; Trash is the vault’s Trash. Sentences."
    },
    "An entry can hold up to %lld files. Remove one to add another." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when Add File… is used on an entry that already holds the most files allowed. %lld is that maximum number of files per entry. “Entry” is the credential being edited. Full sentences."
    },
    "An external connection" : {
      "comment" : "Fallback name for the connected app in the title of the dialog asking whether it may answer a webpage’s prompt, used when the app did not give its name. It stands in for %@ in “Let “%@” answer a prompt?”. Sentence case, no period."
    },
    "an identifier is repeated" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. It says that the same internal identifier appears twice in the received data."
    },
    "An identity document" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. An identity document item."
    },
    "An item added" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: one card or other item was added in WSurf that the other app’s copy doesn’t have. Singular counterpart of “%lld items added”."
    },
    "An item has more than %lld values. Only the first %lld were imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: a card, address or other item held more values (fields) than WSurf keeps, so only the first were kept. Both %lld are the same number: the maximum number of values per item. Full sentences."
    },
    "An older-format vault file reappeared after the vault was upgraded, so WSurf can’t tell which one is current." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: a vault file in the older format came back after the vault had been upgraded, so WSurf can’t tell which file is the current one. Sentence."
    },
    "An SSH key" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in a credential transfer. It begins the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet, so it keeps its article (A/An) and Sentence case. An SSH key item. SSH is a technical name; leave it as is."
    },
    "An upgrade of the older vault didn’t finish." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: an earlier upgrade of the older vault format was started and did not finish. Sentence."
    },
    "and %lld more lines with notes." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after the first notes about lines of the CSV file. %lld is how many more lines have a note. Here “notes” are remarks about lines, not the Notes feature. Starts lowercase."
    },
    "and %lld more." : {
      "comment" : "Last line of the “Not imported” list in the import review sheet. %lld is how many more entries are not shown. Starts lowercase."
    },
    "Android apps can’t be used here, so they weren’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: the Android apps listed for an item were left out because WSurf can’t use them; the item is kept. Plural subject. Full sentence."
    },
    "Another copy of WSurf is keeping Input History." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when another running copy of WSurf already has Input History open, so this copy cannot. WSurf is the app’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Another import is already in progress." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the user starts an import while another one is still open. Full sentence."
    },
    "Another row already replaces that saved login. Change that one first." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the import review when two incoming rows both try to replace the same saved login. Row means a line of the review list. The user is asked to change the other one first."
    },
    "Another transfer is already in progress; this one was not received. Finish or cancel it, then export again from Passwords." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials, shown when another app sends credentials to WSurf while an earlier transfer is still waiting or being reviewed; the new one is refused. Passwords is Apple’s Passwords app (keep its system name). Full sentences."
    },
    "another vault" : {
      "comment" : "Lower-case fragment substituted into “Kept in %@. Moving it needs both vaults unlocked…” when the vault now keeping Input History is not among the listed vaults. Reads as “another vault”, not a sentence."
    },
    "Answer Page Dialog" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app accepts or dismisses a dialog that a web page opened (an alert, confirm or prompt box). Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Any one of these passkeys unlocks the vault. Keep at least one." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Unlock passkeys section. The second sentence is an imperative: the user must not remove all of them."
    },
    "Assistant color" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the color used for the assistant’s interface. Sentence case. The assistant is WSurf’s built-in AI helper."
    },
    "Authentication didn’t finish. Nothing was exported." : {
      "comment" : "Error message on the Credentials page in Settings when the Touch ID or passkey check was cancelled or failed during an export. Full sentences."
    },
    "Authentication didn’t finish. Nothing was shown or copied." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the Touch ID or passkey check was cancelled or failed before revealing or copying a secret. Full sentences."
    },
    "Authentication required" : {
      "comment" : "Message line of the sign-in sheet for a website’s HTTP login (username and password fields) in a Chromium tab, shown when the server supplies no realm text. The sheet’s title is the server’s host name. Buttons are Sign In and Cancel. Sentence case, no final full stop."
    },
    "Autofill and saving will use “%@” instead." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Delete Vault sheet, shown when the vault being deleted is the default one. %@ is the name of the other vault that will become the default (a name, not to be translated). Sentence case."
    },
    "Before: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the Websites part of the merge sheet. %@ is the primary credential’s websites before the merge: host names joined as a list by the system, or “No website”. Fragment, very short."
    },
    "Behind the tabs and the page, and under the side panel." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Window background row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance: where this color shows. The side panel is the panel that opens beside the page."
    },
    "Brightness" : {
      "comment" : "Row title of the slider in Settings › Appearance › Theme that makes the theme’s colors darker or lighter; also the title of its Settings search result. A noun."
    },
    "Browser Engine" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the toolbar’s site controls popover with a menu to choose WebKit or Chromium for the current website. Title Case, a noun phrase. WebKit and Chromium are names, not translated."
    },
    "Browser engine" : {
      "comment" : "Row title with a menu to choose WebKit or Chromium, on a single website’s page in Settings › Websites, and the title of that row in Settings search. Sentence case. WebKit and Chromium are names, not translated."
    },
    "Browsing data could not be cleared. WSurf will stay open." : {
      "comment" : "Title of a warning alert shown while quitting, when clearing browsing data for the Clear on quit setting fails. The quit is cancelled, so the app stays open; the alert’s message is the system’s error text. WSurf is the app name and is not translated."
    },
    "Built-in themes don’t change. Your first edit makes a copy named “%@ Custom” that you can rename." : {
      "comment" : "First note in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance while a built-in theme is selected. %@ is that theme’s name, such as Nord, so the copy is called “Nord Custom”. Keep the curly quotation marks around the name."
    },
    "Buttons, highlights, drop targets and the new-tab dot." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Accent color row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance: where the accent shows. The new-tab dot is a small dot marking a new tab."
    },
    "By Site" : {
      "comment" : "Toggle button next to the search field of the Vault tab’s list: groups credentials under a heading per website. Title Case; a small button, so space is tight."
    },
    "Calm" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a built-in theme (soft, muted pastel colors) on a card in Settings › Appearance and in the list “Choose WSurf, Standard, Calm…”. An ordinary adjective used as a name; translate it, keeping Title Case."
    },
    "Card numbers, security codes (CVV), PINs, document numbers, Wi-Fi passwords and API and SSH keys leave the vault, and the app you pick can read them. Exporting a card or an ID document asks for Touch ID first." : {
      "comment" : "Warning paragraph under that list: the secret values of cards, documents and keys leave the vault, and the receiving app can read them. CVV, PIN, API and SSH are abbreviations. Touch ID is Apple’s product name."
    },
    "Card save suggestions" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Save and fill section of Settings › Autofill, with the caption “Restore prompts on excluded sites.” and a Reset button that brings back the offers to save payment cards on sites where the user chose not to be asked again. Sentence case."
    },
    "Card type" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Payment card item: the type or brand of the card. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Cards" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: entries that hold a payment card. A plural noun; tight."
    },
    "Cards and addresses are saved in a vault. Create one to import them." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Safari payment cards import row in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab), shown only while no vault exists yet. Sentence case."
    },
    "Cards and addresses moved to the vault" : {
      "comment" : "Row title of the card in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) shown after the move, with counts in the caption and the buttons Undo and Erase Old Copies…. Sentence case; a statement of what happened."
    },
    "Cards and addresses saved on this Mac" : {
      "comment" : "Row title of a card on Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) offering to move payment cards and addresses that were saved on this Mac before the vault existed into the vault; its button is Review…. Sentence case."
    },
    "Cards and other items" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor over the cards, addresses, ID documents and custom fields of an entry. Also a line in the vault statistics, a row title in the History panel, and a part name in the export and import lists. Noun phrase, sentence case."
    },
    "cards and other items" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment in an account’s line in the passkey account chooser, saying the account also holds payment cards or other secure items. Joined with other fragments by a middle dot, so keep it short and lowercase."
    },
    "Cards and other items in this export, with every value they hold:" : {
      "comment" : "Bold heading above a list in the Export Credentials sheet. Each line below names a kind of item (payment card, address, Wi-Fi network and so on) and the values it carries. Ends in a colon because the list follows."
    },
    "Cards and other items removed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: cards and other items were removed in WSurf after an earlier import, and the removal is kept. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Cards and other items: %lld → %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Line under “Also kept” in the merge sheet. First %lld is how many cards and other items the primary credential has now, second %lld how many the merged one will have. Keep the arrow. Fragment."
    },
    "Cards or other items changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the credential’s cards or other items, such as addresses or Wi-Fi networks, differ from the transfer’s copy. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Catppuccin" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a built-in color theme in Settings › Appearance. Proper name of a community palette; do not translate."
    },
    "Changed" : {
      "comment" : "Label before a colon and a comma-separated list of credential names, in the notice shown when the vault changed while the Export sheet was open: the selected credentials that changed. The colon is added by the app. One word."
    },
    "Changed by a merge" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for an earlier version that merging two saved credentials into one replaced. Sentence case."
    },
    "Changed by an import" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for an earlier version that an import (credentials brought in from another app or a file) replaced. Sentence case."
    },
    "Changed by Undo" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for an earlier version replaced by Undo (or Redo), which puts back what an earlier action changed. Undo is the name of the command. Sentence case."
    },
    "Changed here and in the other app since the last import." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: both the saved version in WSurf and the other app’s version changed since the previous import, so the user must choose. “Here” means in WSurf."
    },
    "Changed here since the last import. Your version stays." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: the item changed only in WSurf since the last import, so the saved version stays. “Here” means in WSurf; “your version” is the saved one."
    },
    "Changed in the other app" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a group in the import review sheet, and its filter chip with a count after it: items that are already saved and changed only in the app the credentials came from since the last import. Sentence case."
    },
    "Changed in the other app. Its version is used, and yours is kept as an earlier version." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: the item changed in the other app, so Import uses that version and keeps the saved one as an earlier version in the credential’s history. “Its” is the other app’s; “yours” is the saved one."
    },
    "Changed in WSurf (kept)" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a collapsible section in the import review sheet, followed by a count of credentials: ones changed in WSurf since an earlier import, which this import leaves as they are. Also the VoiceOver label of its toggle. Sentence case."
    },
    "Changes are saved to this theme as you make them." : {
      "comment" : "First note in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance while one of the user’s own saved themes is selected: each color change is written to that theme at once."
    },
    "Changes saved." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user saved changes to an existing credential in the editor; it offers Undo. Counterpart of “Credential added.”. Full sentence."
    },
    "Changes the Dock icon while WSurf is running." : {
      "comment" : "Caption above the Dock icon choice cards in Settings › Appearance: the choice only affects the Dock while the app runs. WSurf is the app name and is not translated."
    },
    "Changing engines reloads the website and resets Back/Forward history. Sign-ins are separate. Unloaded Chromium tabs restore only their URL." : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the Browser Engine row in the toolbar’s site controls popover. Back and Forward are the toolbar buttons; unloaded tabs are tabs put to sleep. Chromium is an engine name, not translated. Sentence."
    },
    "Changing the window, sidebar or surface color draws this theme as a solid ground, without the website tint." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Colors card for a theme that takes its look from the page: changing the Window background, Sidebar or Surface color switches it to a plain solid background without the website’s color. Website tint is the name of a switch in Settings › Appearance."
    },
    "Changing this reloads the website and resets Back/Forward history. Sign-ins are separate. Unloaded Chromium tabs restore only their URL." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Browser engine row in Settings › Websites for a website whose engine can be chosen; it warns what changing the engine does. Chromium is an engine name, not translated; Back/Forward names the toolbar’s Back and Forward buttons. Sentences."
    },
    "Check Again" : {
      "comment" : "Main button of the “Credentials can’t be opened” card: looks at the files again without changing any of them. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Check other logins for *.%@" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the autofill dropdown shown when nothing is saved for this exact website but logins exist for other websites of the same site; choosing it lists them. %@ is the site’s domain name, such as example.com, and “*.” is a wildcard that stays as is. Verb phrase. Sentence case."
    },
    "Checking the vault before saving" : {
      "comment" : "Short noun phrase naming the step that failed, inserted as %@ at the start of “… failed and nothing was written …” in an import error message. Sentence case, no period; it must work as the start of a sentence."
    },
    "Choose %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the calendar button beside a date field in the credential editor. %@ is the field’s name as the user typed it and is not translated. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Choose a passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder option of the pop-up menu below Use existing passkey in the Create Credential Vault sheet; nothing is chosen until the user picks one of the passkeys listed under it. Imperative, Sentence case."
    },
    "Choose a passkey…" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder first item of the pop-up menu in the sign-in passkey sheet when several passkeys match; nothing is chosen until the user picks one. Sentence case; keep the ellipsis."
    },
    "Choose a password CSV file, such as one exported from Passwords." : {
      "comment" : "Message line of the file chooser opened by Choose File… in Import & Export. Passwords is Apple’s Passwords app; CSV stays untranslated. Imperative."
    },
    "Choose at least two credentials to merge." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown in the merge sheet of the Credentials page when fewer than two credentials are selected. Full sentence; “merge” is a verb."
    },
    "Choose between 2 and %lld credentials to merge." : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip on the disabled Merge… button in the bar above the credential list, shown when too few or too many credentials are selected. %lld is the most credentials that can be merged at once. Sentence case."
    },
    "Choose Contacts…" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Import contacts row of Settings › Autofill (Vault tab): it opens the system contact picker. Shown off while the vault is locked. A verb phrase, Title Case; the ellipsis means a picker follows."
    },
    "Choose Date" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the calendar button beside a date field of a custom field in the credential editor; it opens a calendar to pick the date. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Choose files to keep encrypted with this entry." : {
      "comment" : "Message line at the top of the Mac file chooser opened by Add File… in the credential editor. “Entry” is the credential being edited; encrypted means stored in the vault. Sentence."
    },
    "Choose Plain or Glass. Glass shows your desktop through the window and uses more GPU." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Material” entry in Settings › Appearance. Plain and Glass are the two window materials, named like the choices in that setting. GPU is the graphics processor. Imperative."
    },
    "Choose regular, medium, semibold, or bold sidebar text." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Sidebar font weight” entry. The four words name font weights and match the menu choices in Settings › Appearance. Imperative."
    },
    "Choose the icon the Dock shows while WSurf is running." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Dock icon” entry in Settings › Appearance. Dock is the macOS Dock; WSurf is the app’s name, not translated. Imperative."
    },
    "Choose the page edge, corner rounding and page spacing of this theme, in the Window section." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Window layout” entry in Settings › Appearance: the layout options of a theme that shape the page, found in the Window section. Imperative; theme means a set of colors and layout."
    },
    "Choose the tab and folder edges, sidebar margin, tab padding, folder indent for each level and tab icons of this theme, in the Sidebar section." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Sidebar layout” entry in Settings › Appearance: the layout options of a theme that shape the sidebar, found in the Sidebar section. Imperative; theme means a set of colors and layout."
    },
    "Choose the ZIP that Safari exported, or its PaymentCards.json file." : {
      "comment" : "Message line of the file-open panel opened by Choose File… in the payment cards import row of Settings › Autofill. ZIP is the archive format; PaymentCards.json is a file name and is not translated; Safari is not translated."
    },
    "Choose WebKit or Chromium for each website." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Browser engine” entry in Settings › Websites. WebKit and Chromium are browser engine names, not translated. Imperative."
    },
    "Choose what to do with every conflict first." : {
      "comment" : "Message on the Credentials page in Settings when the user presses Import in the import review before choosing an action for every conflicting credential. Full sentence; the user must decide on all conflicts first."
    },
    "Choose what to do." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the status line of an import review row that waits for the user’s decision. An instruction to the user."
    },
    "Choose what to send to another app. The system passes your selection to the app you pick next, and that app can read it: any passwords, passkeys, verification code setups, notes, cards and other items you select aren’t encrypted by WSurf. WSurf doesn’t write a file, and your vault keeps its own copy." : {
      "comment" : "Explanatory paragraph in the Export Credentials sheet, the hand-off to another app: the app the user picks next can read what is sent, WSurf writes no file, and the vault keeps its own copy."
    },
    "Choose WSurf, Standard, Calm, Catppuccin, Nord, Dracula, Gruvbox, or Rosé Pine." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Theme” entry. The list names the built-in themes. WSurf, Catppuccin, Nord, Dracula, Gruvbox and Rosé Pine are proper names; Standard and Calm should match how they are translated as theme names."
    },
    "Chromium" : {
      "comment" : "Name of one of the two browser engines a website can open in, as listed in a website’s engine choice (site controls popover and Website Settings) and inserted into sentences. Chromium is the engine’s name and is never translated."
    },
    "Chromium can clear website data only for all time." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown after Clear Browsing Data when cookies or cache were chosen with a time range shorter than all time and the profile has data stored by Chromium, which can only clear that data completely. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium cookies are unavailable." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when clearing website data and Chromium’s cookie store cannot be reached. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium cookies could not be cleared." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when clearing website data and Chromium refused to delete its cookies. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium cookies could not be saved." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when clearing website data and Chromium could not write its cookie store to disk after the cookies were deleted. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium could not create this browsing profile." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when the Chromium engine failed to set up storage for a browsing profile (a WSurf profile) before opening a page. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium could not open this tab." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when the Chromium engine failed to create the browser for a new tab. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium did not return a page archive." : {
      "comment" : "Error text in the alert titled The page couldn’t be saved. when a Chromium tab did not give back the page archive (MHTML file) for Save Page As. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium did not return a page image." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when a Chromium tab did not give back a screenshot image of the page, for a viewport, region or full-page capture. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium did not return a printable page." : {
      "comment" : "Error text in the alert titled The page couldn’t be printed. when a Chromium tab did not give back a PDF to print. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Chromium requires an attached browser view." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when a Chromium page is asked to start while it is not shown in a window. Chromium is the engine’s name and stays untranslated. A technical message; keep it plain."
    },
    "Clear Input History" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Clear Input History?” dialog: deletes all recorded entries on this Mac. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Clear Input History?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog for deleting every Input History entry. Buttons are “Clear Input History” and “Cancel”. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Clear Input History…" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the top right of the Entries section in Input History. It opens the confirmation dialog, hence the ellipsis. Title Case, a verb phrase; can be disabled while the list is empty."
    },
    "Clear Site Data" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app deletes a tab’s saved website data, such as cookies and local storage, so the site loads signed out. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Click each contact you want, then close the list: they are reviewed together." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Import contacts row in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab): the system contact picker stays open while each clicked contact is collected, and all of them are reviewed together once it closes. Sentence case."
    },
    "Code is set up" : {
      "comment" : "Title shown above a live verification code in the credential editor when its setup key carries no service or account name (otherwise those names are shown). A state, sentence case."
    },
    "Colors" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the expandable Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and of its entry in Settings search. Noun, plural; the card edits the selected theme’s colors."
    },
    "Columns %@ hold data WSurf doesn’t import." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the import review for a CSV file. %@ is a comma-separated list of column numbers whose data WSurf does not import. WSurf is the app’s name and should not be translated."
    },
    "Comment" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an SSH key item: the comment attached to the key. Noun."
    },
    "Compare Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app compares two shared tabs that show the same page (differing pixels, layout, console and network). Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Contacts" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: entries that hold a person’s name and an address together. A plural noun; tight."
    },
    "Control" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the access level, between Read only and Development, that lets a connected app click, type and navigate on a tab. Shown in small text beside the app’s name in the toolbar connection chip and the controlled-tab popover. A noun, not a verb."
    },
    "Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Generic brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after copying any other value, such as a card number or the account a verification code is for. One word, a past participle. Title Case."
    },
    "Copied. It leaves the clipboard in a minute." : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation note (checkmark icon) under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill after an entry is copied. WSurf clears the clipboard a minute later unless something else was copied since. Two short sentences."
    },
    "Copies %@ of “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Why a merge is suggested: several numbered copies of a username. First argument: a list of copy numbers, e.g. (1) and (2). Second: the username."
    },
    "Copies %@ of “%@”, same password" : {
      "comment" : "As Copies %@ of “%@”, with the same password (Merge All Identical takes these)."
    },
    "Copy %@" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy-icon button beside each value of a card or other item in the credential editor, History panel and list. %@ is the field’s name, such as “Card number”. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy %@ of “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Why a merge is suggested: one numbered copy of a username, as exports name duplicates. First argument: the copy number in parentheses, e.g. (1). Second: the username."
    },
    "Copy %@ of “%@”, same password" : {
      "comment" : "As Copy %@ of “%@”, with the same password (Merge All Identical takes these)."
    },
    "copy a saved card, document or hidden field" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user copies a hidden value of a saved card or ID document. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "copy a saved password" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user copies a saved password from the credential list on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "copy a verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user copies the current verification code (one-time code) of a saved credential from the credential list on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "Copy current website %@" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy icon beside a website that only the current credential has, in the History panel. %@ is the website address and should not be translated. A verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy Name" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy-icon button beside the Name field in the credential editor; it copies the credential’s name. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy note %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy-icon button on a note in the credential editor; also used in the History panel. %lld is the note’s position, starting at 1. Sentence case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy passkey details" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the copy-icon menu on a passkey row in the credential editor; the menu offers Copy Username and Copy Website. Sentence case."
    },
    "Copy Password" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu and the right-click menu of a credential row, copying the password to the clipboard. Also the tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy button beside the Password field in the credential editor. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Copy the current %@" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of a copy icon beside the current value in the History panel. %@ is a lowercase noun such as name, username, password or verification code name, translated separately. A verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy this version’s %@" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of a copy icon beside the earlier version’s value in the History panel. %@ is a lowercase noun such as name, username, password or verification code name, translated separately. A verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy Username" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy-icon button beside the Username field in the credential editor. Also an item in the menu that copies a passkey’s account name, and in a credential row’s ⋯ menu in the list. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy Verification Code" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the copy-icon button beside a displayed one-time code in the credential editor; also an item in a credential row’s ⋯ menu in the list. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy Website" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the copy-icon menu beside the Websites caption in the credential editor; also an item in the menu that copies a passkey’s website, and in a credential row’s ⋯ menu in the list. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy website" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the small copy-icon menu beside the Websites caption in the credential editor; the menu lists each website to copy. Its tooltip is “Copy Website”. Sentence case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Copy website %@" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of a small copy icon beside a website of the earlier version in the History panel. %@ is the website address as saved; it should not be translated. A verb phrase."
    },
    "Corner rounding" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: how rounded the corners of tabs, folders and the page are. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Could not change website device access" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the warning alert shown when revoking or restoring a website’s camera or microphone access in a Chromium tab fails; the line below it is the specific reason. Sentence case, no final full stop."
    },
    "Couldn’t access credentials." : {
      "comment" : "Generic fallback error on the Credentials page in Settings when an action on the credential vault failed for an unknown reason. Full sentence."
    },
    "Couldn’t add this website. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error line in the popover that offers to add the current website to a saved login, shown when saving it failed. Full sentence; the second sentence is an instruction to retry."
    },
    "Couldn’t clear browsing data" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the error alert in Settings › Privacy when clearing browsing data, or counting the websites that store data, failed. The message is the system’s error text. Sentence case."
    },
    "Couldn’t clear history" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the error alert in the History view when clearing browsing history failed. The message is the system’s error text. Sentence case."
    },
    "Couldn’t find this window to show the passkey prompt. Bring it to the front and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error text on the Autofill page when the passkey prompt cannot be shown because the Settings window is not visible. Second sentence is an imperative."
    },
    "Couldn’t move Input History. It is still kept where it was." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when moving the entries to another vault (Keep Here) failed for any other reason. Nothing was moved."
    },
    "Couldn’t move the cards and addresses. Nothing was erased." : {
      "comment" : "Generic error text on the move-to-vault card in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when moving failed. Sentence case."
    },
    "Couldn’t open Input History. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Generic error under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when showing the entries failed for a reason not covered by the other messages. Try again is an instruction."
    },
    "Couldn’t read this file." : {
      "comment" : "Error text shown under the Import rows in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when the chosen Safari payment cards file cannot be read. Sentence case."
    },
    "Couldn’t save this login. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Generic failure message in the Save as Credential sheet (opened from an Input History entry) when the login could not be written to Credential Manager. A login is a website, username and password. Two short sentences."
    },
    "Couldn’t update website data" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the error alert on the Website data page in Settings › Privacy when removing or loading a website’s stored data failed. The message is the system’s error text. Sentence case."
    },
    "Country" : {
      "comment" : "Used twice: a row label on Address and Driver’s license items, and an entry of the type menu of a custom field (the value is a country). Sentence case. Noun."
    },
    "Create" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the Customize Theme sheet in Settings › Appearance: creates the custom copy of the built-in theme under the entered name. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Create a passkey for %@" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the macOS Touch ID or Mac password prompt that verifies the user right before WSurf saves a new passkey in Credential Manager. %@ is the website’s domain name (the relying party), such as example.com, and is never translated. A verb phrase, no final full stop."
    },
    "Create a passkey for %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the passkey creation sheet. %@ is the domain of the website that owns the passkey, such as example.com, and is never translated. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Create a passkey?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the first alert shown when a website asks to create a passkey, before WSurf unlocks or shows any account. The next line names the website. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Create a vault first: imports are saved into a vault, and there is nothing to export yet." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Import & Export section when the profile has no vault yet, so its buttons are off. Imperative with a colon; the rest gives the reason."
    },
    "Create a vault protected by a passkey to store passwords, passkeys and verification codes." : {
      "comment" : "Caption on the locked card when no vault exists yet; the card offers to create one. Imperative. Verification codes are one-time codes for two-step sign-in."
    },
    "Create Credential Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the locked Autofill page (Settings › Autofill) when no vault exists yet, and the heading of the sheet it opens, where the user names the new vault and chooses its unlock passkey. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Create Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the sheet titled “Create a passkey for %@?”, which appears when a website asks to create a passkey. It saves the new passkey in Credential Manager. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Create Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the Create Credential Vault sheet; it creates the new vault. Verb phrase, Title Case. Disabled until the name and the passkey choice are valid."
    },
    "Create Vault…" : {
      "comment" : "Button in both Import rows of Settings › Autofill (Vault tab), shown when no vault exists yet; it starts creating one. A verb phrase, Title Case; the ellipsis means a dialog follows. A vault is WSurf’s encrypted store for credentials."
    },
    "Created" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an SSH key item: the date the key was created. Short."
    },
    "Created %@" : {
      "comment" : "Date caption of a saved credential, in the list and in the editor. %@ is a formatted date (in the editor with the time). It may be followed by “ · Updated …”. Used only for credentials created in WSurf."
    },
    "Created %@ (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor. First %@ is the creation date and time, for example “Oct 24, 2026 at 3:14 PM”; second %@ is a relative phrase such as “yesterday”. Keep the parentheses."
    },
    "Created by" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an SSH key item: the source that generated the key. Short."
    },
    "Created in WSurf" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor, joined to the other facts by “ · ”: the passkey was created by WSurf. Sentence case."
    },
    "Creates a passkey in your passkey provider just for this vault." : {
      "comment" : "Detail text under the New passkey choice in the Create Credential Vault sheet. The passkey provider is the service that stores the user’s passkeys. The sentence describes the choice, so “Creates” is third person."
    },
    "Creation date unknown" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor, used when the passkey has no creation date. Sentence case."
    },
    "Credential" : {
      "comment" : "A noun: one entry in the vault. The kind label of a Trash row, and the fallback name shown for a credential with no name, website, username or item title, in rows, removal prompts and the import review."
    },
    "Credential added." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user saved a new credential in the editor; it offers Undo. Counterpart of “Changes saved.”. Full sentence."
    },
    "Credential Manager has no vault ready. Set one up in Credential Manager first." : {
      "comment" : "Result text in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History when there is no usable vault to save into. Credential Manager is the name of the settings area for logins. Sentence."
    },
    "Credential Manager is locked. You will unlock it, then choose an account." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the first passkey alert when the vault is locked. Credential Manager is WSurf’s name for its password and passkey vault. Full sentences; the button below it is “Unlock and Choose…”."
    },
    "Credential Manager locked before this was saved. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Result message in the Save as Credential sheet (opened from an Input History entry): Credential Manager’s vault locked before the password was saved, so nothing was written. Two short sentences."
    },
    "Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: how many credentials (logins) the vault holds. Also the section title of the credential list when the vault has no name, and a heading in the Merge Credentials sheet. Plural noun."
    },
    "Credentials are locked" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the card shown on the Vault tab of Settings › Autofill while the vault is locked and its content is hidden. A caption and an Unlock button follow. A state, Sentence case."
    },
    "Credentials are locked." : {
      "comment" : "Error or status line on the Credentials page in Settings when the credential vault is locked and the action needs it open. Full sentence."
    },
    "Credentials are unavailable" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the empty-state card on Settings › Autofill when the profile cannot keep a credential vault. The caption below it is “Private Browsing and removed profiles don’t keep a credential vault.” Sentence case."
    },
    "Credentials can’t be opened" : {
      "comment" : "Title, next to a warning icon, of the card that replaces the Autofill vault page when WSurf refuses to open the credential store for safety. An explanation of the cause follows. Sentence case."
    },
    "Credentials from another app" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a card on the Vault tab shown when another app has sent credentials that wait for review; its buttons are “Review…” and “Dismiss”. Sentence case."
    },
    "Credentials with different usernames can’t be merged." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown in the merge sheet of the Credentials page when the chosen credentials have different usernames. Full sentence."
    },
    "credentials without a website" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase plural noun phrase dropped into the VoiceOver label “Review merge of %@”. Not a sentence."
    },
    "Credentials you remove can be restored from here." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the empty state of the Trash section, under the title “Trash is empty”. Says what Trash is for: removed credentials can be put back from this list. Sentence."
    },
    "Current" : {
      "comment" : "Used in the History panel: the name of the current version in the version menu, and the label of the line with the credential’s current value while the editor has no unsaved changes. The label column is narrow."
    },
    "Current page: %@. Submitted requests stay in their original engine." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the toolbar’s site controls popover, shown when the tab’s loaded page uses a different engine than the one now chosen for the website. %@ is that engine (WebKit or Chromium, not translated). Sentence."
    },
    "Current — not saved" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the current-value line in the History panel when the editor has unsaved changes, so the value shown is the draft. The label column is about 104 points wide, so keep it short. Keep the dash."
    },
    "Custom fields" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. An item whose labelled fields the user defines. Plural noun."
    },
    "Customize" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Appearance › Theme whose button either edits the colors of a saved theme or saves an editable copy of a built-in one and opens its colors; also its Settings search result title. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Customize Theme" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet that asks for a name when the user customizes a built-in theme, which makes an editable copy; its default button is Create. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Customize…" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Customize row of Settings › Appearance › Theme, shown for a built-in theme: it opens a sheet to name an editable copy of the theme. One word, a verb; the ellipsis means a sheet follows."
    },
    "Date" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. A calendar date, which the field shows as YYYY-MM-DD. One word, a noun."
    },
    "Date of baptism" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a pre-made date field in the Identity template of the Credentials page (a person’s date of baptism, intended for a child’s records). Noun phrase, Sentence case."
    },
    "Date of birth" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On Driver’s license, Passport and ID document items. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Default vault" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Vaults section. On the right it says “This vault” if the selected vault is already the default, otherwise it has a Make Default button. Sentence case."
    },
    "Delete %@ permanently" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Delete… button on a row of the Trash list; the button opens the Delete Permanently? confirmation. %@ is the name of the removed item and should not be translated. A command, not shown on screen."
    },
    "Delete Now" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button in the marked-items bar of the Trash list, next to Undo: deletes the marked items permanently right away instead of when the user leaves Trash. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Delete Permanently" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the Delete Permanently? dialog when specific items were chosen (it reads Empty Trash when everything is emptied). Also the VoiceOver action name on a Trash row that deletes that item for good. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Delete Permanently?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown before removed items are deleted for good from Trash. The message below it says what is deleted and that it can’t be undone. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Delete Theme" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive confirm button of the dialog asking whether to delete a saved theme (the dialog title names the theme). A verb phrase, Title Case; the other button is Cancel."
    },
    "Delete Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the Delete Vault sheet, the first of two confirmations before a vault is deleted (the second is a system passkey prompt). Title Case. The sheet’s confirm button is “Delete Vault…”."
    },
    "Delete vault" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Vaults section; its button is Delete Vault…, and a caption under the title explains why deleting is not possible right now, when that applies. Sentence case."
    },
    "Delete Vault…" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button in the Delete Vault sheet that confirms deleting the vault (a system passkey prompt follows), and the button of the Delete vault row on the Vault tab that opens that sheet. A verb phrase, Title Case; the ellipsis means a further step follows."
    },
    "Deleted %lld items permanently." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after marked Trash items were permanently deleted. %lld is the number deleted, 2 or more; the singular is a separate entry."
    },
    "Deleted 1 item permanently." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after one marked Trash item was permanently deleted. Singular form; the plural is “Deleted %lld items permanently.”"
    },
    "Delete…" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button in the This theme row of Settings › Appearance › Theme and in the right-click menu of a saved theme: it asks to confirm before deleting the theme. Also the button on a Trash row in Credential Manager that deletes that item permanently after a confirmation. A verb."
    },
    "Derives the background, surface, and accent palette without changing website content." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Primary color row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Derives is a verb: a palette is calculated from this one color. The websites themselves are not changed."
    },
    "Deselect" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the VoiceOver action and context menu item that removes a credential row from the selection. Alternates with “Select”. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Deselect %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the checkbox at the start of a selected row in the credential list or Trash. %@ is the credential’s name, shown as typed and not translated. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Deselect All" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the bar above the credential list that clears the selection and leaves selection mode; it reads “Done” instead once Select started the mode. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Directly inside a folder." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Level 1 slider under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance."
    },
    "Discard Changes" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Discard Changes?” dialog in the credential editor: closes the editor and throws away the unsaved edits. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Discard Changes?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog that appears when the user cancels the credential editor sheet (Add Credential / Edit Credential) while it has unsaved edits. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "disconnect apps using this window" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “Stop External Connections” command in the command palette. Lowercase fragment, starts with a verb, no period."
    },
    "Disconnects every external app from this window." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button in the toolbar badge’s popover. Third person, present tense."
    },
    "Disconnects them from every tab in this window." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button in the popover of the “AI” badge on a tab. “Them” are the external apps that hold the tab. Third person, present tense."
    },
    "Dismiss Incoming Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the locked card that declines credentials another app is sending to WSurf; they can be sent again later. Verb phrase, Title Case. The paragraph above it calls the button “Dismiss”."
    },
    "Dock icon" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Dock icon section in Settings › Appearance, and of its entry in Settings search. It chooses the icon the macOS Dock shows while WSurf is running. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Document number" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an ID document item: the document’s number, hidden by default. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Don’t Record This Site" : {
      "comment" : "Item in an Input History entry’s “…” menu and context menu: adds the entry’s website to Excluded websites so nothing typed there is recorded. Title Case, a command with a negation. Existing entries stay."
    },
    "Driver’s license" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. A driving licence; use the local term and keep the curly apostrophe if the language has one."
    },
    "Duplicate" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the This theme row of Settings › Appearance › Theme, and an item of the right-click menu on a theme in the theme gallery: it makes a copy of the theme. A verb."
    },
    "Each entry is deleted when this time has passed." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “Keep entries for” menu in Input History. Sentence."
    },
    "Each group has the same login on the same sites. The extra copies move to Trash with their history. No website on another site is added." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Merge All Identical?” dialog. Trash is the vault’s Trash, and history means the earlier versions kept with each credential."
    },
    "Each vault has its own unlock passkeys and its own lock time. The default vault is the one autofill and saving use when they don’t need to ask. Credentials also lock when your Mac or its display sleeps, the screen locks, or you quit WSurf. A shorter lock time applies now; a longer one from the next unlock." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Vaults section. Lock time is the Lock credentials setting: how long a vault stays unlocked. The last sentence means a shorter lock time takes effect immediately and a longer one only after the next unlock."
    },
    "Earlier versions" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: how many earlier versions of credentials the vault keeps. Also a row in the Statistics section. Sentence case."
    },
    "Edit Colors" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Customize row of Settings › Appearance › Theme, shown for a saved theme: it opens the Colors section of the same page. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Edit Credential" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the credential editor sheet when an existing credential is open; Add Credential is the heading for a new one. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Edit Page" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app changes a page’s elements, attributes, text or styles, which needs Developer access. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Edit this theme’s base colors, text and accent under Colors." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Customize row in Settings › Appearance › Theme when the selected theme is one of the user’s own saved themes; its button is Edit Colors. “Colors” is the name of the Colors section lower on the same page. Sentence case."
    },
    "element %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in an Agent Activity line for a connected app’s tool call, naming the page element it acted on. %lld is the element’s reference number from the page read. Lowercase: it is joined to other fragments with “ · ” and never shown alone."
    },
    "Embedded in: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the passkey sheet, shown only when the request comes from a frame embedded in another site. %@ is the address of the outer website, never translated. Label before a colon."
    },
    "Empty Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the chip button with a crossed-out trash icon in the Trash section header; it deletes everything in Trash permanently after a confirmation. Also the destructive button of the Delete Permanently? dialog when everything is emptied. Verb phrase, Title Case, tight."
    },
    "Emulate Device" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app makes a page behave like a phone, a tablet or a responsive size. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Emulate Media" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app overrides how a page sees its environment: light or dark appearance, reduced motion, or being offline. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Ends their access to this tab only." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Take Over button in the popover of the “AI” badge. “Their” is the external app’s. Third person, present tense."
    },
    "Enter a valid setup key or otpauth:// link." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown under the setup key field in the credential editor when what was entered is not a valid key or link. Keep “otpauth://” as is. Sentence."
    },
    "Entries" : {
      "comment" : "Header of the section in Input History that lists the recorded entries (or the locked panel). Sentence case, a plural noun."
    },
    "Erase Old Copies" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive confirm button of the dialog asking whether to erase the copies of cards and addresses saved on this Mac. A verb phrase, Title Case; the other button is Cancel. The button that opens the dialog is “Erase Old Copies…”."
    },
    "Erase Old Copies…" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the card shown after cards and addresses were moved to the vault, in Settings › Autofill: it opens a confirmation dialog before erasing the old copies saved on this Mac. A verb phrase, Title Case; the ellipsis means a dialog follows."
    },
    "Erase the Copies Saved on This Mac?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) for erasing the old copies of cards and addresses that were saved on this Mac outside the vault, after they were moved into it. Title Case, a question; buttons are Erase Old Copies and Cancel."
    },
    "every field, with its label" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment shown after “Custom fields:” in the Export Credentials sheet: an item of the Custom fields kind sends all its fields together with their labels. Other kinds list their value names there instead."
    },
    "Every level below the second." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Level 3 and deeper slider under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Below the second means nested deeper than level 2."
    },
    "Everything it kept on this Mac is deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Message of two dialogs: “Turn off Input History?” and “Clear Input History?”. “It” is Input History. Says the recorded entries on this Mac are deleted. Sentence."
    },
    "Excluded sites" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: websites on which the user chose not to be offered to save logins (“Never for This Site”). Sentence case."
    },
    "Excluded websites" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Input History over a text box listing websites whose typing is never recorded. Sentence case, a noun phrase."
    },
    "Excluded websites (one per line)" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the multi-line text box in Input History where the person types the websites that are never recorded, one per line. Not shown on screen."
    },
    "Expires" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. Expiry date of a card, key or document. Used on Payment card, API key, SSH key, Driver’s license, Passport and ID document items. A verb form used as a label, short."
    },
    "Expires in %lld s" : {
      "comment" : "Caption beside a one-time verification code shown in the credential editor and in the credential list. %lld is the number of whole seconds before the code changes; “s” is the abbreviation for seconds. Very tight."
    },
    "Export Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the export sheet in Settings › Autofill when the user sends credentials to another app through the system; WSurf writes no file. Title Case. Sibling of “Export Passwords to CSV”."
    },
    "Export passwords to a CSV file" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Import & Export section; its button is Export to CSV…, which saves the passwords as an unencrypted CSV file. CSV stays untranslated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Export Passwords to CSV" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the export sheet in Settings › Autofill when the user exports passwords to a plain-text CSV file. Title Case. Sibling of “Export Credentials”."
    },
    "export saved cards, documents and hidden fields" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before saved cards, ID documents or hidden fields are exported. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passkeys" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passkeys (their private keys) to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passkeys, cards and documents" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passkeys (their private keys) and a saved card or ID document to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passkeys, passwords and verification codes" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passkeys (their private keys) and saved passwords or verification code setups to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passkeys, passwords, cards and documents" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passkeys (their private keys), saved passwords or verification codes, and a saved card or ID document to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passwords" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before Export to CSV… writes saved passwords to a file, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passwords and verification codes" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passwords or verification code setups to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "export saved passwords, cards and documents" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before an export hands saved passwords or verification codes, and a saved card or ID document, to another app, on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "Export to another app" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Import & Export section; its button is Export…, which hands credentials (passwords, passkeys, verification codes) to another app through the system’s credential exchange. Sentence case."
    },
    "Export to CSV…" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the Export passwords to a CSV file row; the ellipsis means a sheet to choose what to export follows. Verb phrase, Title Case. CSV stays untranslated."
    },
    "Exporting from the profile “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "Line under the title of the two export sheets, used when the vault’s name can’t be read. %@ is the name of the browser profile, chosen by the user; it should not be translated."
    },
    "Exporting from the vault “%@” of the profile “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "Line under the title of the two export sheets. First %@ is the vault’s name, second %@ is the browser profile’s name. Both are chosen by the user and should not be translated."
    },
    "Export…" : {
      "comment" : "Button that starts exporting credentials: in the Delete Vault sheet as a way to keep them first, in the Import & Export section of Settings › Autofill (the Export to another app row), and as the confirm button of the export sheet. A verb; the ellipsis means a dialog or file panel follows."
    },
    "External: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the Agent Activity panel over the actions an external app (such as Claude Code, connected by MCP) took on a tab. %@ is the app’s name, not translated. Short; external means from outside WSurf."
    },
    "Favorites" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the grid of favorite tabs at the top of the sidebar, small icon tiles. Plural noun, not shown on screen."
    },
    "Field" : {
      "comment" : "Fallback row label of a field in a Custom fields item whose label has not been filled in yet. Sentence case. One word, a noun."
    },
    "File missing" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a file’s name in the Files section of the credential editor, shown instead of its size when the encrypted file is not found in the vault’s folder on this Mac. Sentence case, tight."
    },
    "File moved or deleted" : {
      "comment" : "Short status under a finished download’s name in the small list over the Downloads button, shown instead of its size when the file is no longer where it was saved. Sentence case, tight."
    },
    "File Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list after the user saved a decrypted copy of a file attached to a credential. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Files" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor over the files attached to the credential. Also a section chip on the Vault tab and a row title in the History panel. Plural noun."
    },
    "Files from an earlier vault were found without the store that owns them." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: files of an earlier vault exist, but the store that should own them is not there. Sentence."
    },
    "Fill up to 32 text, select, date, color, range, checkbox, or radio controls without submitting." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Fill Multiple Fields tool in Settings › Assistant › Tools (On the Page group): the assistant can set several form controls in one step without sending the form. The control types are HTML form field kinds; 32 is the most it fills at once."
    },
    "fill your saved payment card" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user picks a saved payment card in the autofill dropdown. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "Find Elements" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app looks up elements in a page by CSS selector. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Find text you typed on websites, encrypted on this Mac. Off until you turn it on." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Input History” entry. It records what is typed on websites; it is off by default. Sentence fragments."
    },
    "Finder and Applications keep the standard icon. Only Default follows your Mac’s icon and widget style." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the Dock icon choices in Settings › Appearance. Finder, Applications and Default are names: Default is the first choice card, which follows the system’s icon style setting."
    },
    "Finish or cancel the open import first." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Delete vault row while a credential import review is still open, so deleting is unavailable. Imperative; “first” means before deleting."
    },
    "Folder color opacity" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: how strongly the color of sidebar folders is drawn. Sentence case."
    },
    "Folder indent" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, a heading above the Level 1, Level 2 and Level 3 and deeper sliders: how far tabs inside folders are shifted in. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Full name" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. Used on Payment card (name on the card), Driver’s license, Passport and ID document items. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Generate Password" : {
      "comment" : "Button under the password field in the credential editor that fills it with a new random password. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Glass" : {
      "comment" : "Option of the Material control in Settings › Appearance › Theme: the window shows your desktop through it. One word, a noun used as a style name; very tight space."
    },
    "Glass shows your desktop through the window. It uses more GPU." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Material row in Settings › Appearance › Theme, explaining the Glass choice of the Plain / Glass control. GPU is the graphics processor. Sentence case."
    },
    "Google blocks sign-in from embedded Chromium, so this page always opens in WebKit." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Browser engine row, with the menu disabled, for Google sign-in websites; in Settings › Websites and in the toolbar’s site controls popover. WebKit and Chromium are engine names, not translated. Sentence."
    },
    "Gruvbox" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a built-in color theme in Settings › Appearance. Proper name of a community palette; do not translate."
    },
    "Has parts not imported" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the import review sheet, with a count after it: items with a part that WSurf does not import. Sentence case."
    },
    "Hidden" : {
      "comment" : "In Input History’s Save as Credential sheet: VoiceOver label of the masked password dots. Also the name of a custom field type in the credential editor menu (Text, Hidden, Date, Number, Email): its value is concealed like a password. An adjective. Also the VoiceOver label of the masked verification code in the credential editor, before Show Code."
    },
    "Hidden network" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Wi-Fi network item: a yes/no value saying the network does not broadcast its name. Noun phrase, not a command."
    },
    "Hide" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the eye button beside a revealed hidden value of a card or other item in the credential editor; also a context menu item in Input History that hides a shown password. Alternates with “Show”. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Hide %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the eye button that masks a revealed value in a card or other item in the credential editor. %@ is the field’s name, such as “Card number”. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Hide Details" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row that holds a card or other item: hides the item’s values shown on the row. Counterpart of Show Details. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Hide History" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the bottom left of the credential editor sheet while the History panel is open beside the form; it closes the panel. Alternates with “View History”. History is the list of earlier versions of this credential. Title Case."
    },
    "Hide Password" : {
      "comment" : "Button beside each credential in the merge sheet that shows its password again hidden; also an item in a credential row’s ⋯ menu in the list. Alternates with “Show Password”. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Hide password of %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Hide Password button for one credential in the merge sheet. %@ is the credential’s name, shown as typed and not translated. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Hide Secrets" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the top right of the History panel, shown while secret values are revealed: it masks passwords, notes and card details again. Title Case, a command. Alternates with “Show Secrets”."
    },
    "Hide Side Panel (⌥⌘A)" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the toolbar button that toggles the side panel on the right (assistant activity or lyrics) while the panel is visible. ⌥⌘A is the keyboard shortcut and stays as it is. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Hide Username" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row whose username is hidden: hides the username again once it was shown. Counterpart of Show Username. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Hide username" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the eye button beside the Username field when the username is masked, in the credential editor; clicking it masks the name again. Alternates with “Show username”. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Hide Verification Code" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row that holds a verification code (a one-time code): hides the code shown on the row. Counterpart of Show Verification Code. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "History…" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row; it opens the credential’s earlier versions in the History panel. Title Case; the ellipsis means a panel opens."
    },
    "How much of a website the assistant may use when the website has no setting of its own." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Website access” entry in Settings › Assistant: the default access the assistant gets on websites. A sentence fragment, not a command."
    },
    "How strongly folder colors draw: folder icons, outlines and the icons a folder tints." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Folder color opacity row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. “Tints” is a verb: a folder can tint the icons of its tabs with its color."
    },
    "Hue" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance for a slider that shifts the derived colors around the color wheel. The color term (hue), a noun; Sentence case."
    },
    "Hue, primary color and brightness are applied on top of these colors, so what you see can differ from what you pick." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Colors card, shown while Hue, Primary color or Brightness is changed: the color pickers show the chosen colors before those adjustments, so the colors on screen can look different. Hue, Primary color and Brightness are the names of settings."
    },
    "Icons" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the color of toolbar and control icons. Sentence case; plural noun."
    },
    "Icons opacity" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the opacity slider beside the Icons color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "ID document" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. A national identity card or similar identity document."
    },
    "ID number" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. Used for two identification-number fields: the national identification number on a Passport item and the identification number on an ID document item. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Identities" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: entries that hold a person’s name or an identity document and have no sign-in or passkey. A plural noun; tight."
    },
    "Identity" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor for an identity, which is a person with no sign-in (a name, ID documents, custom fields). Also the name of that choice in the Add (+) menu at the top of the credential list. A noun."
    },
    "Idle" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of the toolbar badge and of the “AI” mark on a tab for an external app: it is connected but not running a command right now. Counterpart “Working”. A state adjective, not shown on screen."
    },
    "IDs" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: driver’s licenses, passports and other identity documents. Short for identity documents; very tight."
    },
    "If it is only part of Passwords, leave this off. WSurf can’t tell, so it keeps all of them." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the “No longer in Passwords” section, shown while the checkbox is off. “It” is the transfer, “them” the listed credentials. Passwords is Apple’s app. Sentences."
    },
    "Images, PDFs and any other files, up to %@ each and %lld per entry. They are encrypted in the vault and aren’t included when you export credentials to another app." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Files section of the credential editor. First %@ is the largest allowed size of one file, written by the system, for example “50 MB”; %lld is how many files one entry may hold. Files are left out when credentials are exported to another app."
    },
    "Import & Export" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the section on the Settings tab of Settings › Autofill for moving credentials in and out; it is also shown with disabled controls while the vault is locked. Title Case with an ampersand, two nouns."
    },
    "Import All as New" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of the “Suggested merges” group in the import review sheet: imports each item as a separate new credential instead of merging it. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Import All New" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of the New group heading in the import review sheet: imports every item of the group. New means not saved yet. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Import and export wait until WSurf knows whether a credential vault exists." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Import & Export section while WSurf has not yet found out whether a vault exists, so its buttons are off. Sentence."
    },
    "Import Anyway" : {
      "comment" : "Action for an item in the import review sheet’s Skipped group: imports it although it is left out by default. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Import as New" : {
      "comment" : "Action for one item in the import review sheet that duplicates a saved credential: imports it as a separate new credential instead of merging. Title Case, a command; may be a segment of a segmented control, so space is tight."
    },
    "Import contacts from Contacts" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Import & Export section of Settings › Autofill (Vault tab). The last “Contacts” is the name of the macOS Contacts app, so translate it as macOS does. Its button is Choose Contacts…. Sentence case."
    },
    "Import into the Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the review sheet that lists the payment cards or contacts about to be imported into the vault, with Cancel and Import buttons. Title Case."
    },
    "Import passwords from a CSV file" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Import & Export section; its button is Choose File…, which opens a file chooser. CSV (a comma-separated values file) stays untranslated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Import payment cards from a Safari export" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Import & Export section of Settings › Autofill (Vault tab); its button is Choose File…. Safari is the Apple browser and is not translated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Imported" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor, joined to the other facts by “ · ”: the passkey was brought in from another app. Sentence case; an adjective, not a command."
    },
    "Imported %@" : {
      "comment" : "Date caption of a saved credential that was imported from another app or a file, in the list and the editor. %@ is a formatted date, with the time in the editor."
    },
    "Imported into WSurf: %lld added, %lld updated, %lld moved to Trash. Nothing was changed in the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Success message after an import from another app (normally Apple’s Passwords), used when some credentials were also moved to Trash. In order, the %lld values are the number added, the number updated and the number moved to the vault’s Trash. “The other app” is the app that sent them."
    },
    "Imported into WSurf: %lld added, %lld updated. Nothing was changed in the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Success message in the “Transfer finished” section of Settings › Credentials after credentials sent by another app (normally Apple’s Passwords) were imported. First %lld is how many credentials were added, second %lld how many existing ones were updated. “The other app” is the app that sent them."
    },
    "Importing into the profile “%@”. Nothing is saved until you choose Import. Imported passwords, passkeys, verification codes and notes are encrypted in that profile’s vault." : {
      "comment" : "Text under the “Review Import” headline. %@ is the name of the browser profile that receives the credentials; do not translate it. A vault is that profile’s encrypted store, and Import is the sheet’s button."
    },
    "Importing into the vault “%@” of the profile “%@”. Nothing is saved until you choose Import. Imported passwords, passkeys, verification codes and notes are encrypted in that vault." : {
      "comment" : "Text under the “Review Import” headline. First %@ is the vault’s name, second %@ the browser profile’s name; do not translate them. A vault is the profile’s encrypted store, and Import is the sheet’s button."
    },
    "Imports %lld new, updates %lld, leaves %lld unchanged, skips %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the import review sheet. In order, the counts are items imported as new, items updated or merged, items left unchanged, and items skipped. Verbs describe what Import will do."
    },
    "In the current credential" : {
      "comment" : "Small caption beside a note of the earlier version in the History panel, shown instead of the Add button when the same note is already in the current credential. Sentence case."
    },
    "In Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Statistics section; the number on the right is how many removed items are in the vault’s Trash right now (a dash while unknown). Use the same word for Trash as on the Trash tab of the credentials list. Sentence case."
    },
    "Input History" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the feature that keeps text the user typed on websites, encrypted on this Mac. Chip on the Vault tab, Settings search result and page title, and tooltip and VoiceOver label of the toolbar icon that opens it. Title Case."
    },
    "Input History couldn’t be opened, so it was cleared." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when the stored entries could not be opened (their keys are unusable), so WSurf deleted them. Input History is the feature that remembers text typed on websites."
    },
    "Input History entries" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet, shown only when the vault holds some. Input History is a feature of the Autofill page (a name, so translate it consistently with the rest of the UI). Sentence case."
    },
    "Input History is kept in a vault that is locked. Unlock that vault with the vault picker, then show the entries: Touch ID or your Mac password is asked for next." : {
      "comment" : "Message under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when Show Entries was pressed but the vault keeping the entries is locked. The vault picker is the selector at the top of the Autofill page’s Vault tab. The colon introduces what happens next."
    },
    "Input History is kept with this vault, so what it recorded is deleted too." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Delete Vault sheet, shown only when the vault holds Input History entries. Input History is the name of a feature of the Autofill page. Sentence case."
    },
    "Input History is locked" : {
      "comment" : "Headline of the locked panel of the Entries section in Input History; entries stay encrypted until the person asks to see them. Sentence case, a state."
    },
    "Input History is now kept in %@." : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation note under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill after the Keep Here button moved the entries to another vault. %@ is the name of that vault, chosen by the user, and is not translated."
    },
    "Input History was cleared because the vault it was kept with was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Message under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill: its entries were deleted because the vault that kept them was deleted. Also shown if that happens while moving the entries to another vault."
    },
    "Inside a folder that is inside a folder." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Level 2 slider under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance."
    },
    "Inspect Element" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app inspects one page element: its attributes, geometry, box model and styles. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Also the last item of a Chromium page’s context menu when the Web Inspector is on, which opens Chromium’s DevTools on the clicked element (WebKit supplies its own). Title Case; a verb phrase, singular."
    },
    "Issued" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. The date a document was issued, on Driver’s license, Passport and ID document items. Short."
    },
    "Issued by" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. The authority that issued a document, on Driver’s license, Passport and ID document items. Short."
    },
    "Issuing country" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On Passport and ID document items: the country that issued the document. Noun phrase."
    },
    "It can’t be undone, and you’ll confirm with an unlock passkey." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the Delete Permanently? dialog message, after the one saying what is deleted. The unlock passkey is the passkey that unlocks the vault; it is asked for again to authorize the deletion."
    },
    "it contains the username or the website’s name" : {
      "comment" : "A reason in the note “The saved password is weak: %@.” in the credential editor: the password holds the credential’s username or the name of its website. A lowercase clause with no period; it can be joined with other reasons into a list."
    },
    "It has more than %lld cards and other items. Only the first %lld were imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: an item held more cards and other items (addresses, IDs, custom fields…) than WSurf keeps. Both %lld are the same number: the maximum number per item. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentences."
    },
    "It has more than %lld websites. Only the first %lld were imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: an item listed more websites than WSurf keeps, so only the first ones were kept. Both %lld are the same number: the maximum number of websites per item. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentences."
    },
    "It has more than one login. Only the first was imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: an item held several logins and only the first was kept. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentences."
    },
    "It has more than one verification code. Only the first was imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: an item held several verification codes (one-time codes) and only the first was kept. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentences."
    },
    "It has nothing WSurf can store yet, so it wasn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: the whole item was skipped because it held nothing WSurf can store. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentence."
    },
    "it is only digits, or letters of one case" : {
      "comment" : "A reason in the note “The saved password is weak: %@.” in the credential editor: the password, under 12 characters, is all digits, all lowercase or all uppercase letters. A lowercase clause with no period; it can be joined with other reasons into a list."
    },
    "it was cancelled" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment with no period; it must read correctly after “because”."
    },
    "it was no longer open" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period; the import review was no longer open or no longer belonged to this window."
    },
    "Items in Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: how many items sit in the vault’s Trash. Sentence case."
    },
    "Its brightness, transparency, spacing, folder indent and layout go back to how WSurf ships them. You can’t undo this." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Reset theme confirmation dialog for a theme with no original to go back to. “Its” refers to the theme named in the dialog title; “folder indent” is how far folders are indented in the sidebar. Sentence case."
    },
    "its collections are nested more than %@ levels deep" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of nesting levels of collections (groups inside groups)."
    },
    "Its colors, brightness, transparency, spacing, folder indent and layout go back to “%@”, the theme it was made from. You can’t undo this." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Reset theme confirmation dialog for a saved theme. %@ is the name of the theme it was made from (a name, not to be translated). “Its” refers to the theme named in the dialog title. Sentence case."
    },
    "Its credential files can’t be read right now, so they may contain recoverable items. They are erased with it and WSurf can’t undo this." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the confirmation for deleting a profile when its credential vault files cannot be read to count what they hold. It says they may still contain recoverable items and will be erased with the profile, which cannot be undone."
    },
    "Its credential vaults, with their Trash and earlier versions, are erased with it and WSurf can’t undo this: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the confirmation for deleting a profile: its credential vaults, with Trash and earlier versions, are erased with it and cannot be restored. %@ is a semicolon-separated list of per-vault facts (see the two entries before this one) and ends with a period added by this sentence."
    },
    "Keep" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the per-credential menu in the “No longer in Passwords” list (the other item is “Move to Trash”), and the menu’s label showing the current choice. A verb: the credential stays in WSurf."
    },
    "Keep All" : {
      "comment" : "Small button in the “No longer in Passwords” section, shown when the checkbox is on: keeps every listed credential in WSurf. Title Case, a command. Sibling of “Move All to Trash”."
    },
    "Keep All Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of an import review group heading: for every item of the group, keeps the version that is already saved. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Keep All Unchanged" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of the “Already saved” group in the import review sheet: leaves every item as it is saved. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Keep Both" : {
      "comment" : "Action for an item on the import review sheet that conflicts with a saved credential: keeps the saved version and also adds the other app’s version next to it. Title Case, a command; may be a segment, so space is tight."
    },
    "Keep Editing" : {
      "comment" : "Cancel-style button of the “Discard Changes?” dialog in the credential editor: closes the dialog and returns to the editor. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Keep entries for" : {
      "comment" : "Row title of the menu in Input History that sets how long recorded entries are kept. Sentence case, a label before a choice such as “30 minutes”."
    },
    "Keep everything you type until you delete it?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert shown when the person picks “Until I delete” as the time entries are kept in Input History. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Keep Here" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the row “Keep Input History in this vault”: moves the kept entries into the vault shown in the picker. Title Case, a verb phrase, short."
    },
    "Keep Input History in %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the “Keep Here” button in Input History. %@ is the vault’s name (not translated). Not shown on screen. Title Case."
    },
    "Keep Input History in this vault" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a vault’s row in the Input History settings (Settings › Autofill, Vault tab) while Input History is not kept in that vault; the row’s button is “Keep Here”. Once it is kept there the title reads “Kept in this vault”. Sentence case."
    },
    "Keep Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Action for one item on the import review sheet (menu item or segment), and the row menu’s label once chosen: keeps the version that is already saved. Title Case, a command; the opposite of “Use Incoming”."
    },
    "Keep Until I Delete" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the alert “Keep everything you type until you delete it?”; confirms entries never expire. Title Case twin of the menu choice “Until I delete”."
    },
    "Keeps what you type on websites, including passwords, encrypted on this Mac for the time you choose. Opening it needs the vault that keeps it unlocked, then Touch ID or your Mac password; without a vault, Touch ID or your Mac password alone. Private windows are never recorded." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “Remember what I type” switch of Input History. “It” is the recorded history; “opening it” means showing the entries. A vault is the encrypted store for logins and passkeys. Touch ID is the Apple name."
    },
    "Kept from a merged credential" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for a password or verification code that a merge kept in this credential’s History, taken from a credential that was merged away. Sentence case."
    },
    "Kept in %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the checkmark icon in the “Kept in this vault” row of Input History. %@ is the vault’s name (not translated). Not shown on screen."
    },
    "Kept in %@. Moving it needs both vaults unlocked. No entry is lost or encrypted again." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the row “Keep Input History in this vault” when Input History is kept in a different vault. %@ is that vault’s name, or the phrase “another vault”. “It” is Input History. Sentence."
    },
    "Kept in this vault" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Input History when the vault shown by the page’s vault picker already keeps the entries; a checkmark replaces the button. Sentence case, a state."
    },
    "Key" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an API key item: the key itself, a secret hidden by default. A noun, one word; not a keyboard key and not a verb."
    },
    "Key type" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On API key and SSH key items: the type of the key. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Label" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the small text field that names each custom field in the credential editor. Noun, sentence case, tight."
    },
    "Last local signature %@" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor. %@ is the date and time of the last signature made with this passkey on this Mac. Sentence case."
    },
    "Leave" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the Leave page? / Reload page? sheet: goes ahead and leaves or reloads the page. One word, a verb; the other button is Stay."
    },
    "Leave page?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet shown by a Chromium tab when the page asks for confirmation before the user navigates away from it or closes it. The page’s own message appears below it; buttons are Leave and Stay. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Left by an upgrade that was interrupted before it finished." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a file path in the “Credentials can’t be opened” card: this file is a leftover of a vault upgrade that did not finish. Sentence."
    },
    "Let “%@” answer a prompt on %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the dialog asking whether an external connection (a connected app) may answer a prompt on a webpage. The first %@ is the app’s name, the second is the website’s host name; neither should be translated. Keep the curly quotes."
    },
    "Let “%@” answer a prompt?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the same dialog when the website is not known. %@ is the connected app’s name (or “An external connection”) and should not be translated. Keep the curly quotes."
    },
    "Lets you take over this tab or stop the app." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the “AI” badge on a sidebar tab; pressing it opens a popover with Take Over and Stop buttons. “The app” is the external app using the tab."
    },
    "Level 1" : {
      "comment" : "Slider row title under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance: the indent for items directly inside a folder. Level is a nesting depth; keep the number."
    },
    "Level 2" : {
      "comment" : "Slider row title under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance: the indent for items inside a folder that is itself inside a folder. Level is a nesting depth; keep the number."
    },
    "Level 3 and deeper" : {
      "comment" : "Slider row title under Folder indent in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance: the indent used at the third folder level and every level below it. Level is a nesting depth; keep the number."
    },
    "License class" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Driver’s license item: the licence class or category. Noun phrase."
    },
    "License number" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Driver’s license item: the licence number, hidden by default. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Line" : {
      "comment" : "Label before a line number, in a list of notes about a CSV file: “Line 12: …”. A noun; the number and the note are added by the app."
    },
    "Line %lld of the file" : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the details of one part of an import review row that came from a CSV file. %lld is the line number in the file."
    },
    "Load Older Versions…" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the bottom of the version menu in the History panel, shown only when more earlier versions exist; it loads the next batch. Title Case, a command; the ellipsis stays."
    },
    "Loaded" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of a favorite tile in the sidebar: its page is loaded in memory. Counterpart “Unloaded”. Spoken after the tab’s title; not shown on screen."
    },
    "Lock" : {
      "comment" : "Small button with a lock icon in the Input History section: locks the vault (or Input History) so it must be unlocked again. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Lock Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the padlock button, which has no text, on the Vault tab and in the Trash header of Settings › Autofill: locks the credential vault so it must be unlocked again. Title Case, a command; Credentials is the feature’s name."
    },
    "Lock credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Vaults section; its pop-up menu sets how long the selected vault stays unlocked (After 1 minute … When WSurf quits). Sentence case; Lock is a verb."
    },
    "Locked vaults are listed by number. The name appears after you unlock." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Name row of the selected vault, shown while it is locked (the name field is disabled). A locked vault is listed as “Vault 1”, “Vault 2” and so on until it is unlocked."
    },
    "Login details changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the login differs in something other than its username or password, such as how the other app described its fields. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Logins" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: credentials that hold a login (username and password). Also a row title with a count in the Statistics section. A plural noun; tight."
    },
    "Logins, passkeys, identities, cards, addresses, notes and other items in an encrypted vault." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description (tooltip of the result, also matched by the query) for the “Vault” entry, the Autofill tab for saved logins and other items. A vault is an encrypted store. A list of item types. Sentence."
    },
    "Low contrast: %@:1 on the sidebar color. Aim for 4.5:1 or more." : {
      "comment" : "Warning under a text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance when it reads poorly on the sidebar color. %@ is the measured contrast ratio as a number with one decimal, such as 3.2, followed by the literal :1. Keep 4.5:1 as is."
    },
    "Low contrast: %@:1 on the surface color. Aim for 4.5:1 or more." : {
      "comment" : "Warning under a text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance when it reads poorly on the surface color. %@ is the measured contrast ratio as a number with one decimal, such as 3.2, followed by the literal :1. Keep 4.5:1 as is."
    },
    "Low contrast: %@:1 on the window color. Aim for 4.5:1 or more." : {
      "comment" : "Warning under a text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance when it reads poorly on the window background. %@ is the measured contrast ratio as a number with one decimal, such as 3.2, followed by the literal :1. Keep 4.5:1 as is."
    },
    "Make Default" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the Default vault row that makes the selected vault the default one, used by autofill and saving. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Make this theme’s light or dark colors darker or lighter." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Brightness” entry in Settings › Appearance (a slider). Imperative."
    },
    "Makes this theme’s dark colors darker or lighter." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Brightness row in Settings › Appearance › Theme while the dark appearance is shown; the light appearance shows the same sentence with “light colors”. Sentence case."
    },
    "Makes this theme’s light colors darker or lighter." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Brightness row in Settings › Appearance › Theme while the light appearance is shown; the dark appearance shows the same sentence with “dark colors”. Sentence case."
    },
    "Material" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Appearance › Theme for the choice between the Plain and Glass window looks; also the title of its Settings search result. A noun."
    },
    "Medical" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a pre-made text field in the Identity template of the Credentials page, meant for medical notes. Adjective used as a noun label. Sentence case."
    },
    "Merge" : {
      "comment" : "Confirm button of the “Merge Credentials?” dialog. Also the label of an import review menu, where it shows the chosen way to bring in an item: merge it into a saved credential. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Merge %@ Groups" : {
      "comment" : "Confirming button of the “Merge All Identical?” dialog. %@ is the number of groups. Title Case, a command; the plural of group."
    },
    "Merge %lld credentials" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Merge… button in the bar above the credential list; not shown on screen. %lld is the number of selected credentials. A command."
    },
    "Merge All Identical (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the bottom of the Suggested Merges sheet: merges every group of identical credentials after a confirmation. %@ is the number of such groups. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Merge All Identical?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog opened by “Merge All Identical (n)”. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Merge All Suggested" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of the “Suggested merges” group in the import review sheet: merges each item into the saved credential that already holds its login or passkey. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Merge Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the sheet for merging several credentials into one, opened from Merge… in the credential list. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Merge Credentials?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown after Merge… is clicked in the merge sheet. Its message names which credentials move to Trash. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Merge into “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Action for one item on the import review sheet, in the row’s menu or as a segment: adds what the item brings to the saved credential named in the quotes and links the two. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Merge Into…" : {
      "comment" : "Menu item on an import review row, or in the menu of one of its parts: opens a list of saved credentials to merge into. Also the headline of that list. Title Case, a command; the ellipsis means more input follows."
    },
    "Merge Selected Credentials…" : {
      "comment" : "Right-click menu item on a credential row when several rows are selected: opens the Merge Credentials sheet to combine them into one. Verb phrase, Title Case; for a single row the item is “Merge…”."
    },
    "Merged %@ groups. %@ credentials moved to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the Suggested Merges sheet after Merge All Identical. First %@ is the number of groups merged, second %@ the number of extra credentials moved to Trash."
    },
    "Merged %lld credentials." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user merged the chosen credentials into one; it offers Undo. %lld is the number of credentials that were merged, always 2 or more."
    },
    "Merged %lld groups of identical credentials." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user merged every group of identical credentials at once; it offers Undo. %lld is the number of groups merged, each into one credential."
    },
    "Merged into a saved credential." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row that is set to be merged into a saved credential. Short fallback wording used when no further details are shown."
    },
    "Merged into “%@” before, so it isn’t imported unless you choose to." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of a skipped import review row: in an earlier import it was merged into a saved credential, so it is left out unless the user chooses Import Anyway. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Merged into “%@” before." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the status line of an import review row: in an earlier import this item was merged into a saved credential. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated. Other sentences may follow."
    },
    "Merged with another credential" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: in WSurf, this credential was merged with another credential. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Merge…" : {
      "comment" : "Button that combines the selected credentials into one: in the bar above the credential list, in a row’s More actions menu, and as the confirm button of the Merge Credentials sheet. A verb; the ellipsis means a review or confirmation follows."
    },
    "Merging adds %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row that matches a saved credential. %@ is a list joined with “and” of fragments such as “a website and a passkey”."
    },
    "Merging only links the two." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row that matches a saved credential: merging adds nothing, it only records that the item and the saved credential are the same one."
    },
    "Middle name" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Name item. Noun."
    },
    "Mono" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the Mono choice card in Settings › Appearance › Dock icon, next to Default, Light and Dark: a monochrome version of the app icon. Short for monochrome; Title Case; very tight."
    },
    "Monochrome" : {
      "comment" : "Option in the Tab icons segmented control in Settings › Appearance › Layout, opposite Color: website icons are drawn in a single color. Sentence case; tight."
    },
    "Month and year" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. A month and a year, like a card’s expiry date."
    },
    "More Actions" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the round “…” menu button on each Input History entry. The menu holds Save as Credential…, Don’t Record This Site and Delete. Title Case, plural noun phrase."
    },
    "More actions for %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the circled-ellipsis menu button on a credential row, whose menu has copy, show or hide, History and Merge items. %@ is the credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "More in Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Row title at the end of the Trash list when only the first part of Trash is listed. Its caption is “Showing %lld of %lld” and its button is “Show More”. Sentence case."
    },
    "More sites where this credential fills, one per line." : {
      "comment" : "Caption inside the “Other HTTPS origins” group of the credential editor. Sentence."
    },
    "More than one saved login matches this username. Change the right one in Credential Manager." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History, as caption and as result text, when several saved logins match the username so WSurf will not pick one. Credential Manager is the name of the settings area for logins."
    },
    "Move %@ to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Remove button on a credential row (its tooltip is “Move to Trash”). %@ is the credential’s title and should not be translated. A command, not shown on screen."
    },
    "Move %lld credentials to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Move to Trash button in the bar above the credential list; not shown on screen. %lld is the number of selected credentials. A command."
    },
    "Move All to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Small button in the “No longer in Passwords” section, shown when the checkbox is on: chooses to move every listed credential to Trash when the import runs. Title Case, a command. Sibling of “Keep All”."
    },
    "Move Selected Credentials to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive right-click menu item on a credential row when several rows are selected: moves all of them to Trash without a dialog (Undo is offered). For a single row the item is “Move to Trash”. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Move them into this vault, where autofill fills them from. Nothing is read until you choose Review." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Cards and addresses saved on this Mac row in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) before anything was moved. “Them” are the cards and addresses; Review is the name of that row’s button (Review…). Sentence case."
    },
    "Move to the Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Section title in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) listing the cards and addresses about to be moved from their old copies into the vault, with Cancel and Move to Vault buttons below. Title Case."
    },
    "Move to Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Prominent button of the Move to the Vault section in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab): it writes the listed cards and addresses into the selected vault. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Moved %lld credentials to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user moved several credentials from the list to Trash; it offers Undo. %lld is the number moved, 2 or more; the singular is a separate entry."
    },
    "Moved 1 credential to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user moved a credential from the list to Trash; it offers Undo. Singular form; the plural is “Moved %lld credentials to Trash.”"
    },
    "Moved from the cards and addresses saved on this Mac" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for a change made when the payment cards and addresses saved on this Mac were moved into the vault (Settings › Autofill), or when that move was undone. Sentence case."
    },
    "Moved to WSurf %@" : {
      "comment" : "Date caption of a saved credential that was moved into WSurf’s credential vault from earlier storage instead of being created there, in the list and the editor. %@ is a formatted date, with the time in the editor."
    },
    "Moves %lld to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the import review footer. %lld is the number of saved credentials the other app no longer holds that the user chose to move to Trash."
    },
    "Moves the tabs and folders inside an open folder in. Each level of folders takes its own step, and the steps add up." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Folder indent row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Moves … in means shifts them inward (toward the right in left-to-right languages); in is an adverb here. Folders can be nested, and a level is a nesting depth."
    },
    "Moving Input History needs both vaults unlocked: the one that keeps it now and %@. Unlock them with the vault picker, then try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error under the Input History list in Settings > Autofill when Keep Here was pressed while a vault was locked. %@ is the name of the vault the entries should move to (user-chosen, not translated). The vault picker is the selector at the top of the Autofill page’s Vault tab."
    },
    "name" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase noun, never shown alone: inserted into “Copy this version’s %@” and “Copy the current %@”, the tooltips and VoiceOver labels of copy buttons in the History panel. Here it is the credential’s name."
    },
    "Name Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies a credential’s name to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Name or websites" : {
      "comment" : "Name of one kind of change in the History panel of a credential’s editor: its name or its list of websites changed. Shown inside the “Until %@ · %@” version menu item, joined with other change names by commas. Sentence case."
    },
    "Nationality" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On Passport and ID document items. Noun."
    },
    "Needs your decision" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a group of items in the import review sheet (Settings › Autofill › Vault): items where a part conflicts with a saved credential and only the user can settle it. Also that group’s filter chip, with a count after it. Sentence case."
    },
    "Needs your decision: %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the import review footer. %lld is the number of items still waiting for a decision; same wording as the group heading “Needs your decision”."
    },
    "Network name" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Wi-Fi network item: the network’s name (its SSID). Noun phrase."
    },
    "New account%@" : {
      "comment" : "First entry of the account pop-up menu in the create-passkey sheet, which makes a new account for the passkey. %@ is empty, or a space followed by the requested user name in curly quotes, such as “jane”; keep it at the end. Sentence case."
    },
    "New passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the first choice in the Create Credential Vault sheet: protect the new vault with a newly created passkey. The second choice is “Use existing passkey”. Sentence case; a noun phrase, not a command."
    },
    "New Vault" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the chip button with a plus icon in the Vaults section header; it opens the Create Credential Vault sheet. Verb phrase (a command), Title Case, tight."
    },
    "Nickname" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Name item: an informal given name. Noun."
    },
    "No approved website" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under a saved credential in the “Merge Into…” sheet when it has no website approved for autofill. Sentence case."
    },
    "No credential vault exists for this profile yet. Create one to continue." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when no vault exists yet for the current profile. The second sentence tells the user to create one. Full sentences."
    },
    "No credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the empty state of the Vault tab’s list when the vault holds nothing. Sentence case."
    },
    "No earlier versions are kept." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the History panel beside a credential’s editor when the credential has no earlier versions yet. Sentence."
    },
    "No local signature recorded" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor, used when this Mac has never recorded a signature made with the passkey. Sentence case."
    },
    "No longer in Passwords" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a collapsible section in the import review sheet, followed by a count: credentials an earlier import brought in that this transfer doesn’t contain. Passwords is Apple’s app. Also the VoiceOver label of its toggle. Sentence case."
    },
    "No longer in the vault" : {
      "comment" : "Label before a colon and a comma-separated list of credential names, in the same notice: the selected credentials that no longer exist in the vault. The colon is added by the app. Sentence case."
    },
    "No saved credential can take this." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the “Merge Into…” sheet when no saved credential can receive the part being merged."
    },
    "No saved password" : {
      "comment" : "Detail text on a row of the autofill dropdown for a saved login that has no password stored. It is shown with other short details separated by middle dots. Sentence case, no period."
    },
    "No suggested merges" : {
      "comment" : "Empty state of the Suggested Merges sheet when the vault has no suggestion. Sentence case."
    },
    "No unlocked vault has this login, and another vault is locked and may hold it." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Which vault?” alert when no unlocked vault has the login but a locked vault might. A login is the username and password saved for a website. Full sentence."
    },
    "No weak or reused passwords" : {
      "comment" : "Shown above the credential list in Settings › Credentials, in place of the Show Password Health button, when the check found no weak password and no password saved for more than one website. No period."
    },
    "No website" : {
      "comment" : "Word in the merge sheet’s Before and After lines for a credential that has no websites. Sentence case, a fragment."
    },
    "No website · %@" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of credentials without a website in the By Site list. %@ is the number of credentials in the group. Keep the “·” separator."
    },
    "None puts the page against the window and the sidebar." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Page spacing row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. None is the slider’s label at zero, so no gap is left between the page and the window or sidebar."
    },
    "Not added, as they are on other sites: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row: the item’s websites that a merge leaves out because they belong to other sites than the saved credential’s. %@ is a comma-separated list of website hostnames."
    },
    "Not imported" : {
      "comment" : "Bold heading of a short list in the import review sheet: parts of the received data that WSurf does not import and that belong to no row. Sentence case."
    },
    "not imported: same as line %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that is skipped because an earlier row has the same website, username and password; shown after “Line N:”. %lld is the line number of that earlier row. Lowercase fragment."
    },
    "not imported: the password is too long." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that is skipped, shown after “Line N:” or “Entry N:”. Lowercase fragment. The row’s password exceeds the size limit."
    },
    "not imported: the row can’t be saved." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that is skipped, shown after “Line N:” or “Entry N:”. Lowercase fragment. The row’s values are not valid for a saved login."
    },
    "not imported: the row doesn’t match the header." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that is skipped, shown after “Line N:”. Lowercase fragment. The row has a different number of columns than the file’s header line."
    },
    "not imported: the website is missing or isn’t a secure https address." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review for one row of a CSV file (or entry of the old Passwords list), shown after “Line N:” or “Entry N:”, saying why it is skipped. Lowercase fragment that continues that prefix. Row is skipped because its website is empty or is not an https address."
    },
    "not imported: there is no password." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that is skipped, shown after “Line N:” or “Entry N:”. Lowercase fragment. The row has no password."
    },
    "Not in the current credential" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of a minus icon in the History panel next to a website or file of the earlier version that the current credential no longer has. Sentence case."
    },
    "Not kept in a vault yet: your default vault keeps it the first time you show the entries. Keeping it here needs this vault unlocked." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the row “Keep Input History in this vault” when no vault keeps Input History yet. “It” is Input History; “here” is the vault shown in the picker above. Sentence."
    },
    "Not saved yet." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row for a new item: nothing is saved for it yet; Import will save it."
    },
    "Note %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of one note’s text editor in the credential editor. %lld is the note’s position, starting at 1. Sentence case."
    },
    "Note Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies a note of a credential to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "notes" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment in an account’s line in the passkey account chooser, saying the account also has notes. Joined with other fragments such as “password” by a middle dot, so keep it short and lowercase. Plural noun, not a verb."
    },
    "Notes removed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: notes were removed in WSurf after an earlier import, and the removal is kept. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Notes: %lld → %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Line under “Also kept” in the merge sheet. First %lld is how many notes the primary credential has now, second %lld how many the merged one will have. Keep the arrow. Fragment."
    },
    "Nothing changes until you choose Save." : {
      "comment" : "Small note at the bottom of the History panel. Use This and Add only copy a value into the editor; Save is the editor’s Save button. Sentence."
    },
    "Nothing in this vault matches your search or filter." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the “No matches” empty state on the Vault tab, shown when the search or a kind filter leaves nothing."
    },
    "Nothing recorded yet" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the empty state of the Entries section in Input History, in two cases: recording is on but nothing was captured, or recording is off. Sentence case."
    },
    "Nothing typed on these websites or their subdomains is recorded. One per line." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Excluded websites text box in Input History. The person types one website per line. Sentence."
    },
    "Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused; it says the vault was left as it was. It follows “This can’t be restored right now.” and a reason sentence in the same paragraph."
    },
    "Nothing was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list when leaving Trash did not delete the marked items, for example because the passkey or Touch ID check was declined or failed. Full sentence."
    },
    "Nothing was imported." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials after an import in which every incoming item was skipped or was already identical to what the vault holds. A short full sentence."
    },
    "Nothing was merged." : {
      "comment" : "Message in the Suggested Merges sheet after Merge All Identical when no group was merged."
    },
    "Notice" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the last row in the “Passkeys not confirmed with the website” section; its only control is the Dismiss button. A noun."
    },
    "Number" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. A number. One word, a noun."
    },
    "Numbered copies of one username" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: same website and one username with copy numbers, such as “name (1)”, as exports name duplicates. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Numbered copies with the same password" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: copies numbered like “name (1)” that hold the same password. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "OIB" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a pre-made hidden field in the Identity template of the Credentials page: the Croatian personal identification number (OIB). Keep the acronym if the local term is the same; it is a name, not an abbreviation of English words."
    },
    "On %lld credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Plural of “On 1 credential”: caption under the Passkeys row in the Statistics section, shown when some credentials hold several passkeys. %lld is the number of credentials that hold at least one passkey (always 2 or more here). Sentence case."
    },
    "On 1 credential" : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Passkeys row in the Statistics section of Settings › Autofill (Settings tab), shown when one credential holds several passkeys: all the passkeys counted above sit on a single credential. Singular; the plural is “On %lld credentials”. Sentence case."
    },
    "One HTTPS address per line. Passwords and codes fill only on these websites. Command-click an address to open it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the websites field in the credential editor. Passwords and verification codes are filled only on the listed websites; Command is the Mac modifier key; use the name the Mac gives that key. Sentence."
    },
    "Only in the current credential" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of a plus icon in the History panel next to a website the credential has now but the earlier version did not. Sentence case."
    },
    "Opacity %@" : {
      "comment" : "Value shown to the right of an opacity slider in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. %@ is the opacity already formatted as a percentage, such as 85%. Noun; fixed narrow width, so keep it short."
    },
    "Open Comparison" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app opens one page in WebKit and in Chromium, side by side in a split, to compare them. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. WebKit and Chromium are engine names. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Open in Another App?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the dialog that follows Open With… on an attached file in the credential editor; its buttons are the apps that can open the file. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Open Input History in WSurf." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the macOS Touch ID or Mac password prompt that appears when the user shows the entries of Input History (Settings > Autofill > Vault tab). Input History is the feature that remembers text typed on websites. A full sentence; WSurf is the app’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "Open Website" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver action on a credential row, and an item of its right-click menu: opens the credential’s website in a new tab. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Open Website in a New Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the arrow button beside the Websites caption in the credential editor, whose menu lists the saved addresses to open; also the tooltip of the arrow button on each credential row in the list. Opens the page in a new browser tab. Title Case."
    },
    "Open website of %@ in a new tab" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the arrow-square icon button on a credential row (its tooltip is “Open Website in a New Tab”). %@ is the credential’s title, usually the website’s name; do not translate it. Not shown on screen."
    },
    "Open With…" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of an attached file in the credential editor; it lets the user pick another app to open a decrypted copy. Title Case, ellipsis because a dialog follows; use the Finder’s own term for Open With."
    },
    "Opening it needs the vault that keeps it unlocked, then Touch ID or your Mac password." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the locked Input History panel when a vault already keeps the entries. “It” is Input History; “opening” means showing the entries. Sentence."
    },
    "Opening it needs Touch ID or your Mac password." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the locked Input History panel when the profile has no vault. “It” is Input History; “opening” means showing the entries. Touch ID is the Apple name. Sentence."
    },
    "Opening it needs your default vault unlocked, then Touch ID or your Mac password." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the locked Input History panel when the profile has a vault but none keeps the entries yet; the default vault will. “It” is Input History. Sentence."
    },
    "Opening…" : {
      "comment" : "Text under a spinner shown briefly on the Autofill settings page while it first loads, before it is known whether the vault is locked. Present participle with an ellipsis, Sentence case."
    },
    "Organization" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a field of a saved contact or address in the credential vault: the company or organization name. Noun. Sentence case; it appears next to “Email” in the entry’s fields."
    },
    "Other" : {
      "comment" : "Filter chip in the Vault tab, with a count after it: items such as Wi-Fi networks, API and SSH keys and custom fields. Shown only while the vault holds one. One word; tight."
    },
    "Other code settings differ" : {
      "comment" : "Small caption under the Verification code row in the History panel: the setup key is the same, but other settings of the code, such as its digits or period, differ. Sentence case."
    },
    "Other HTTPS origins" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a collapsible group under Websites in the credential editor. An origin is a website address (scheme, host and port); the group lists extra websites where the credential also fills. Sentence case."
    },
    "Other HTTPS origins (one per line)" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the multi-line text field inside the “Other HTTPS origins” group of the credential editor; one address per line. HTTPS stays as is. Sentence case."
    },
    "Other logins have this website and username with a different password." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row that waits for a choice: other logins, saved or in the same file, have this website and username but a different password. Also in the details of a part; see the longer variant."
    },
    "Other logins have this website and username with a different password. Choose Skip or Add Separately for each." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the details of one part of an import review row. “Skip” and “Add Separately” are menu items and must match their translations."
    },
    "Other passwords kept in History: %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Line under “Also kept” in the merge sheet. %lld is how many other passwords go into the merged credential’s History (its earlier versions). Fragment, no final stop."
    },
    "Other verification codes kept in History: %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Line under “Also kept” in the merge sheet. %lld is how many other verification codes go into the merged credential’s History (its earlier versions). Fragment, no final stop."
    },
    "Page edge" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, with the options Standard, Thin edge and None: how the edge of the page area around the web content is drawn. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Page spacing" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: the gap, in points, around the page. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Word in a credential’s detail line in the merge sheet, joined to other facts by “ · ”: the credential has one passkey. Also a part name in the export and import lists. Noun, singular; the plural is “%lld passkeys”."
    },
    "Passkey registration was cancelled, but the provider may have created it. Check your passkey provider before trying again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when creating a passkey was cancelled but the passkey provider may still have made one. It tells the user to check the provider before trying again."
    },
    "Passkey saved, but not confirmed" : {
      "comment" : "Title of an alert shown after a passkey was saved to Credential Manager but WSurf could not confirm that the website received it. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Passkeys" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor over the passkeys saved with the credential. Also a section chip on the Vault tab and a line in the vault statistics. Plural noun; passkey is Apple’s term."
    },
    "Passkeys for websites" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: how many passkeys for websites the vault holds. Not the passkey that unlocks the vault itself. Sentence case."
    },
    "Passkeys for websites saved in this vault stop working. Those websites still list them: sign in another way and remove them there." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Delete Vault sheet, shown only when the vault holds passkeys for websites. “Them” are the passkeys; the user is told to remove them on each website’s own account page. Sentence case."
    },
    "Passkeys have no earlier versions; a removed passkey is in Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Note at the bottom of the History panel’s field list: passkeys are never rolled back to an earlier version, and a removed passkey is found in the vault’s Trash. Sentence."
    },
    "Passkeys not confirmed with the website" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a warning section (triangle icon) on the Vault tab, listing passkeys that WSurf saved but could not confirm the website received. Sentence case."
    },
    "Passkeys: %lld → %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Line under “Also kept” in the merge sheet. First %lld is how many passkeys the primary credential has now, second %lld how many the merged one will have. Keep the arrow. Fragment."
    },
    "Passport" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. A passport document."
    },
    "Passport number" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Passport item: the passport number, hidden by default. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Passport type" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Passport item: the type of passport. Noun phrase."
    },
    "password" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase noun with two uses: inserted into “Copy this version’s %@” and “Copy the current %@” in the History panel; and one item in a “ · ” separated list of what an existing saved login holds, in the account menu of the passkey-creation prompt."
    },
    "Password also saved for another website" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the orange Reused badge on a login’s row in Settings › Credentials: the same password is saved for a credential of another website. Sentence case, no period."
    },
    "Password changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the password was changed in WSurf after an earlier import, and the change is kept. A date can follow after “ · ”. The password itself is never shown."
    },
    "Password Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies a saved password to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Password save suggestions" : {
      "comment" : "Row title of a reset row in Settings › Autofill for password save prompts, with the caption “Restore prompts on excluded sites.” and a Reset button. Counterparts: “Card save suggestions” and “Address save suggestions”. The code defines it, but this build shows only the card and address rows. Sentence case."
    },
    "Password, hidden" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label for an Input History row whose value is a password that has not been revealed; read instead of the row’s masked bullets. Not shown on screen. A noun, then a state."
    },
    "Password, passkey or code for the same website, saved separately" : {
      "comment" : "Why a merge is suggested: a password, a passkey and a verification code for one person on one website were saved as separate entries."
    },
    "Password, passkey or code saved separately" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: a password, a passkey or a verification code saved apart that seem to belong together. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Passwords and other text will stay on this Mac until you clear them. Anyone who learns your Mac password could read them." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert “Keep everything you type until you delete it?” in Input History. A warning about passwords being kept with no expiry. Sentence."
    },
    "Passwords, passkeys and verification codes stay hidden until you reveal or copy them." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote under the list of credentials on the Vault tab. Reveal and copy are the controls on each row."
    },
    "Payment Card" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the Add menu of the Credentials page that starts a new entry with an empty payment card. Noun. Title Case."
    },
    "Picture in Picture is unavailable for Chromium pages" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the disabled Picture in Picture button on the media card in the sidebar, replacing the usual Picture in Picture tooltip when the playing page runs in the Chromium engine. Chromium is a name and is not translated. No final period."
    },
    "PIN" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Payment card item: the card’s PIN; the value is hidden by default. Use the local abbreviation or word."
    },
    "Place of birth" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On Passport and ID document items. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Plain" : {
      "comment" : "Option of the Material control in Settings › Appearance › Theme: the alternative to Glass, which shows the desktop through the window. One word, an adjective; very tight space."
    },
    "Preparing the imported credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Short noun phrase naming the step that failed, inserted as %@ at the start of “… failed and nothing was written …” in an import error message. Sentence case, no period; it must work as the start of a sentence."
    },
    "Primary" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up menu in the merge sheet that picks which of the merged credentials is the primary one, the one that stays and whose values win. One word, an adjective used as a noun."
    },
    "Primary color" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: one chosen color from which the theme’s background, surface and accent colors are derived. Sentence case. Not the same as Primary text."
    },
    "Primary text" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the main text color. Sentence case. Not the same as Primary color, which seeds the palette."
    },
    "Private Browsing and removed profiles don’t keep a credential vault." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Credentials are unavailable card. Private Browsing is WSurf’s private mode, and a removed profile is one that was deleted. Use the app’s existing terms for both. Sentence."
    },
    "Private key" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an SSH key item: the private key, hidden by default and kept as it was received. Noun phrase."
    },
    "Protects this vault with a passkey one of your vaults already uses. You’ll confirm with it." : {
      "comment" : "Detail text under the Use existing passkey choice. “Protects” is third person (this choice protects the new vault). “It” is the passkey, which the user is asked to confirm with right after."
    },
    "Put this theme’s colors, brightness, transparency, spacing and layout back to the defaults." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Reset Theme to Default” entry in Settings › Appearance. Imperative."
    },
    "Puts this theme’s brightness, transparency and layout settings back to how WSurf ships them." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Reset theme row in Settings › Appearance › Theme for a theme that has no original to go back to, such as a built-in theme. Sentence case."
    },
    "Puts this theme’s colors and settings back to “%@”, the theme it was made from." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Reset theme row in Settings › Appearance › Theme for a saved theme that was made from another theme. %@ is the name of that original theme (a name, not to be translated). Sentence case."
    },
    "Read Accessibility Tree" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app reads an outline of a page’s accessibility roles, names and states. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase. Accessibility tree is the technical term."
    },
    "Read Console" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app reads the console messages captured from a tab. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase. Console is the web developer console."
    },
    "Read Development Info" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app reads a tab’s engine, measured viewport, zoom and development support, without any page content. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Read Network Activity" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app reads the network requests captured from a tab. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Read only" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the access level a connected app holds on a tab. Shown in small text beside the app’s name in the toolbar connection chip and the controlled-tab popover, for example “Claude Code · Read only”. Sentence case; a state, not a command. The dialog button Read Only is a separate string."
    },
    "Read Performance" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app reads how a page loaded: timing, paint, layout shift and resource sizes. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Reading credentials…" : {
      "comment" : "Progress caption with a spinner while the merge sheet reads and compares the selected credentials. Sentence case, ellipsis because it is ongoing."
    },
    "Redid Add Credential." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is adding a new credential. Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Add Credential” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Delete." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is deleting Trash entries permanently (they are hidden at once and removed for good when the Trash is left). Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Delete” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Edit." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is saving changes to a credential. Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Edit” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Merge." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is merging duplicate credentials into one. Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Merge” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Move to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is moving credentials to the vault’s Trash. Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Move to Trash” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Not the Same." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after Redo of Not the Same."
    },
    "Redid Restore." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Redo repeated the action; the action is restoring an item from the Trash. Past tense of Redo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Redo Restore” menu title."
    },
    "Redid Suggest Again." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after Redo of Suggest Again."
    },
    "Redo Add Credential" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is adding a new credential. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Delete" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is deleting Trash entries permanently (they are hidden at once and removed for good when the Trash is left). Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Edit" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is saving changes to a credential. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Merge" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is merging duplicate credentials into one. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Move to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is moving credentials to the vault’s Trash. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Not the Same" : {
      "comment" : "Edit menu: repeat Not the Same on a merge suggestion."
    },
    "Redo Restore" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Redo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Redo”. Title Case. Here the action is restoring an item from the Trash. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Redo Suggest Again" : {
      "comment" : "Edit menu: repeat Suggest Again on a dismissed merge suggestion."
    },
    "Reduce motion is on in System Settings, so WSurf skips these animations." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Fast transitions row in Settings › Appearance › Window, shown instead of its usual caption when the macOS accessibility setting Reduce motion is on. Use the macOS name of that setting. Sentence case."
    },
    "Reduce transparency or increase contrast is on in System Settings, so WSurf uses Plain." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Material row in Settings › Appearance › Theme, shown instead of the Glass caption when a macOS accessibility setting (Reduce transparency or Increase contrast) is on. Use the macOS names of those settings. Plain is the “Plain” choice of the Material control. Sentence case."
    },
    "Reload page?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet shown by a Chromium tab when the page asks for confirmation before it is reloaded. The page’s own message appears below it; buttons are Leave and Stay. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Relying party: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the passkey sheet. “Relying party” is the technical WebAuthn term for the website that owns the passkey. %@ is its domain, such as example.com, and is never translated. Label before a colon."
    },
    "Remember what I type" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the on/off switch of Input History in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab): WSurf records text typed on websites, including passwords, encrypted on this Mac. Sentence case. Also named by the hint “Turn on Remember what I type to start.”, so keep both identical."
    },
    "Remembered %@: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line under an assistant answer in the Ask panel when the assistant saved one note about the person. First %@ is what the note is about (its subject), second %@ is the note’s value. Both come from the assistant’s note and are not translated. Shown crossed out after Undo."
    },
    "Remembered %lld things" : {
      "comment" : "Line under an assistant answer in the Ask panel when the assistant saved several notes about the person from that turn. %lld is the number of notes, at least 2; the one-note case uses “Remembered %@: %@”. Shown crossed out after Undo. Tight space."
    },
    "Remove Favorite" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the context menu of a sidebar tab, split or favorite tile: takes the tab out of the Favorites tiles at the top of the sidebar, without closing it. Title Case, a verb phrase. Counterpart “Add Favorite”."
    },
    "Remove File" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Remove File?” dialog in the credential editor. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove File?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown after Remove… is chosen for an attached file in the credential editor. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Remove from Favorites" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an undoable action, shown in the Edit menu after Undo or Redo (for example “Undo Remove from Favorites”), for taking a tab out of Favorites at the top of the sidebar. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove Item" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Remove Item?” dialog; also the small red button on each item in the credential editor. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove Item?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown after Remove Item is clicked on a card or other item in the credential editor. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Remove Note" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Remove Note?” dialog in the credential editor. Also the tooltip of the red circled X button in the corner of each note. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove note %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the red circled X button on a note in the credential editor. %lld is the note’s position, starting at 1. Sentence case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove Note?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown when the user removes a note that has text, in the Notes section of the credential editor. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Remove Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Remove Passkey?” dialog in the credential editor: takes the passkey out of the credential when the editor is saved. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove passkey for %@ on %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Remove… button on a passkey row in the credential editor. First %@ is the passkey’s account name, second %@ is the website it belongs to; neither is translated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Remove passkey for %@ on %@ (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Remove… button on a passkey row, used only when two passkeys share the same account and website. First %@ is the account name, second the website, third a long identifier that tells them apart; do not translate any."
    },
    "Remove Passkey?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown after Remove… is clicked next to a passkey in the Passkeys section of the credential editor. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Remove the data stored by \"%@\" in %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog for the Remove… button on a row of Settings › Privacy › Website data. First %@ is the website’s name, in straight quotes; second %@ is the browser engine that stored it (WebKit or Chromium, not translated). A question."
    },
    "Remove Unlock Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the Remove Unlock Passkey? dialog, next to Cancel. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Remove unlock passkey %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Remove… button on a row of the Unlock passkeys section. %lld is the same position number as in the row title. A command, not shown on screen."
    },
    "Remove Unlock Passkey?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog before an unlock passkey is removed from a vault (Unlock passkeys section, Settings tab). Its message is a separate text. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Remove Verification Code" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Remove Verification Code?” dialog in the credential editor. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove verification code" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Remove… button in the Verification code section of the credential editor. Sentence case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Remove Verification Code?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown after Remove… is clicked in the Verification code section of the credential editor. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "Removed credentials stay here, encrypted, with their earlier versions, until you delete them permanently." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Trash section on the Vault tab of Settings › Autofill. Credentials the user removed are kept in Trash, still encrypted, together with their earlier versions, until deleted for good."
    },
    "Removed from this vault before, so it isn’t imported unless you choose to." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of a skipped import review row: the user removed it from this vault earlier, so it is left out unless the user chooses to import it. A vault is the encrypted store of credentials."
    },
    "Removing this file would leave the entry empty. Add a login, note or other detail first, or delete the entry. Nothing was saved." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when Save is chosen after removing the last file of an entry that holds nothing else. “Entry” is the credential being edited. Full sentences."
    },
    "Rename Theme" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet that asks for a new name for one of the user’s saved themes; its default button is Rename. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Rename…" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the This theme row of Settings › Appearance › Theme, and an item of the right-click menu on a saved theme in the theme gallery: it opens a sheet to type a new name. A verb; the ellipsis means a sheet follows."
    },
    "Replace Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Menu item for a part of an import review row that conflicts with a saved credential, and the menu’s label once chosen: overwrites the saved version with the other app’s. Title Case, a command; “Saved” means the already saved version."
    },
    "Replace Saved removes the password saved for “%@”. The other app’s login has none." : {
      "comment" : "Warning in the details of one part of an import review row: the saved credential named in the quotes has a password, but the other app’s login has none. “Replace Saved” is a menu item and must match it. %@ is a title."
    },
    "Replaces the saved password for this username." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History when a login with this username exists and the typed password differs. Sentence."
    },
    "Reported by the other app: created %@" : {
      "comment" : "Date line in the credential editor for a credential imported from another app that reported its own creation time. %@ is that date and time, already formatted. “The other app” is the app it was imported from."
    },
    "Reset Colors" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Reset colors row of the Colors card in Settings › Appearance: puts the colors of the shown light or dark variant of this theme back to the built-in theme’s. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Reset colors" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, shown only for a theme made from a built-in one; its button, Reset Colors, restores the original colors. Sentence case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Reset Development Settings" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app removes its viewport, device emulation and diagnostics from a tab. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Reset Theme" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive confirm button of the dialog that asks whether to reset the selected theme to its defaults. A verb phrase, Title Case; the other button is Cancel."
    },
    "Reset theme" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Appearance › Theme for undoing the changes made to the selected theme; its button is Reset Theme to Default. Sentence case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Reset Theme to Default" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the Reset theme row in Settings › Appearance › Theme; it opens a confirmation dialog. Also the title of its Settings search result. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Reset “%@” to its defaults?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog opened by Reset Theme to Default in Settings › Appearance › Theme. %@ is the name of the selected theme (a name, not to be translated). Sentence case, a question; the buttons are Reset Theme and Cancel."
    },
    "Restore %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Restore button on a row of the Trash list. %@ is the name of the removed item and should not be translated. Restore is a verb: put the item back in the vault."
    },
    "Restore the original colors of this theme’s shown variant." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Reset colors row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. The shown variant is the light or dark color set that is currently displayed."
    },
    "Restored from Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice above the Credentials list after the user restored a credential, or one removed password, code or passkey, from Trash; it offers Undo. Full sentence."
    },
    "Reveal" : {
      "comment" : "Button on a recorded password entry in Input History that shows the real text instead of dots; “Hide” takes its place afterwards. One word, a verb. Tight space."
    },
    "Review Import" : {
      "comment" : "Headline of the sheet in Settings › Autofill › Vault where credentials sent by another app or read from a CSV file are reviewed before anything is saved. Title Case; its confirming button is “Import”."
    },
    "Review merge of %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label only, for the Review Merge… button on a site heading. %@ is the site, or “credentials without a website” when the group has none."
    },
    "Review Merge…" : {
      "comment" : "Small button on a site heading in the By Site list, and on each suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: opens a sheet to review the merge before anything changes. Title Case, a command; the ellipsis means more follows."
    },
    "Rounds tabs, folders and the page." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Corner rounding row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Rounds is a verb: the slider rounds their corners."
    },
    "Rows grow with the icon." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Tab icon size row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance: sidebar tab rows get taller as the icon gets larger."
    },
    "Run Script" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app runs JavaScript in a shared page, which needs Developer access. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Same as current" : {
      "comment" : "Small caption at the right of a field’s title row in the History panel when the earlier version’s value equals the current one. Sentence case, narrow space."
    },
    "Same passkey as “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row: the item’s passkey is the same as the one in the saved credential named in the quotes. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Same site and username" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: the credentials share a website and a username. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Same site, username and password" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: credentials that share website, username and password. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "Same username on a related site" : {
      "comment" : "Reason line under a suggestion in the Suggested Merges sheet: the same username on another website with the same password or site name. Sentence case, no final period."
    },
    "same website and username as line %lld with another password or note. Choose what to do with each of them." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that has the same website and username as an earlier row but another password or note. %lld is the earlier row’s line number. The user must choose what to do with each one in the review. Lowercase fragment after “Line N:”."
    },
    "Same website, username and password" : {
      "comment" : "Why a merge is suggested: identical logins on the same website (Merge All Identical takes these)."
    },
    "Same website, username and password as “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the status line of an import review row: the item is identical to the saved credential named in the quotes. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated. A sentence about what a merge adds follows."
    },
    "Save an editable copy of a theme under a name and edit its colors, or edit the colors of your own theme. Saved themes can be renamed, duplicated or deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Customize” entry in Settings › Appearance. It also stands in for the old Save as Theme entry, so a search for save, rename, duplicate or delete finds it. Imperative; theme means a set of colors and layout."
    },
    "Save and fill" : {
      "comment" : "Section title at the top of the Settings tab of Settings › Autofill, above the switches for saving and filling passwords, payment cards, and contacts and addresses. Sentence case; “fill” means entering saved details into web forms."
    },
    "Save as Credential" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet opened by “Save as Credential…” in Input History, which shows website, username and masked password before saving them as a login. Title Case. “Credential” means a saved login."
    },
    "Save as Credential…" : {
      "comment" : "Item in an Input History entry’s “…” menu and context menu: opens a sheet to save the typed password as a login in the vault. Title Case, ellipsis because a sheet follows. “Credential” means a saved login."
    },
    "Save Copy…" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of an attached file in the credential editor; it saves a decrypted copy to a place the user chooses. Title Case, a verb phrase, ellipsis because a save panel follows. Also named in another message, so keep them the same."
    },
    "Save your credentials to another app first, if you want to keep them." : {
      "comment" : "Note beside the Export… button in the Delete Vault sheet. Sentence case."
    },
    "Saved as a new account that works on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a part that will be saved as a new credential in the vault. %@ is a comma-separated list of the websites it works on."
    },
    "Saved as a new account with no approved website, so autofill won’t offer it until you add one." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a part that will be saved as a new credential in the vault with no website, so autofill will not offer it until the user adds a website."
    },
    "Saved as a new account. The passkey stays tied to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a passkey part that will be saved as a new credential in the vault. %@ is the website the passkey belongs to and should not be translated."
    },
    "Saved as a separate credential, although “%@” already holds it." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row: the item will be saved as a new separate credential although the saved credential named in the quotes already holds it. %@ is that credential’s title and should not be translated."
    },
    "Saved into “%@”, which has no approved website, so autofill won’t offer it until you add one." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a part that will be saved into an existing credential named in the quotes, which has no website, so autofill will not offer it until the user adds one. %@ is its title."
    },
    "Saved into “%@”, which works on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a part that will be saved into an existing credential. First %@ is its title, second %@ a comma-separated list of the websites it works on."
    },
    "Saved to Credential Manager." : {
      "comment" : "Result text in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History after the login was saved. Credential Manager is the name of the settings area for logins. Sentence."
    },
    "Saved with this theme. Changing it never makes a copy." : {
      "comment" : "Note at the top of the Layout card in Settings › Appearance: the layout options below belong to the selected theme and are saved with it. “It” means any of those options; unlike colors, they never create a copy of a built-in theme."
    },
    "Saved with “%@”. The passkey stays tied to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the details of a passkey part that will be saved into an existing credential. First %@ is that credential’s title, second %@ the website the passkey belongs to. Do not translate them."
    },
    "Saves a copy named “%@” with this theme’s brightness, material and layout, and opens its colors." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Customize row in Settings › Appearance › Theme when a built-in theme is selected; its button is Customize…. %@ is the suggested name of the new copy (the built-in theme’s name plus “Custom”), and is a name, not to be translated. The copy keeps the theme’s brightness, material and layout settings, and the Colors section opens for it. Sentence case."
    },
    "Saves a new login for this website." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History when no matching login exists yet. Sentence."
    },
    "Saving the imported credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Short noun phrase naming the step that failed, inserted as %@ at the start of “… failed and nothing was written …” in an import error message. Sentence case, no period; it must work as the start of a sentence."
    },
    "Search %lld credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder and VoiceOver label of the search row at the top of a long autofill dropdown under a web page field. %lld is how many suggestions the list holds. Lowercase noun; “credentials” means saved logins and similar items."
    },
    "Search by name, username or website" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the search field above a list of credentials: in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab), in the Export sheet and in the import review sheet. It matches names, usernames and websites. Sentence case."
    },
    "Search by website, field or text" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the search field above the entries in Input History; it matches the website, the field name and the typed text. Sentence case, lowercase fragment after the verb."
    },
    "Search credentials" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the credential search fields, and of the search row at the top of a long autofill suggestion list. Sentence case. The Pick Credential… sheet has its own visible placeholder, “Search Credentials”."
    },
    "Search Input History" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the search field above the entries in Input History. Not shown on screen. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Search saved credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the search field in the “Merge Into…” sheet; it searches titles and websites of saved credentials. Sentence case."
    },
    "Second last name" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Name item: a second family name, as used in some countries. Noun."
    },
    "Secondary text" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the dimmer text color, used for unloaded tabs. Sentence case."
    },
    "Secondary text opacity" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the opacity slider beside the Secondary text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "Sections" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label only, for the row of filter chips on the Vault tab (All, Logins, Passkeys and so on). A plural noun."
    },
    "Secure Note" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the Add menu of the Credentials page that starts a new entry that holds only a private note. Noun. Title Case."
    },
    "Security" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Wi-Fi network item: the network’s security type, such as WPA2. Noun."
    },
    "Security code" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Payment card item: the code printed on the card (CVV or CVC); the value is hidden by default."
    },
    "Select" : {
      "comment" : "Context menu item on a credential row that turns on selecting and starts with this row; also the VoiceOver action name for selecting a row. Alternates with “Deselect”. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Select %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the checkbox at the start of an unselected row in the credential list or Trash. %@ is the credential’s name, shown as typed and not translated. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Select All (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the bar above the credential list that selects every row currently shown. %@ is how many rows that is, formatted for the locale. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Select at least one credential to export." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when an export is started with nothing selected. Full sentence; the first word is an imperative verb."
    },
    "Select None" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Export sheet, next to “Select All”, that unchecks every listed credential. Title Case, a verb phrase, small button."
    },
    "Select two or more to merge them." : {
      "comment" : "Hint under the selection count in the bar above the credential list, shown while fewer than two credentials are selected, about the Merge… button. Sentence case."
    },
    "Select, then type to filter the list. What you type is not sent to the page." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the search row at the top of the autofill dropdown that appears under a web page field (saved logins, cards or contacts). Typing filters the list inside WSurf and never reaches the website. Sentence."
    },
    "Sent to the profile “%@”. Nothing is saved until you review and confirm. Dismiss declines them; to import them later, send them again from the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the “Credentials from another app” card. %@ is the name of the browser profile that received them; do not translate it. Dismiss declines them."
    },
    "Set the window, sidebar, surface, text, secondary text, accent and assistant colors, plus tab text, icons, URL text, primary color and hue. Built-in themes make a copy." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Colors” entry in Settings › Appearance. Lists the color slots of a theme; editing a built-in theme first creates a copy. Imperative."
    },
    "Set Up" : {
      "comment" : "Button beside the setup key field in the credential editor that turns the entered key into verification codes. Title Case, a verb (the two-word phrasal verb “set up”)."
    },
    "Set Viewport" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app lays a page out at an exact viewport size, given in CSS pixels. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Setup key differs" : {
      "comment" : "Small caption under the Verification code row in the History panel: the setup key (the secret that produces the codes) of the earlier version differs from the current one. Sentence case."
    },
    "Setup key or otpauth:// link" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the secure text field in the Verification code section of the credential editor, where the user pastes the secret setup key or an otpauth:// link. Keep “otpauth://” as is. Sentence case."
    },
    "several saved logins have this website and username. Choose Skip or Add Separately." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row whose website and username match more than one login already saved in the vault, so Replace is not offered. “Skip” and “Add Separately” are the exact labels of the choices in the review; translate them identically. Lowercase fragment after “Line N:”."
    },
    "Sex" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On Passport and ID document items: the sex recorded on the document. One word, a noun."
    },
    "Show" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the eye button beside a masked value of a card or other item in the credential editor; it reveals the value. Alternates with “Hide”. One word, a verb."
    },
    "Show %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the eye button that reveals a masked value in a card or other item in the credential editor. %@ is the field’s name, such as “Card number”. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Show Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Button next to the message of a finished import in the Transfer finished section; it switches to the list of saved credentials on the Vault tab. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show Details" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row that holds a card or other item: reveals the item’s hidden values on the row. Counterpart of Hide Details. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show Entries" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the locked panel of Input History: asks for Touch ID or the Mac password and then lists the entries. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Show More" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the More in Trash row that loads and lists the next batch of removed items. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show Password" : {
      "comment" : "Button beside each credential in the merge sheet that reveals its password; also an item in a credential row’s ⋯ menu in the list. Alternates with “Hide Password”. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Show Password Health" : {
      "comment" : "Button above the credential list in Settings › Credentials. After Touch ID or the Mac password, the list marks weak and reused passwords (Weak and Reused chips and badges) until the vault locks. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Show password of %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Show Password button for one credential in the merge sheet. %@ is the credential’s name, shown as typed and not translated. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "show saved cards, documents and hidden fields" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt before the user reveals saved cards, ID documents or hidden fields of a credential. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "show a saved password" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user chooses Show Password for a saved credential on the Credentials page in Settings (its row menu or the merge sheet). It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "show a verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user chooses Show Verification Code for a saved credential on the Credentials page in Settings. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "show or copy a saved password or verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt the first time the user shows or copies the password or verification code in the editor of a saved credential, or shows the secrets of its History; that editor then does not ask again. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "show saved passwords, cards and documents" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the Touch ID or password prompt when the user opens the editor of a saved credential that holds a card or ID document, or shows the secrets of a credential’s History that holds one before that editor has asked: the same answer then also shows and copies the credential’s passwords and verification code. It completes a system sentence like “WSurf is trying to …”, so it is a lowercase verb phrase with no period."
    },
    "Show Secrets" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the top right of the History panel that unmasks the passwords, notes and card details of the versions shown; it can ask for Touch ID first. Title Case, a command. Alternates with “Hide Secrets”."
    },
    "Show Side Panel (⌥⌘A)" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of the toolbar button that toggles the side panel on the right (assistant activity or lyrics) while the panel is hidden. ⌥⌘A is the keyboard shortcut and stays as it is. A verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show Username" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row whose username is hidden (“Username hidden”): reveals it on the row. Counterpart of Hide Username. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show username" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the eye button beside a masked Username field in the credential editor; clicking it reveals the name. Alternates with “Hide username”. Sentence case, a command."
    },
    "Show Verification Code" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the “…” menu of a credential row that holds a verification code (a one-time code): shows the current code on the row, with a countdown. Counterpart of Hide Verification Code. Verb phrase, Title Case."
    },
    "Show Code" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Verification code section of the credential editor, beside the masked code of a saved credential: asks for Touch ID or the Mac password once for that editor, then shows the code. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Showing %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the More in Trash row. The first %lld is how many removed items are listed now; the second is how many items are in Trash in total."
    },
    "Showing the entries needs %@ unlocked, then Touch ID or your Mac password." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the row “Kept in this vault” in Input History when the vault the page’s picker shows is the one keeping the entries. %@ is that vault’s name (user-chosen, not translated). Touch ID is the Apple name."
    },
    "Showing the latest %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the Agent Activity panel above an external app’s action list when it is cut short. First %lld is how many entries are shown (the newest), second %lld is the total."
    },
    "Shown at %@ so it stays readable." : {
      "comment" : "Note under a text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance when the text is drawn with more opacity than the slider says, to stay readable. %@ is the opacity actually used, already formatted as a percentage such as 85%."
    },
    "Shows what it can use and lets you stop it." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the toolbar badge for an external app using the window; pressing it opens a popover listing the tabs it can use, with a Stop button. “It” is the external app."
    },
    "Sidebar font weight" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the “Font weight” row of Settings › Appearance (weight of the sidebar text) as it appears in Settings search results. Sentence case; weight means thickness of letters, not mass."
    },
    "Sidebar layout" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Sidebar layout entry in Settings search: the Layout options in the Sidebar section of Settings › Appearance (tab and folder edges, margin, padding, folder indent and tab icons). A noun phrase."
    },
    "Sidebar margin" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: the space, in points, between the sidebar’s tabs and the window edge. Sentence case."
    },
    "Sign in to %@ with a passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the macOS Touch ID or Mac password prompt that verifies the user right before WSurf signs in to a website with a passkey saved in Credential Manager. %@ is the website’s domain name, such as example.com, and is never translated. A verb phrase, no final full stop."
    },
    "Sign in to %@ with a passkey?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the passkey sign-in sheet. %@ is the domain of the website the user would sign in to, such as example.com, and is never translated. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Sign in with a saved passkey?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the first alert shown when a website asks to sign in with a passkey, before WSurf unlocks or shows any account. The next line names the website. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Sign-in" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor over the Name, Username, Password fields and the Generate Password button. A noun (the act of signing in). Sentence case."
    },
    "Skip All" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of an import review group heading: imports nothing of any item in the group. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Skipped" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a group in the import review sheet, and its filter chip: items left out by default, such as ones removed here before. Also the first word of an import receipt line for a credential that was skipped. A past participle, not a command."
    },
    "Some copies are still saved on this Mac. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error text on the move-to-vault card in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when erasing the old copies did not finish. Sentence case."
    },
    "Some websites aren’t secure HTTPS addresses, so they weren’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: some of an item’s websites were left out because they are not secure HTTPS addresses; the item itself is kept. Plural subject. Full sentence."
    },
    "something went wrong" : {
      "comment" : "Fallback reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period."
    },
    "Source unknown" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a passkey’s detail line in the credential editor, joined to the other facts by “ · ”: it is not known whether WSurf created the passkey or it was imported. Sentence case."
    },
    "Square" : {
      "comment" : "Value label of the Corner rounding slider in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance when it is at zero: no rounding at all. An adjective; at other positions the label is a percentage. Tight."
    },
    "SSH key" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. An SSH key, which can only arrive through a transfer; SSH stays as is."
    },
    "staging.example.com" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder in the text field of the Add a Developer Site dialog in Settings › Connected apps: an example website address. Do not translate."
    },
    "Start Diagnostics" : {
      "comment" : "Activity title when a connected app starts capturing a tab’s console messages and network request details. Shown in Agent Activity and as the Latest action of an external connection. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Statistics" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the section on the Settings tab of Settings › Autofill that lists counts of what the open vault holds: credentials, logins, passkeys, notes and so on. Sentence case, a plural noun."
    },
    "Stay" : {
      "comment" : "Second button of the Leave page? / Reload page? sheet: keeps the page open and where it is. One word, a verb; the other button is Leave."
    },
    "Stop %@" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the context menu of a sidebar tab, favorite tile or split held by one external app: disconnects it from every tab in the window. %@ is the app’s name, not translated. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Stop %lld Apps" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the context menu of a sidebar tab, favorite tile or split held by several external apps: disconnects all of them. %lld is the number of apps, at least 2. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Stop External Connections" : {
      "comment" : "View menu item (⌥⌘.) and Command Palette command that disconnects the connected apps (external MCP clients) using this window. Title Case; a verb phrase."
    },
    "Stopping ends their access to this window’s tabs. They need your approval to connect again." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the toolbar badge’s popover, above the Stop button. “Their” and “they” are the external apps listed in the popover; approval means the person must allow them again. Sentence."
    },
    "Street" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On an Address item: the street and house number line. Noun."
    },
    "Suffix" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Name item: a name suffix such as Jr. or III. Noun."
    },
    "Suggested (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Segment of the Suggested Merges sheet: the suggestions, with their count."
    },
    "Suggested Merges" : {
      "comment" : "Headline of the sheet listing credentials that look like duplicates; opened by the Suggested Merges (n) button. Title Case."
    },
    "Suggested merges" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of a group in the import review sheet, and its filter chip with a count after it: items whose login or passkey a saved credential already holds and that add something to it, such as a note or a website. Sentence case; not the Title Case “Suggested Merges” sheet."
    },
    "Suggested Merges (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the Vault tab toolbar that opens the Suggested Merges sheet. %@ is the number of suggestions. Title Case."
    },
    "Surface" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the color behind interface elements such as toolbar controls and buttons. Noun; Sentence case."
    },
    "Surname prefix" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. On a Name item: a particle placed before the surname, such as “van” or “de”. Noun."
    },
    "Switch Engine" : {
      "comment" : "Default (destructive-style) button of the Switch rendering engine? alert; the other button is Cancel. Title Case, a verb phrase; engine means the browser engine (WebKit or Chromium)."
    },
    "Switch rendering engine?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation alert shown before a website switches between the WebKit and Chromium engines while a tab has something that would be lost (edited form fields, audio, a download, screen sharing, camera or microphone use, or the assistant at work). Sentence case, a question. Rendering engine means the browser engine."
    },
    "Tab and folder edges" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, with the options Standard, Thin edge and None: how the edges of sidebar tab and folder rows are drawn. Sentence case; plural."
    },
    "Tab icon size" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: the size, in points, of the website icon in each sidebar tab row. Sentence case."
    },
    "Tab icons" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, with the options Monochrome and Color: whether the website icons of loaded tabs in the sidebar are drawn in one color or in full color. Sentence case."
    },
    "Tab padding" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its slider: the inner space, in points, at the start of a sidebar tab row. Sentence case."
    },
    "Tab text" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the color of the titles of loaded tabs and folders in the sidebar. Sentence case."
    },
    "Tab text opacity" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the opacity slider beside the Tab text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "Tab titles, icons and the address, unless one is colored below." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Primary text row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance: where this text color applies, unless the Tab text, Icons or URL text row below sets its own."
    },
    "Take Over" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the popover of the “AI” badge on a tab. It ends the external app’s access to that tab only, so the person uses it again themselves. Title Case, a verb phrase; sits next to “Stop”."
    },
    "Take Over Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the top of the context menu of a sidebar tab or favorite tile (or a split holding one such tab) when an external app holds it: ends that app’s access to it. Title Case, a verb phrase. Plural twin: “Take Over Tabs”."
    },
    "Take Over Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the top of the context menu of a split in the sidebar (two pages shown together) when external apps hold its tabs: ends their access to those tabs. Title Case, a verb phrase. Singular twin: “Take Over Tab”."
    },
    "Takes back what the assistant just remembered" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Undo button in the “Remembered …” line under an assistant answer; it forgets the new notes or restores the earlier value. Third person, present tense, no period."
    },
    "Taking over ends their access to this tab. Stopping ends their access to this window’s tabs, and they need your approval to connect again." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the popover of the “AI” badge on a tab, above the Take Over and Stop buttons. “Their” and “they” are the external apps listed there. Sentence."
    },
    "Text" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. Plain text. One word, a noun."
    },
    "Text you type on websites appears here." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under “Nothing recorded yet” in Input History when recording is on. Sentence."
    },
    "That choice isn’t available, or it doesn’t fit with the other choices. Change it, or skip the credential, and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the user’s choices in the import review do not fit together. The user is told to change a choice or skip the credential."
    },
    "That choice isn’t available. Change it and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown in the merge sheet when one of the user’s picks is not valid for the credentials being merged. Full sentences; the second is an instruction."
    },
    "That import is no longer waiting. Start the transfer again from the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when an import started from another app through the macOS credential exchange is no longer pending. The user must start the transfer again from the other app."
    },
    "That passkey can’t protect the vault. Choose a passkey provider that supports the PRF extension." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the chosen passkey provider cannot be used to protect a vault. “PRF extension” is a technical WebAuthn term and stays as is. Full sentences."
    },
    "That passkey can’t unlock this vault." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the chosen passkey does not match the vault being unlocked. Full sentence."
    },
    "That passkey is no longer enrolled in that vault. Choose a passkey again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the chosen passkey is no longer one of the vault’s unlock passkeys. The second sentence asks the user to pick a passkey again."
    },
    "That vault is no longer listed. Check again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the selected vault is gone from the profile’s list of vaults. The user is asked to check (read the list) again."
    },
    "The %lld attached files stay in WSurf: other apps can’t receive files. To copy one, open its entry and choose Save Copy…." : {
      "comment" : "Notice in the Export Credentials sheet when the selected credentials hold attached files. %lld is the number of files (1 or more). “Save Copy…” is the button in an entry’s Files section; keep it identical to that button’s translation."
    },
    "The address in the toolbar." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the URL text row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. The address is the website address in the toolbar."
    },
    "The assistant’s activity, questions and buttons. A theme without one uses the accent color." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Assistant color row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. “One” is an assistant color; if the theme has none it uses the Accent color row."
    },
    "The cards and addresses or the vault changed. Nothing was erased. Review them again." : {
      "comment" : "Error text on the move-to-vault card in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab), shown when the old copies or the vault changed since they were reviewed. “Them” are the cards and addresses. Sentence case."
    },
    "The Chromium page is closed." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when an action is attempted on a Chromium tab’s page that has already been closed. Chromium is the browser engine’s name and stays untranslated."
    },
    "The copies saved on this Mac stay until you erase them." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Move to the Vault section in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab): moving does not delete the old copies. Sentence case."
    },
    "The copy isn’t encrypted. Anyone who can open it can read it." : {
      "comment" : "Message line in the Mac save panel opened by Save Copy… on an attached file. It warns that the saved copy is a plain, decrypted file. Two short sentences."
    },
    "The credential already has one of these, and restoring would replace it." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused, after “This can’t be restored right now.”. “One of these” is the kind of item named in that row (password, verification code, passkey, notes and so on); the credential already has one. Joined into one paragraph."
    },
    "The credential store belongs to another profile or installation." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: the stored credentials belong to another profile or another installation of WSurf. The credential store is the saved credentials as stored on this Mac. Sentence."
    },
    "The credential store couldn’t be read. It may be damaged." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: the stored credentials could not be read, and the data may be damaged. Sentence."
    },
    "The credential store doesn’t match its own records, so it may have been replaced or rolled back." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: the stored credentials don’t match their own records, so they may have been swapped for another copy or restored to an older state. Sentence."
    },
    "The credential store was made for a different profile." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: the stored credentials were made for a different browser profile than the one open now. Sentence."
    },
    "The credential store’s files are missing or incomplete, but parts of it remain." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: some of the stored credentials’ files are missing or incomplete, but others remain. Sentence."
    },
    "The credential this belongs to is no longer in the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Reason shown in the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused, after “This can’t be restored right now.”. “This” is the removed part (a password, passkey, note and so on) and the credential it belonged to has been deleted. The sentences are joined into one paragraph."
    },
    "The credential vault couldn’t be read. It may be damaged." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the vault file is unreadable or corrupt. Full sentences."
    },
    "the credentials couldn’t be read (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period. The inner %@ is a short technical code in English (for example where in the data it failed) and should not be translated."
    },
    "The CSV file could not be saved, so nothing was exported. Anything already at that location was left as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Message when saving the exported CSV file failed. “That location” is the place the user chose in the save panel; a file already there was not replaced. Full sentences."
    },
    "The default vault is locked." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Which vault?” alert when a new login would be saved to the default vault but that vault is locked. Full sentence."
    },
    "The export did not start, so no credentials were sent. Nothing was changed in WSurf." : {
      "comment" : "Message when an export from WSurf to another app failed before any credential data was passed on. Full sentences."
    },
    "The file could not be opened, so nothing was imported. It may have moved, not be readable by this account, or not be an ordinary file. The file was not changed." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when the chosen import file cannot be opened at all. “Not an ordinary file” means something other than a regular file, such as a folder. “This account” is the Mac user account. Full sentences."
    },
    "The file could not be used as a password CSV (it may be too large, not a Passwords export, damaged, or hold more logins than the vault can keep), so nothing was imported. %@ The file was not changed." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when the CSV file the user chose cannot be read as a password list. %@ is either empty or the sentence “The problem is on line N.”, so it sits between two sentences. Passwords is Apple’s Passwords app; the vault is the encrypted store of Credential Manager."
    },
    "The file couldn’t be imported (%@). Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when a file could not be imported. %@ is a short technical code in English (what kind of problem and where in the data) and should not be translated."
    },
    "The file has %lld rows. %lld already saved here, %lld can’t be imported." : {
      "comment" : "Summary at the top of the review sheet for a password CSV file. In order, the numbers are rows in the file, rows already saved in the vault, and rows that cannot be imported. “Here” means in the vault."
    },
    "The file will not be encrypted. Anyone who can open it can read the passwords in it." : {
      "comment" : "Message line of the save panel for exporting passwords to a CSV file: a security warning that the saved file is plain readable text. Sentence."
    },
    "The files in this vault would take more than %@. Remove files from entries to make room." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when adding a file would take all the files kept in the vault over its storage limit. %@ is that limit with a unit, such as “2 GB”. “Entries” are the saved credentials. Full sentences."
    },
    "The floating sidebar and the Minimal bar. The docked sidebar uses the window color." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sidebar row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Minimal is a window style whose bar floats over the page; the docked sidebar is the standard one attached to the window, and “the window color” is the Window background row."
    },
    "The icons on the toolbar and on controls." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Icons row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance."
    },
    "The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. To import the file, choose it again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when importing a CSV file ended. %@ is a lowercase reason clause such as “it was cancelled”. The user must choose the file again."
    },
    "The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. To import these credentials, send them again from the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when an import sent from another app ended. %@ is a lowercase reason clause such as “it was cancelled”. The user must send the credentials again from the other app."
    },
    "The import is no longer open. To import these credentials, send them again from the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the import review the user was working in is gone. The user must send the credentials again from the other app."
    },
    "The merged credential would have more than %lld cards and other items. Remove some first." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the merge sheet. %lld is the maximum number of cards, addresses and other items one credential can hold. The second sentence tells the user to remove some before merging."
    },
    "The merged credential would have more than %lld files. Remove some files first." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the merge sheet. %lld is the maximum number of attached files one credential can hold. The second sentence tells the user to remove some files before merging."
    },
    "The merged credential would have more than %lld notes. Remove some notes first." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the merge sheet. %lld is the maximum number of notes one credential can hold. The second sentence tells the user to remove some notes before merging."
    },
    "The merged credential would have more than %lld websites. Remove some websites first." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the merge sheet. %lld is the maximum number of websites one credential can hold. The second sentence tells the user to remove some websites before merging."
    },
    "The other app sent no website for this." : {
      "comment" : "Small caption on an import review row that has a login or verification code but no website, so autofill will not offer it until the user adds one."
    },
    "The other app’s websites aren’t added: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to a part’s destination line. %@ is a comma-separated list of websites the other app sent that are not added to the saved credential."
    },
    "The page asks: “%@”\n\nThe answer would be: “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Body of the dialog that asks whether an external connection (a connected app) may answer a JavaScript prompt on a webpage. The first %@ is the text the page asks, shortened if long; the second is the answer the app would type. Both are supplied at runtime. The text contains a blank line between the two parts."
    },
    "The page changed. Read it again before continuing." : {
      "comment" : "Error text for an automated page action (such as a script run by a connected app) that was aimed at a page or frame that has since changed or is no longer allowed to run it. Two short sentences; the second is an instruction to read the page again."
    },
    "The page couldn’t be printed." : {
      "comment" : "Title of the warning alert shown when printing a page fails; the line below it is the specific reason. Sentence case, ends with a full stop."
    },
    "The page image is unavailable." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when WebKit could not produce a snapshot image of the current page (for example for a screenshot) and gave no reason. One sentence."
    },
    "The passkey for %@ on %@ moves to Trash when you save. The website still lists it; remove it there too if you no longer use it." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove Passkey?” dialog in the credential editor. First %@ is the passkey’s account name, second %@ is the website it belongs to; neither is translated. Trash is the vault’s Trash. Two sentences."
    },
    "The passkey was created but setup didn’t finish. It still exists in your passkey provider; remove it there if you don’t want it." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when a new unlock passkey was created in the user’s passkey provider but the vault setup did not finish. It tells the user to remove the leftover passkey there if unwanted."
    },
    "The password will fill on: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Bold line in the merge sheet. %@ is the host names of the websites the merged password will fill on, joined as a list by the system. Fragment, not a full sentence."
    },
    "The primary credential’s name, username, password, verification code and notes win. The other passwords and codes stay in its History, and every passkey, note, item and website is kept." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Primary pop-up menu in the merge sheet. History is the list of earlier versions of a credential; the other credentials’ passwords and codes are saved there. One sentence."
    },
    "The problem is on line %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence inserted into the “The file could not be used as a password CSV…” message when the broken line of the CSV file is known. %lld is that line’s number in the file."
    },
    "The room between a tab’s edge and its icon." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Tab padding row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Room means space."
    },
    "The room between the tabs and the window edge." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Sidebar margin row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Room means space."
    },
    "The saved logins changed. Check the details and save again." : {
      "comment" : "Notice with a warning icon inside the Save as Credential sheet (opened from an Input History entry) after the saved logins changed while the sheet was open and the plan was recomputed. Asks the user to review the shown details and press Save again."
    },
    "The saved logins changed. Nothing was changed. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Result message in the Save as Credential sheet (opened from an Input History entry): the saved logins changed in the meantime, so the login was not saved. Three short sentences; Try again is an instruction."
    },
    "The saved password is weak: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Note under the sign-in fields of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials. %@ is a list of one or more reasons, joined in the system’s list format (“…, … and …”), each a lowercase clause such as “it is shorter than 8 characters”. A full sentence."
    },
    "The setup key moves to Trash when you save." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove Verification Code?” dialog in the credential editor. The setup key is the secret that makes the verification codes. Trash is the vault’s Trash. Sentence."
    },
    "The system couldn’t complete the transfer." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when macOS rejected the credential transfer (import or export between WSurf and another app). Full sentence."
    },
    "the system couldn’t deliver the credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period. The credentials are those sent from another app through the macOS credential exchange."
    },
    "The title of tabs and folders that are loaded." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Tab text row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Loaded means the tab’s page is active, the opposite of an asleep (unloaded) tab."
    },
    "The titles of tabs that are asleep (unloaded), dimmer than primary text." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Secondary text row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. A tab that is asleep, or unloaded, has had its web content released but stays in the sidebar. Primary text is the name of another row."
    },
    "The transfer could not be read, so nothing was imported. The problem is at %@%@: %@. This transfer was discarded, and WSurf does not retry it." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when data sent by another app is rejected. First %@ is the technical position of the bad record, such as “account[2]/item[0]”, never translated. Second %@ is empty or a space plus a technical credential type in parentheses; keep it glued to the first. Third %@ is a lowercase reason fragment, with no final period."
    },
    "the transfer has more than %@ collections" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of collections (groups of items) allowed in one transfer, formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "the transfer has more than %@ credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of credentials allowed in one transfer, formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "the transfer has more than %@ items" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of items (accounts) allowed in one transfer, formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "the transfer holds more than %@ MB" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum size of the whole transfer as a number of megabytes (MB)."
    },
    "the transfer is over WSurf’s import limits" : {
      "comment" : "Fallback reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. It says that the received data is larger than WSurf accepts."
    },
    "The vault already holds everything here." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in the import review sheet when every listed item is already in the vault, so the Import button is off. Sentence case."
    },
    "The vault changed. Review your selection before exporting again." : {
      "comment" : "Bold headline of a notice in the Export sheet, shown when the vault changed while the sheet was open. Nothing was sent; the user checks the selection and clicks Export again. Lines below name the credentials that changed or are gone. Sentence case."
    },
    "The vault is encrypted with your unlock passkeys. If you lose every unlock passkey, WSurf cannot recover the vault or anything stored in it, and there is no recovery option. Removing an unlock passkey does not change the vault’s encryption key. Someone with that passkey and an older vault file can still decrypt later copies of this vault they obtain. Deleting the vault does not delete backups." : {
      "comment" : "Warning paragraph at the bottom of the Create Credential Vault sheet, read before creating a vault: losing every unlock passkey means no recovery, removing a passkey does not change the encryption key, and deleting a vault does not delete backups. Keep the serious, precise tone."
    },
    "The vault locked. Unlock it and review again." : {
      "comment" : "Error text on the move-to-vault card in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when the vault locked, or its unlock expired, during the move. “Review” refers to the Review… button. Sentence case."
    },
    "The vault needs at least one unlock passkey." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings saying a vault must keep at least one passkey that can unlock it. A passkey here is the sign-in credential kept in the user’s passkey provider."
    },
    "Theme brightness" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the brightness slider in Settings › Appearance › Theme; not shown on screen. A noun phrase."
    },
    "Theme hue" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Hue slider in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "Theme name" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Name text field in the Customize Theme and Rename Theme sheets in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "These can be suggested for merging again." : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation after Suggest Again, in the sheet and the page notice (with Undo)."
    },
    "These changes stay as they are. Only the names of the fields and the dates are shown, never their values." : {
      "comment" : "Caption shown when the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” section is expanded in the import review sheet. It says the changes stay and that only field names and dates are listed. Sentences."
    },
    "These colors are for the dark appearance, which is showing now." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Every theme has separate light and dark colors; this says the color pickers edit the dark set because the dark appearance is showing now. The light-appearance sentence is a separate string."
    },
    "These colors are for the light appearance, which is showing now." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Every theme has separate light and dark colors; this says the color pickers edit the light set because the light appearance is showing now. The dark-appearance sentence is a separate string."
    },
    "These contacts have no details autofill can use." : {
      "comment" : "Error text under the Import rows in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when several contacts were picked and none has usable details. Plural counterpart of “This contact has no details autofill can use.” Sentence case."
    },
    "These credentials look like one. Nothing is merged until you review it and confirm." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the headline of the Suggested Merges sheet."
    },
    "These credentials were saved by a newer version of WSurf. Update WSurf to open them. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "One explanation under the title “Credentials can’t be opened”: the credentials were saved by a newer WSurf, which this version can’t read. The user should update WSurf. Nothing was changed. Sentences."
    },
    "These passkeys were saved here, but WSurf could not confirm that the website received them. Test sign-in on the website; remove any passkey that does not work. Dismiss only hides this notice." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the “Passkeys not confirmed with the website” section. “Dismiss” is the name of the button in that section; it hides the notice, not the passkeys."
    },
    "These websites are on other sites. The merged password and verification code fill on one only if you tick it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “Also fill on” checkboxes in the merge sheet. Other sites means websites that belong to a different site than the primary credential’s. Sentence."
    },
    "These won’t be suggested for merging again." : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation after Not the Same, in the sheet and the page notice (with Undo)."
    },
    "They are in the vault. Review them, then erase the copies saved on this Mac." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Cards and addresses saved on this Mac row in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when the entries are already in the vault but old copies remain. “They” are the cards and addresses; the button is Review…. Sentence case."
    },
    "Thin edge" : {
      "comment" : "Option in the Page edge and Tab and folder edges segmented controls in Settings › Appearance › Layout, between Standard and None: a thin line is drawn at the edge. Sentence case; very tight."
    },
    "Thin edge and None draw selected tabs without glass." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Tab and folder edges row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Thin edge and None are the names of two options; glass is the translucent glass highlight behind a selected tab."
    },
    "This answer %@ and usually can’t be undone." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the same dialog, added when the answer would also trigger a sensitive action. %@ is a clause such as “completes a purchase” or “moves money” (see those entries); it must read correctly right after “This answer”."
    },
    "This can’t be redone: the credential changed since, or its copy in Trash is gone. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when Redo is no longer possible because the credential changed since or its copy in Trash is gone. Counterpart of the “can’t be undone” entry. “Redo” means applying an undone change again."
    },
    "This can’t be restored right now." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the note under a Trash row when Restore was refused. It is followed by a reason sentence and then “Nothing was changed.”, all joined into one paragraph, with the Dismiss and Try Again buttons below."
    },
    "This can’t be undone: the credential changed since, or its copy in Trash is gone. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when Undo is no longer possible because the credential changed since or its copy in Trash is gone. Counterpart of the “can’t be redone” entry. “Undo” means taking back the last change."
    },
    "This contact has no details autofill can use." : {
      "comment" : "Error text under the Import rows in Settings › Autofill (Vault tab) when the single contact picked has no usable details. Singular; the plural counterpart is “These contacts have no details autofill can use.” Sentence case."
    },
    "This credential changed while the list was open. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when Show Details or a copy found a card or ID document that the list did not hold when it was read, so nothing was shown or copied without Touch ID. The page has already read the vault again; trying again asks for Touch ID first. Full sentences."
    },
    "This file couldn’t be decrypted. It may be damaged. Nothing was saved or opened." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when an attached file’s encrypted copy doesn’t open or isn’t the file that was added, for example while previewing it or saving a copy. “Decrypted” means unlocked from its encrypted form. Full sentences."
    },
    "This file is missing from the vault’s folder. Restore the vault’s files from a backup, or remove the file." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when an attached file is previewed, saved as a copy or opened in another app but its encrypted copy is no longer in the vault’s folder on this Mac. Full sentences."
    },
    "This import was discarded. WSurf dropped its copy of the file’s data. No data was written and the file was not changed. To import it, choose the file again." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when importing a password CSV file that the user chose ended before anything was saved. “Dropped its copy” means WSurf let go of the data it had read; the file itself is untouched. Full sentences."
    },
    "This item" : {
      "comment" : "Fallback that starts the sentence “%@ isn’t supported yet, so it wasn’t imported.” in the import review sheet when the kind of the received part isn’t known. A noun phrase with a capital first letter, because it begins a sentence."
    },
    "this item has more than %@ notes" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of notes one item may hold, formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "this item has more than %@ websites" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum number of websites one item may list, formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "this item holds more than %@ MB" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum size of one item as a number of megabytes (MB), formatted for the user’s locale."
    },
    "This item is removed when you save. You can copy it back from History." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove Item?” dialog in the credential editor. History is the panel of earlier versions of the credential. Sentence."
    },
    "this item would be larger than %@ MB once saved" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message after a colon and before a full stop. Lowercase, no final period. %@ is the maximum size of one item as saved, a number of megabytes (MB) that may have a decimal part."
    },
    "This login is already saved." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the Save as Credential sheet of Input History: caption when the typed login is already saved, and the result text after pressing Save. Sentence."
    },
    "This login is saved in more than one unlocked vault." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Which vault?” alert when the login to fill is found in several unlocked vaults. A login is the username and password saved for a website. Full sentence."
    },
    "This note is removed when you save. You can copy it back from History." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove Note?” dialog in the credential editor. History is the panel of earlier versions of the credential, opened with View History. Sentence."
    },
    "This permanently deletes %lld item(s) from Trash, including their earlier versions." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Delete Permanently? dialog for the items chosen. %lld is the number of chosen items; “item(s)” covers one or many. More sentences follow in the same paragraph, such as that it can’t be undone."
    },
    "This permanently deletes everything in Trash, including anything added to it before you confirm (%lld items right now), and all their earlier versions." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Delete Permanently? dialog after Empty Trash was chosen. %lld is how many items are in Trash at that moment (it can be any number, including 1). More sentences follow in the same paragraph, such as that it can’t be undone."
    },
    "This permanently deletes the vault, its Trash and its earlier versions. It can’t be undone." : {
      "comment" : "Warning note at the top of the Delete Vault sheet. Its Trash is the vault’s own Trash of removed items; earlier versions are the saved older versions of credentials. Sentence case."
    },
    "This profile already has the most vaults it can hold." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the profile has reached the maximum number of credential vaults. Full sentence."
    },
    "This reloads the website and may end active work, media, or downloads." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Switch rendering engine? alert. It warns that changing the engine reloads the website and may end active work, playing media or downloads. One sentence."
    },
    "This removes the items from the vault only. It can’t reach copies of the vault saved elsewhere, such as backups." : {
      "comment" : "Warning sentence in the marked-items bar of the Trash list and in the Delete Permanently? dialog message: deleting changes this vault only and cannot touch copies of the vault saved elsewhere, such as backups. Joined with other sentences into one paragraph."
    },
    "This removes the vault from WSurf only. It can’t reach copies of the vault saved elsewhere, such as backups. You’ll confirm with this vault’s unlock passkey." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Delete Vault sheet. The vault’s unlock passkey is the passkey this vault is unlocked with; the system asks for it as the second confirmation after the user confirms in the sheet. Sentence case."
    },
    "this row has a verification code, which isn’t imported. Set it up again with the website." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the CSV import review for a row that holds a verification code (one-time code). The row is still imported but the code is not. Shown after “Line N:”. Lowercase fragment."
    },
    "This saved login is then offered on %@ too. No copy is saved." : {
      "comment" : "Line under the headline “Add %@ to “%@”?” in the toolbar popover; says what Add Website does. %@ is the current website (address-bar form). Sentence."
    },
    "This saves the selected passwords to a CSV file that is NOT encrypted: anyone who can open the file can read every password in it. You choose where it goes, and WSurf never deletes it for you. Delete it as soon as you have imported it elsewhere. Don’t open it in a spreadsheet app, which may change or run cells that start with = + - or @." : {
      "comment" : "Warning paragraph in the Export Passwords to CSV sheet: the CSV file is not encrypted and should be deleted after use. “NOT” is capitalised for emphasis, so keep the emphasis. The characters = + - and @ are literal and stay as they are."
    },
    "This theme" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in Settings › Appearance › Theme, shown only for a saved theme, in front of the Rename…, Duplicate and Delete… buttons that act on the selected theme. Sentence case."
    },
    "This theme draws its window, sidebar and surface colors as a solid ground, without the website tint." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Colors card for a copy of Standard or Calm whose base colors are drawn as a plain solid background instead of picking up the current website’s color. Website tint is the name of a switch in Settings › Appearance. Window, sidebar and surface are the color rows below."
    },
    "This theme is already at its defaults." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Reset theme row in Settings › Appearance › Theme when there is nothing to reset, so its button is off. Sentence case."
    },
    "This transfer has everything from Passwords" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox label in the “No longer in Passwords” section: the user confirms that the transfer contains everything from Passwords, which allows moving the missing credentials to Trash. Passwords is Apple’s app."
    },
    "This transfer was discarded. WSurf dropped its copy of the imported data and can no longer use it. No data was written. Export again from Passwords." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when an import sent by another app (normally Apple’s Passwords) ended before anything was saved, for example because WSurf locked. “Dropped its copy” means WSurf let go of the received data. Full sentences."
    },
    "This vault" : {
      "comment" : "Text on the Default vault row, shown instead of a button when the selected vault is already the default vault. Sentence case, a plain statement."
    },
    "This vault isn’t empty. Nothing was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the user tries to delete a vault that still holds credentials. Full sentences."
    },
    "This vault was saved by an older version of WSurf. Unlocking it upgrades it to a new format that every other WSurf build, including older ones, cannot read. A copy from before the upgrade is kept next to the vault, but it won’t include anything you change afterwards." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the Upgrade This Vault? dialog. A build is a version of the WSurf app. The copy kept next to the vault is a backup file made before the upgrade; it does not get later changes."
    },
    "This vault was saved by an older version of WSurf. Unlocking it upgrades it to the new format." : {
      "comment" : "Caption on the locked card under “Credentials are locked” when the vault needs an upgrade; unlocking then asks for confirmation. Short version of the Upgrade This Vault? message."
    },
    "This vault was saved by an older version of WSurf. Unlocking it upgrades it to the new format. Confirm to continue." : {
      "comment" : "Message on the Credentials page in Settings when unlocking a vault would upgrade its file format first. The user confirms to continue. Full sentences."
    },
    "This version" : {
      "comment" : "Label at the left of the line that shows the value from the version being viewed, in the History panel; the line below shows the current value. Narrow column, about 104 points. Sentence case."
    },
    "Title" : {
      "comment" : "Label and placeholder of the text field that names a custom-fields item in the credential editor. Also the name of a person’s title, such as Dr, in a name item’s fields. Noun; two meanings, one word, sentence case."
    },
    "Too many credentials were already merged into one of these. Keep a different credential instead." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the merge sheet when one of the chosen credentials already absorbed too many earlier merges. The second sentence suggests keeping a different credential as the one that stays."
    },
    "Toolbar controls, buttons and the highlight of the selected tab." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Surface row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance: which parts of the interface use this color."
    },
    "Transfer" : {
      "comment" : "Title (with a warning icon) of the section above the Vault and Settings tabs when an import or export ended with a problem; the success title is “Transfer finished”. A noun, Sentence case."
    },
    "Transfer finished" : {
      "comment" : "Title (with a check mark icon) of the section above the Vault and Settings tabs after an import or export ended successfully. When it did not, the title is “Transfer”. Sentence case."
    },
    "Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. Label of the second segment of the Active and Trash switch above the credentials list, and also the title of the Trash section it opens, which holds removed credentials until they are deleted permanently. Keep it short in the segment."
    },
    "Trash is empty" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the empty state shown in the Trash section when no removed items are left. The caption below it reads “Credentials you remove can be restored from here.” Sentence case, a statement."
    },
    "Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Fallback message of error alerts such as “Couldn’t clear browsing data”, “Couldn’t update website data” and “Couldn’t clear history”, used only when the system gave no error text. Imperative sentence."
    },
    "Turn Off and Delete" : {
      "comment" : "Destructive button of the “Turn off Input History?” alert: stops recording and deletes all kept entries. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Turn off Input History?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert shown when the person flips off the Input History switch. Its button deletes everything kept. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Turn On" : {
      "comment" : "Confirm button of the “Turn on Input History?” alert; it starts recording what is typed on websites. Title Case, a verb phrase. The cancel button is separate."
    },
    "Turn on Input History?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert shown when the person flips on the Input History switch; its message explains what is recorded. Buttons are “Turn On” and “Cancel”. Sentence case, a question; Input History is the feature’s name."
    },
    "Turn on Remember what I type to start." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under “Nothing recorded yet” in Input History when recording is off. “Remember what I type” is the exact title of the switch above, so translate it the same way. Sentence."
    },
    "Turns the colors derived from the primary color around the color wheel." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Hue row in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Turns is a verb: the hue slider rotates the colors derived from the Primary color around the color wheel."
    },
    "Type of %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the pop-up menu that sets the type of a custom field (Text, Hidden, Date, Number, Email) in the credential editor. %@ is the field’s name as the user typed it and is not translated. Sentence case."
    },
    "Type the vault’s name to confirm" : {
      "comment" : "Label above the name text field in the Delete Vault sheet; the user must type the vault’s name before Delete Vault… turns on. Also the VoiceOver label of that field. Sentence case, an instruction."
    },
    "Undid Add Credential." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is adding a new credential. Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Add Credential” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Delete." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is deleting Trash entries permanently (they are hidden at once and removed for good when the Trash is left). Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Delete” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Edit." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is saving changes to a credential. Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Edit” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Merge." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is merging duplicate credentials into one. Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Merge” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Move to Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is moving credentials to the vault’s Trash. Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Move to Trash” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Not the Same." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after Undo of Not the Same."
    },
    "Undid Restore." : {
      "comment" : "Notice shown briefly above the credential list after Undo took the action back; the action is restoring an item from the Trash. Past tense of Undo, full sentence with a final period; the action name matches the one in the “Undo Restore” menu title."
    },
    "Undid Suggest Again." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after Undo of Suggest Again."
    },
    "Undo Add Credential" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is adding a new credential. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Delete" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is deleting Trash entries permanently (they are hidden at once and removed for good when the Trash is left). Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Edit" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is saving changes to a credential. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Merge" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is merging duplicate credentials into one. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Move to Trash" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is moving credentials to the vault’s Trash. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Not the Same" : {
      "comment" : "Edit menu: take back Not the Same on a merge suggestion."
    },
    "Undo Restore" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Edit menu’s Undo item while the keyboard is in the credential list or Trash of Settings › Credentials; it replaces the plain “Undo”. Title Case. Here the action is restoring an item from the Trash. Verb phrase."
    },
    "Undo Suggest Again" : {
      "comment" : "Edit menu: take back Suggest Again on a dismissed merge suggestion."
    },
    "Undone: %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the “Remembered …” line under an assistant answer after the notes were taken back. %@ is the list of notes, one “subject: value” per line."
    },
    "Unload Tabs" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the context menu of a split in the sidebar (two pages shown together): frees both pages’ memory while keeping their rows, to reload when selected. Title Case, a verb phrase. Singular twin: “Unload Tab”."
    },
    "Unloaded" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of a favorite tile in the sidebar: its page is not loaded and will reload when selected. Counterpart “Loaded”. Spoken after the tab’s title; not shown on screen."
    },
    "Unloaded tabs stay monochrome." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Tab icons row in the Layout card in Settings › Appearance. Unloaded tabs are asleep, with their web content released; their icons are always drawn in one color."
    },
    "Unloaded. It reloads when selected." : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip and VoiceOver label of the small down-arrow badge on a tab whose page is unloaded. “It” is the tab’s page. Two short sentences."
    },
    "Unlock and Choose…" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the first passkey alert when the vault is locked: it unlocks Credential Manager and then lets the user choose an account. Title Case, a verb phrase; the ellipsis says another step follows, keep it."
    },
    "Unlock Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Main button on the locked Autofill page when the profile has a single vault: unlocks it. Title Case, a command. With several vaults the button names the vault instead."
    },
    "Unlock Credentials…" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the autofill dropdown under a sign-in, card or address field when the credential vault is locked; choosing it starts unlocking the vault. Verb phrase. Title Case, ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Unlock one of your vaults first. A new vault is created with the approval of a vault that is already open." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when creating an additional vault while every vault is locked: a new vault needs approval from one that is open. Full sentences."
    },
    "Unlock passkey %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Unlock passkeys section. %lld is the passkey’s position in the list, counting from 1 (its own name is not shown). Sentence case."
    },
    "Unlock passkey of “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Option in the pop-up menu below Use existing passkey. %@ is the label of the vault that uses that passkey: its name, or “Vault 2” while it is locked. Do not translate the name; keep the curly quotes."
    },
    "Unlock passkeys" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the section on the Settings tab that lists the passkeys that unlock the selected vault. “Unlock” describes the passkeys’ purpose, it is not a command. Plural noun phrase, Sentence case."
    },
    "Unlock the profile “%@” to review the credentials another app is sending to WSurf. Dismiss declines them; to import them later, send them again from the other app." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph on the locked card when another app has sent credentials to WSurf and they wait for review. %@ is the profile’s name (user-chosen; do not translate). “Dismiss” refers to the Dismiss Incoming Credentials button below, so use the same wording in both."
    },
    "Unlock the vault to import or export credentials. Nothing is read or saved while it is locked." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote of the Import & Export section while the vault is locked and its buttons are off. Imperative first sentence, then a reassurance that nothing is read or saved."
    },
    "Unlock this vault to delete it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Delete vault row, shown while the vault is locked, so deleting is unavailable. Imperative, Sentence case."
    },
    "Unlock with a passkey to view and edit your credentials." : {
      "comment" : "Caption on the locked card under “Credentials are locked” in the normal case. Imperative; the Unlock button is on the same card."
    },
    "Unlock “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Main button on the locked Autofill page when the profile has several vaults. %@ is the vault’s numbered name, such as “Vault 2”; names are hidden while a vault is locked. Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Unnamed account" : {
      "comment" : "Name shown for an account in the passkey account chooser when the account has neither a display name nor a username. Sentence case."
    },
    "Until %@ · %@" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the version menu of the History panel naming an earlier version. First %@ is the date and time that version was replaced (formatted by the system); second %@ is a comma-separated list of what changed, such as Password or Notes. Keep the “ · ” separator."
    },
    "Until I delete" : {
      "comment" : "Last choice in the “Keep entries for” menu of Input History: entries never expire and stay until the person deletes them. Sentence case. Its Title Case twin is the button “Keep Until I Delete”."
    },
    "Untitled item" : {
      "comment" : "Stands in for an item’s title at the start of a line in the import review sheet when the other app sent an item with no title, followed by a colon and the reason, as in “Untitled item: …”. A noun phrase, Sentence case."
    },
    "Updated" : {
      "comment" : "One word in the caption of each imported credential in the Transfer finished list, saying what the import did with it: Added, Updated, Already saved or Skipped. Joined with the kind and website by “ · ”. Past participle."
    },
    "Updated %@" : {
      "comment" : "Date caption of a saved credential showing when it last changed, in the list and the editor; it follows “Created …”, “Moved to WSurf …” or “Imported …”, separated by a middle dot. %@ is a formatted date, with the time in the editor."
    },
    "Upgrade and Unlock" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the Upgrade This Vault? dialog: upgrades the vault to the new format and then unlocks it. Title Case, two verbs joined by “and”."
    },
    "Upgrade and Unlock…" : {
      "comment" : "Main button on the locked Autofill page in Settings, shown for a vault saved by an older WSurf. It opens the “Upgrade This Vault?” confirmation, hence the ellipsis. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Upgrade This Vault?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation dialog shown when the user unlocks a vault that an older WSurf saved; its message explains the new format. Title Case, a question."
    },
    "URL text" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the color of the web address text in the toolbar. Sentence case."
    },
    "URL text opacity" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the opacity slider beside the URL text color in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance. Not shown visually."
    },
    "Use a name of 1 to %lld characters." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when a vault’s name is empty or too long. %lld is the maximum number of characters."
    },
    "Use a Passkey…" : {
      "comment" : "Row at the bottom of the autofill dropdown under a sign-in field that supports passkeys; choosing it lets the user sign in with a passkey instead of a password. Verb phrase. Title Case, ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Use All Incoming" : {
      "comment" : "Item in the ⋯ menu of the “Changed in the other app” group in the import review sheet: replaces every saved version with the other app’s version (the incoming one). Title Case, a command."
    },
    "Use at most %lld characters." : {
      "comment" : "Hint under a name field when the name is too long. %lld is the maximum number of characters. Used for a theme’s name in the theme naming sheet, and for a vault’s name in Credential settings (when naming or renaming a credential vault)."
    },
    "Use existing passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the second choice in the Create Credential Vault sheet: protect the new vault with a passkey that another vault of the profile already uses. Shown only when such a passkey exists. Sentence case."
    },
    "Use Incoming" : {
      "comment" : "Action for one item on the import review sheet (menu item or segment), and the row menu’s label once chosen: replaces the saved version with the other app’s version, the incoming one. Title Case, a command; the opposite of “Keep Saved”."
    },
    "Use light or dark, or match your Mac." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Appearance” entry in Settings › Appearance: light, dark, or follow the Mac’s system setting. Imperative."
    },
    "Use Passkey" : {
      "comment" : "Default button of the sheet titled “Sign in to %@ with a passkey?”, which appears when a website asks to sign in with a saved passkey. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "Use the current website’s color in the toolbar and sidebar. Off while a theme’s colors or brightness are changed." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Website tint switch in Settings › Appearance › Theme: the toolbar and sidebar take the color of the page being viewed. The last sentence says the tint is switched off while theme colors or brightness are being edited. Sentence case."
    },
    "Use This" : {
      "comment" : "Small button at the right of a field’s title row in the History panel: copies the earlier version’s value into the editor as a draft; nothing is saved until Save. Title Case, very tight."
    },
    "Use this version’s %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the “Use This” button. %@ is the field’s title: Name, Login, Websites, Verification code, Notes, Files or Cards and other items. Those titles start with a capital; lowercase it if your language needs to."
    },
    "username" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase noun, never shown alone: inserted into “Copy this version’s %@” and “Copy the current %@”, the tooltips and VoiceOver labels of copy buttons in the History panel. Here it is the login’s username."
    },
    "Username changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the username was changed in WSurf after an earlier import, and this import keeps the change. A date can follow after “ · ”. A value is never shown."
    },
    "Username Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies a username (or a passkey’s user name) to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Username hidden" : {
      "comment" : "Fragment in a credential’s detail line (list rows, merge sheet, import review), joined by “ · ”. It stands in for a username that is stored but masked until revealed. A state, sentence case; not the Hide username command."
    },
    "Valid from" : {
      "comment" : "Row label, shown beside the value, of a field of an item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials. Sentence case. Start date of validity, on Payment card and API key items. Short."
    },
    "Vault" : {
      "comment" : "A vault is the encrypted store of logins, passkeys and other items. A noun: the Vault tab beside Settings on the Autofill page, the vault picker’s row title and VoiceOver label, and the Settings search result for that page."
    },
    "Vault %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Default name of a vault when the user typed none, such as “Vault 1”. %lld is the vault’s number. Also the small grey line under a custom name in the Delete Vault sheet. A noun plus a number."
    },
    "Vault %lld (locked)" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a vault in the Vault pop-up menus of Settings › Credentials, the page title, the “Which vault?” prompt and the Pick Credential… sheet (when there is more than one vault). Shown for a locked vault, whose own name stays hidden until it unlocks, so it is told by its number. %lld is the vault’s number. Keep “(locked)” in parentheses."
    },
    "Vault %lld was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Vaults section after a vault was deleted, next to a Dismiss button. %lld is the vault’s number (as in “Vault 2”); its name is deliberately not shown. A statement, Sentence case."
    },
    "Vault check" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a warning section at the top of Settings › Autofill, shown when a temporary file left by WSurf’s check of a vault could not be removed. The row below lists the file’s path. Sentence case, a noun phrase."
    },
    "Vault name" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the text field where the vault’s name is typed in the Delete Vault sheet. Also the VoiceOver label of the vault name field in the Name row and in the Create Credential Vault sheet. A noun phrase."
    },
    "Vaults" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the section on the Settings tab of Settings › Autofill that lists the profile’s vaults and their options: name, lock time, default vault, delete. A vault is an encrypted store of credentials. Plural noun, Sentence case."
    },
    "Verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Section header in the credential editor over the one-time code settings; also a word in a credential row’s detail line (joined by “ · ”), a label next to a shown code, and a part name in the merge and import lists. Noun, sentence case, not a command."
    },
    "verification code" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase fragment in an account’s line in the passkey account chooser, saying the account also holds a one-time verification code. Joined with other fragments such as “password” and “notes” by a middle dot, so keep it short and lowercase. A noun."
    },
    "Verification code changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the verification code was changed in WSurf after an earlier import, and the change is kept. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Verification Code Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies the current verification code (one-time code) of a credential to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Verification code for %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the small native field for a code from Messages or Mail. %@ is the website the code is for, as the address bar draws it. Sentence case."
    },
    "verification code name" : {
      "comment" : "Lowercase noun phrase, never shown alone: inserted into “Copy this version’s %@” and “Copy the current %@” for the copy button of a verification code’s name (its issuer and account), not its secret setup key."
    },
    "Verification code setup" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox label inside an expanded credential row of the Export Credentials sheet: includes the credential’s verification code setup (what another app needs to produce the same codes) in the export. A noun phrase, sentence case."
    },
    "Verification codes" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a count row in the Delete Vault sheet: how many sign-in verification codes the vault holds. Also a filter chip above the credential list and a row in the Statistics section. Sentence case."
    },
    "Verifying your credentials…" : {
      "comment" : "Heading with a spinner on the locked Credentials card while WSurf checks the vault before opening it. The caption below reads “WSurf is checking the vault before opening it. This can take a moment.” Ends with an ellipsis."
    },
    "Version" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label, not visible, of the pop-up menu in the History panel that chooses which earlier version of the credential is shown. A noun."
    },
    "View History" : {
      "comment" : "Button at the bottom left of the credential editor sheet that opens the History panel (earlier versions of this credential) beside the form. Alternates with “Hide History”; disabled for a new credential. Title Case, a verb phrase."
    },
    "WebKit" : {
      "comment" : "Name of one of the two browser engines a website can open in, as listed in a website’s engine choice (site controls popover and Website Settings) and inserted into sentences. WebKit is Apple’s engine and is never translated."
    },
    "Webpages can carry hidden instructions aimed at connected apps. Allow this only if it’s what you asked for." : {
      "comment" : "Closing warning paragraph of the dialog that asks whether an external connection (a connected app) may answer a page’s prompt. Full sentences."
    },
    "Website added from autofill" : {
      "comment" : "Small grey line under the version menu in the History panel of the credential editor, for an earlier version replaced when the user added the page’s website to this credential with the Add Website button of an autofill offer. Sentence case."
    },
    "Website Copied" : {
      "comment" : "Brief notice above the Credentials list in Settings, shown after the user copies a website address of a credential or passkey to the clipboard. Title Case, short."
    },
    "Website preferences could not be applied." : {
      "comment" : "Title of a warning alert shown when the browser’s website settings could not be applied to an open page that runs in the Chromium engine. The alert’s message is the system’s error text. Chromium is a name and is not translated."
    },
    "Website: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the passkey alerts naming the website that made the request. %@ is its address as verified by WSurf, such as https://example.com, and is never translated. Also used in the body of the longer passkey sheet."
    },
    "Websites (one HTTPS address per line)" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the multi-line text field in the credential editor where the credential’s websites are typed, one per line. HTTPS is the secure web protocol and stays as is. Sentence case."
    },
    "Websites or name changed" : {
      "comment" : "Line in the “Changed in WSurf (kept)” list of the import review sheet: the credential’s websites or name were changed in WSurf after an earlier import. A date can follow after “ · ”."
    },
    "Whether the assistant may close a tab without asking. Pinned tabs are never closed." : {
      "comment" : "Settings search description for the “Closing tabs” entry in Settings › Assistant. Pinned tabs are tabs fixed in the sidebar. A fragment, then a sentence."
    },
    "Which vault?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert that asks which of the profile’s credential vaults to use for a login or passkey. Its buttons are the vault names and Cancel. Sentence case, a question."
    },
    "Who it is shared with isn’t imported." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the import review sheet (Settings › Credentials), shown after the item’s title and a colon, under the item’s row or in the “Not imported” list: the sharing information of an item (who it is shared with) is not imported. “It” is the item named before the colon. Full sentence."
    },
    "Wi-Fi network" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a kind of item in Settings › Credentials: the heading of the item’s box in the credential editor, an entry in the Add Item menu and a word in the export notice. Noun, sentence case. A saved Wi-Fi network with its password; Wi-Fi stays as is."
    },
    "Wi-Fi security" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. A Wi-Fi security type, such as WPA2."
    },
    "Will be imported anyway." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of an import review row from the Skipped group that the user chose to import although it is left out by default."
    },
    "Window background" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Colors card in Settings › Appearance, and the VoiceOver label of its color picker: the theme’s base background color for the window. Sentence case; a noun phrase."
    },
    "Window layout" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Window layout entry in Settings search: the Layout options in the Window section of Settings › Appearance (page edge, corner rounding and page spacing). A noun phrase."
    },
    "Without a website" : {
      "comment" : "Row title in the Statistics section of Settings › Autofill; the number on the right is how many saved credentials have no website attached. Sentence case, a short noun phrase."
    },
    "Won’t be imported." : {
      "comment" : "Status line of a skipped import review row, and the line in a part’s details saying that this part is not saved. A short statement of fact."
    },
    "WSurf cannot confirm whether the credentials left. Check the other app before exporting again. WSurf did not retry and recorded nothing about this export." : {
      "comment" : "Message when an export to another app had started and then failed or was cancelled, so it is unknown whether any data left WSurf. “Recorded nothing” means WSurf kept no record that an export happened. Full sentences."
    },
    "WSurf can’t tell whether a credential vault exists, so it won’t offer to create one. Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Caption on the locked card when the check for a vault failed, so no Create option is offered. “Nothing was changed” means no vault data was touched."
    },
    "WSurf could not confirm the result of this import. It may have been saved. Check Credentials before choosing Review again. The old list was not changed." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when importing the old list (the passwords saved before Credential Manager) ended with an unknown result. “Credentials” is the Credentials page of Settings. “Review” is the button “Review…” on the old-passwords card; match its translation."
    },
    "WSurf could not confirm the result of this import. It may have been saved. Check Credentials before choosing the file again." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when importing a password CSV file that the user chose ended with an unknown result. “Credentials” is the Credentials page of Settings; a Show Credentials button accompanies this message."
    },
    "WSurf could not confirm the result of this import. It may have been saved. Check Credentials before exporting again." : {
      "comment" : "Message in Settings › Credentials when saving an import from another app had started and its result is unknown (for example WSurf locked or the user cancelled). “Credentials” is the Credentials page of Settings, where a Show Credentials button accompanies this message. Exporting again is done in the other app."
    },
    "WSurf could not validate this data" : {
      "comment" : "Reason fragment dropped into the “The transfer could not be read…” message as its third %@, right after a colon and before a full stop, so it has no final period. Says the received data failed WSurf’s checks."
    },
    "WSurf decrypts a copy for the app you choose. That app can keep its own copy, for example in its recent documents. WSurf removes its copy when the vault locks or WSurf quits." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Open in Another App?” dialog. WSurf is the app name; the vault is the encrypted store holding the credentials. The copy is the temporary decrypted file handed to the other app. Two sentences."
    },
    "WSurf handed the selected credentials to the system. WSurf cannot tell whether the other app received or imported them." : {
      "comment" : "Message after the user exports selected credentials from WSurf to another app (normally Apple’s Passwords). “The system” is macOS, which received the hand-off; WSurf cannot see whether the other app took the data. Full sentences."
    },
    "WSurf is checking for your credential vault." : {
      "comment" : "Caption on the locked card while WSurf has not yet found out whether a vault exists. Sentence."
    },
    "WSurf is checking the vault before opening it. This can take a moment." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the “Verifying your credentials…” heading on the locked Credentials card while the vault is being checked before it opens. Sentence."
    },
    "WSurf Passwords.csv" : {
      "comment" : "Suggested file name in the save panel when exporting passwords to a CSV file. Keep WSurf and the .csv extension; only the word Passwords may be translated."
    },
    "WSurf saved %lld password rows to a CSV file. The file is not encrypted and anyone who can open it can read the passwords. Delete it as soon as you have imported it. WSurf does not delete it for you." : {
      "comment" : "Warning shown after the user exports credentials as a CSV file. %lld is the number of password rows written. A CSV file is plain, unencrypted text, which is why it must be deleted after use. Full sentences."
    },
    "WSurf saves passwords in an encrypted vault that you unlock with a passkey. There is no recovery: if you lose every passkey that unlocks the vault, its passwords can’t be recovered. This password isn’t saved now. After you set up the vault, sign in again to save it." : {
      "comment" : "Body text of the toolbar popover that offers to save a password when no vault exists yet (title “Save passwords in Credential Manager?”). Nothing is saved now. A vault is an encrypted store unlocked by a passkey. WSurf is not translated."
    },
    "WSurf then erases the cards and addresses saved on this Mac, and the list it suggested them from. Autofill fills them from the vault. This can’t be undone." : {
      "comment" : "Last part of the message in the dialog confirming that the old copies of cards and addresses are erased. The “list it suggested them from” is the older list that autofill suggestions were drawn from. The sentence “This can’t be undone” is the warning."
    },
    "WSurf will remember text you type on websites in every window of this profile, including passwords. It stays encrypted on this Mac. It is never synced, and never shown to assistants or connected apps. Nothing is recorded in a tab while the assistant or a connected app works in it. Entries are deleted after the time you choose. Anyone who knows your Mac password can open it. Card numbers, security codes and one-time codes are not recorded." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Turn on Input History?” alert. A consent text: lists what is recorded, that it stays encrypted on this Mac, is never synced or shown to the assistant or connected apps, and the password risk. WSurf stays untranslated."
    },
    "WSurf won’t create, reset or overwrite anything while this is unresolved. These files are involved:" : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the “Credentials can’t be opened” card, followed by a list of file paths. It says nothing is created, reset or overwritten while the problem remains. Sentences."
    },
    "Yes or no" : {
      "comment" : "Entry in the type menu on each row of a Custom fields item in the credential editor of Settings › Credentials; it sets what kind of value the field holds. Sentence case. A value that is either yes or no."
    },
    "You can remove this vault’s unlock passkey from Passwords if nothing else uses it." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the “Vault %lld was deleted.” row, shown when the deleted vault’s unlock passkey is left over in the passkey provider. Passwords is Apple’s app."
    },
    "You can’t undo this." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the dialog that asks whether to delete a saved theme in Settings › Appearance. Sentence case."
    },
    "You have saved %lld themes, the most WSurf keeps. Delete one to save another." : {
      "comment" : "Caption of the Customize row in Settings › Appearance › Theme, replacing the normal caption when the limit of saved themes is reached (the button is then off). %lld is that limit, also the number of themes saved. Sentence case."
    },
    "You stopped this connection" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the Agent Activity log of an external app, recorded when the person pressed Stop on that connection. Past tense, “you” is the user."
    },
    "You will be asked to verify with your Mac next." : {
      "comment" : "Last line of the passkey sheet when WSurf will ask for user verification afterwards, such as Touch ID or the Mac password. Full sentence."
    },
    "You will choose an account next." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the first passkey alert when the vault is already unlocked; the button below it is “Choose…”. Full sentence."
    },
    "Your changes to this credential aren’t saved." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Discard Changes?” dialog in the credential editor. Sentence."
    },
    "Your credential files changed while WSurf was reading them. Check again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the vault files on disk changed while WSurf was reading them. The user is asked to check (read them) again."
    },
    "Your credentials changed elsewhere. Reload and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error on the Credentials page in Settings when the vault was changed elsewhere after the page loaded. “Reload” is an instruction to the user to read the vault again."
    },
    "your credentials changed while it was open" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period; it must read correctly after “because”. “It” means the import review."
    },
    "your credentials were locked" : {
      "comment" : "Reason clause inserted as %@ into “The import ended because %@, and nothing was saved. …”. Lowercase fragment, no period; the credential vault locked during the import."
    },
    "Your Mac will not ask for further verification." : {
      "comment" : "Last line of the passkey sheet when no further user verification will be requested. Full sentence."
    },
    "You’ll confirm with one of the %lld remaining unlock passkeys. The passkey itself stays in your passkey provider. Removing it does not change the vault’s encryption key. Someone with that passkey and an older vault file can still decrypt later copies of this vault they obtain." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove Unlock Passkey?” confirmation dialog on the Credentials page. %lld is how many unlock passkeys remain after this one is removed; one of them is used to confirm. It explains that the passkey stays in the passkey provider and that removing it does not change the vault’s encryption key."
    },
    "“%@” couldn’t be read. Choose a file, not a folder, and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when the item chosen with Add File… is not a regular file or couldn’t be read. %@ is the name of the chosen item (the curly quotes surround it; do not translate it). Full sentences."
    },
    "“%@” holds %lld credentials and %lld in Trash" : {
      "comment" : "One item of the list in the confirmation shown when deleting a profile, for an unlocked credential vault. %@ is the vault’s name, the first %lld is how many credentials it holds and the second is how many items are in its Trash. Joined with semicolons into a longer sentence."
    },
    "“%@” is larger than %@. Each file in the vault can be up to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Error text at the bottom of the credential editor in Settings › Credentials, when a file chosen with Add File… is too big. First %@ is the file’s name (the curly quotes surround it; do not translate it). The second and third %@ are the same size limit with a unit, such as “50 MB”. Full sentences."
    },
    "“%@” is locked, so what it holds is unknown and may contain recoverable items" : {
      "comment" : "One item of the list in the confirmation shown when deleting a profile, for a credential vault that is locked and cannot be counted. %@ is the vault’s name; keep the curly quotes. It is joined to other items with semicolons and ends up inside a longer sentence, so it has no final period."
    },
    "“%@” is removed from this entry when you save. You can bring it back from History." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Remove File?” dialog in the credential editor. %@ is the file’s name and is not translated; the curly quotes surround it. History is the panel of earlier versions of the credential. Sentence."
    },
    "“%@” moves to Trash with its history, and its password and code stay in the History of “%@”. It can’t be restored while “%@” is in the vault." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the “Merge Credentials?” dialog when one credential is merged away. First %@ is the title of the credential that moves to Trash; second and third %@ are the title of the primary credential. Titles are not translated. Trash is the vault’s Trash."
    },
    "• Allow Development: also inspect page structure and styles, read console and network metadata, and change the viewport. These can disclose additional private site data, including text a page writes to its console." : {
      "comment" : "One bullet in the message of the dialog that asks whether a connected app may access a tab; it explains the Allow Development button and follows the bullets for Read Only and Allow Control. Keep the leading bullet, and spell Allow Development as the button’s translation does. Shown only when development access can be granted."
    }
  },
  "version" : "1.0"
}